{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794550526916,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799ae9ffehgaY2UX9uAVWD2","part":{"partID":"prt_1d38bf270001VON5utlfTmJ3yb","sessionID":"ses_e2c799ae9ffehgaY2UX9uAVWD2","messageID":"msg_1d38be67d001pQe6S2Meoz258U","type":"tool","id":"call_01_OAwfkis9slOkJSOUjX1Z8645","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml"},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml, lines 1-73\n1: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: # DOCTOR: SETUP UMBRELLA (READ-ONLY DIAGNOSTIC)\n3: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: role: Diagnostic Operator giving a first-run overview of every doctor command and running the existing read-only setup checks once\n5: purpose: List every doctor target with what it checks, run seven read-only legs, and name the runnable doctor command that repairs each failing leg\n6: action: Print the doctor target list -> run the seven read-only legs once -> render the per-leg verdict and repair lines through the presentation contract\n7: skill_owner: \".skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/\"\n8: \n9: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n10: # OPERATING MODE\n11: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n12: operating_mode:\n13:   workflow: single-step\n14:   compliance: MANDATORY\n15:   execution: read_only\n16:   approvals: none\n17:   tracking: single_run\n18:   validation: read_only_assertion\n19: \n20: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n21: # MUTATION BOUNDARIES (READ-ONLY)\n22: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n23: mutation_boundaries:\n24:   read_only: true\n25:   allowed_targets: []\n26:   forbidden_targets:\n27:     - \"**/*\"\n28:   invariant: \"Every leg runs in its check-only form. This route MUST NOT regenerate the trigger index, sync a runtime mirror, start the advisor daemon, install hooks or provision the tree. A failing leg prints the doctor command that repairs it; repair is an explicit operator action, never a side effect of this diagnostic.\"\n29: \n30: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n31: # UPSTREAM ASSETS\n32: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n33: upstream_assets:\n34:   route_manifest: \".skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml\"\n35:   sk_code_battery: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/sk-code-setup-check.cjs\"\n36:   sk_git_battery: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-setup-check.cjs\"\n37:   trigger_index_check: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/generate-trigger-index.mjs\"\n38:   runtime_mirror_check: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs\"\n39:   hop_history: \".skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/bin/session-relaunch.cjs\"\n40:   hook_wiring_check: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\"\n41:   codex_approval_check: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs\"\n42: \n43: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n44: # INPUTS\n45: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n46: inputs:\n47:   target: \"The command takes no positional target and no flag. /doctor:setup alone runs it; anything else fails before this YAML loads.\"\n48: \n49: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n50: # EXECUTION\n51: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n52: execution:\n53:   steps:\n54:     - \"Read .skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml and print the doctor target list through the presentation contract. The presentation table owns the rows and their wording. It shows /doctor:ci as one row for its report target. That row names the scaffold and toggle routes. Each row carries the one-line description of what it checks.\"\n55:     - \"Leg sk-code: run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/sk-code-setup-check.cjs. Exit 0 passes. Any other exit fails, with repair /doctor:sk-code setup.\"\n56:     - \"Leg sk-git: run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-setup-check.cjs --tool=<name>, where <name> is the AI tool executing this command: claude, codex, devin, cursor, opencode, pi or dsh. On any other runtime, run it without --tool, because the battery accepts no other name. Exit 0 passes. Exit 3 is DEGRADED, not a failure: no check failed, but one is UNKNOWN or DEGRADED, so the row names /doctor:git setup to show which. Exit 2 is a usage error or a crash and is ERROR. Any other exit fails, with repair /doctor:git setup.\"\n57:     - \"Leg trigger-index: run node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/generate-trigger-index.mjs --check --json. Exit 0 passes. Exit 1 (stale documents) or 2 and higher (unreadable index) fails, with repair /doctor:speckit.\"\n58:     - \"Leg runtime-mirrors: run node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check. Exit 0 passes. Any other exit fails, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors.\"\n59:     - \"Leg advisor: run node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --format json --timeout-ms 500 --warm-only. Exit 0 with data.freshness set to live is PASS. Exit 0 with any other freshness is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor rebuild. Exit 75 with a staleDistWarning field in stderr JSON is FAIL, with repair npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build. Exit 75 without that field is SKIP because the daemon is not running. Any other exit is FAIL, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor rebuild. When data.hookHealth is present, show hook p95 <rollingP95Ms> ms over <invocations> prompts and fail-open <rollingFailOpenRate as a percent> under the leg. It never changes the leg's status.\"\n60:     - \"Leg embedder: run node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --include-semantic-health true --format json --timeout-ms 1500 --warm-only. Exit 75 is SKIP, as for the advisor leg, because the daemon is not running. Exit 0 with data.semanticLaneHealth.laneEnabled true and data.semanticLaneHealth.commandVectorCoverage.embedded above 0 is PASS. Any other result is DEGRADED, never FAIL, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor embedder.\"\n61:     - \"Leg delivery: run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\" and node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\", and show each line they print under the leg. Both exit 0 is PASS. A hook-missing line is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors in a Skilled checkout or /doctor:symlink check in a linked project. WARN codex-hooks-unapproved is DEGRADED, with the repair line the check printed. WARN codex-advisor-hook-absent is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors. Exit 2 from either check is ERROR. This leg is never FAIL, because a hook that is not wired or not approved stops the brief, not the install.\"\n62:     - \"Last session hop (informational, not a leg): run node .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/bin/session-relaunch.cjs history --last 1 and show its first output line under the result as the last session hop, plus its open notes line when it prints one. Its exit and output never change the status.\"\n63:     - \"Claude context window (informational, not a leg): run node .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/bin/session-relaunch.cjs window and show its line. Its exit and output never change the status.\"\n64:     - \"Orphan processes (informational, not a leg): run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/orphan-process-check.cjs --summary and show its line. Its exit and output never change the status.\"\n65:     - \"Run every leg even when an earlier one fails, then render the per-leg table, the DOCTOR DIAGNOSTIC RESULT summary and the troubleshooting table through .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt.\"\n66: \n67: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n68: # OUTPUT\n69: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n70: output: |\n71:   STATUS=OK when no leg fails: each leg passes, is skipped or is degraded. List each degraded leg with the command that shows why.\n72:   STATUS=FAIL when any leg fails; list each failing leg with its repair command.\n73:   STATUS=ERROR when a leg crashes or its output cannot be read; report the message and the accepted invocation (/doctor:setup).","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml, lines 1-73\n1: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: # DOCTOR: SETUP UMBRELLA (READ-ONLY DIAGNOSTIC)\n3: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: role: Diagnostic Operator giving a first-run overview of every doctor command and running the existing read-only setup checks once\n5: purpose: List every doctor target with what it checks, run seven read-only legs, and name the runnable doctor command that repairs each failing leg\n6: action: Print the doctor target list -> run the seven read-only legs once -> render the per-leg verdict and repair lines through the presentation contract\n7: skill_owner: \".skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/\"\n8: \n9: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n10: # OPERATING MODE\n11: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n12: operating_mode:\n13:   workflow: single-step\n14:   compliance: MANDATORY\n15:   execution: read_only\n16:   approvals: none\n17:   tracking: single_run\n18:   validation: read_only_assertion\n19: \n20: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n21: # MUTATION BOUNDARIES (READ-ONLY)\n22: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n23: mutation_boundaries:\n24:   read_only: true\n25:   allowed_targets: []\n26:   forbidden_targets:\n27:     - \"**/*\"\n28:   invariant: \"Every leg runs in its check-only form. This route MUST NOT regenerate the trigger index, sync a runtime mirror, start the advisor daemon, install hooks or provision the tree. A failing leg prints the doctor command that repairs it; repair is an explicit operator action, never a side effect of this diagnostic.\"\n29: \n30: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n31: # UPSTREAM ASSETS\n32: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n33: upstream_assets:\n34:   route_manifest: \".skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml\"\n35:   sk_code_battery: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/sk-code-setup-check.cjs\"\n36:   sk_git_battery: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-setup-check.cjs\"\n37:   trigger_index_check: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/generate-trigger-index.mjs\"\n38:   runtime_mirror_check: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs\"\n39:   hop_history: \".skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/bin/session-relaunch.cjs\"\n40:   hook_wiring_check: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\"\n41:   codex_approval_check: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs\"\n42: \n43: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n44: # INPUTS\n45: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n46: inputs:\n47:   target: \"The command takes no positional target and no flag. /doctor:setup alone runs it; anything else fails before this YAML loads.\"\n48: \n49: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n50: # EXECUTION\n51: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n52: execution:\n53:   steps:\n54:     - \"Read .skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml and print the doctor target list through the presentation contract. The presentation table owns the rows and their wording. It shows /doctor:ci as one row for its report target. That row names the scaffold and toggle routes. Each row carries the one-line description of what it checks.\"\n55:     - \"Leg sk-code: run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/sk-code-setup-check.cjs. Exit 0 passes. Any other exit fails, with repair /doctor:sk-code setup.\"\n56:     - \"Leg sk-git: run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-setup-check.cjs --tool=<name>, where <name> is the AI tool executing this command: claude, codex, devin, cursor, opencode, pi or dsh. On any other runtime, run it without --tool, because the battery accepts no other name. Exit 0 passes. Exit 3 is DEGRADED, not a failure: no check failed, but one is UNKNOWN or DEGRADED, so the row names /doctor:git setup to show which. Exit 2 is a usage error or a crash and is ERROR. Any other exit fails, with repair /doctor:git setup.\"\n57:     - \"Leg trigger-index: run node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/generate-trigger-index.mjs --check --json. Exit 0 passes. Exit 1 (stale documents) or 2 and higher (unreadable index) fails, with repair /doctor:speckit.\"\n58:     - \"Leg runtime-mirrors: run node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check. Exit 0 passes. Any other exit fails, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors.\"\n59:     - \"Leg advisor: run node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --format json --timeout-ms 500 --warm-only. Exit 0 with data.freshness set to live is PASS. Exit 0 with any other freshness is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor rebuild. Exit 75 with a staleDistWarning field in stderr JSON is FAIL, with repair npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build. Exit 75 without that field is SKIP because the daemon is not running. Any other exit is FAIL, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor rebuild. When data.hookHealth is present, show hook p95 <rollingP95Ms> ms over <invocations> prompts and fail-open <rollingFailOpenRate as a percent> under the leg. It never changes the leg's status.\"\n60:     - \"Leg embedder: run node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --include-semantic-health true --format json --timeout-ms 1500 --warm-only. Exit 75 is SKIP, as for the advisor leg, because the daemon is not running. Exit 0 with data.semanticLaneHealth.laneEnabled true and data.semanticLaneHealth.commandVectorCoverage.embedded above 0 is PASS. Any other result is DEGRADED, never FAIL, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor embedder.\"\n61:     - \"Leg delivery: run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\" and node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\", and show each line they print under the leg. Both exit 0 is PASS. A hook-missing line is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors in a Skilled checkout or /doctor:symlink check in a linked project. WARN codex-hooks-unapproved is DEGRADED, with the repair line the check printed. WARN codex-advisor-hook-absent is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors. Exit 2 from either check is ERROR. This leg is never FAIL, because a hook that is not wired or not approved stops the brief, not the install.\"\n62:     - \"Last session hop (informational, not a leg): run node .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/bin/session-relaunch.cjs history --last 1 and show its first output line under the result as the last session hop, plus its open notes line when it prints one. Its exit and output never change the status.\"\n63:     - \"Claude context window (informational, not a leg): run node .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/bin/session-relaunch.cjs window and show its line. Its exit and output never change the status.\"\n64:     - \"Orphan processes (informational, not a leg): run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/orphan-process-check.cjs --summary and show its line. Its exit and output never change the status.\"\n65:     - \"Run every leg even when an earlier one fails, then render the per-leg table, the DOCTOR DIAGNOSTIC RESULT summary and the troubleshooting table through .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt.\"\n66: \n67: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n68: # OUTPUT\n69: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n70: output: |\n71:   STATUS=OK when no leg fails: each leg passes, is skipped or is degraded. List each degraded leg with the command that shows why.\n72:   STATUS=FAIL when any leg fails; list each failing leg with its repair command.\n73:   STATUS=ERROR when a leg crashes or its output cannot be read; report the message and the accepted invocation (/doctor:setup)."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml\"}"},"time":{"start":1794550526576,"end":1794550526916}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794550526939,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799ae9ffehgaY2UX9uAVWD2","part":{"partID":"prt_1d38bf372001Anrn6c9jUFwU1W","sessionID":"ses_e2c799ae9ffehgaY2UX9uAVWD2","messageID":"msg_1d38be67d001pQe6S2Meoz258U","type":"tool","id":"call_02_iL16PQrew8BF71hN1tqW5845","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml"},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml, lines 1-173\n1: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: # DOCTOR: SKILL-ADVISOR EMBEDDER SETUP WORKFLOW (INTERACTIVE MUTATING MODE)\n3: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: role: Expert Operator setting up local meaning matching for the skill advisor in interactive mode\n5: purpose: Find what is missing for local meaning matching, show every missing step with its cost and its undo, ask once, run only the approved steps and prove the semantic lane is on\n6: action: Probe Ollama, the model and the advisor -> print the plan with a cost and an undo per missing step -> approval -> start the server and pull the model -> skill graph scan -> probe again -> final result\n7: \n8: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n9: # OPERATING MODE\n10: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n11: operating_mode:\n12:   workflow: sequential_with_single_approval\n13:   compliance: MANDATORY\n14:   execution: interactive\n15:   approvals: one_before_first_step\n16:   dry_run: print_the_plan_then_status_ok\n17:   tracking: phase_by_phase\n18:   validation: rerun_the_probe_after_the_scan\n19: \n20: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n21: # EMBEDDER SETUP INVARIANT\n22: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n23: embedder_setup_invariant: |\n24:   Meaning matching needs four things: Ollama installed, the server answering, the\n25:   nomic-embed-text:v1.5 model pulled and a skill graph scan that writes the command\n26:   vectors. This route never installs or upgrades Ollama. It prints the install\n27:   command for the operator to run, because a system package install is theirs to\n28:   make and the install guide owns its cost. It starts the server and pulls the\n29:   model only after the one approval, and only for a step the probe found missing.\n30:   The scan writes only skill-graph.sqlite, which is derived state. Nothing is\n31:   pulled, started or written before the approval, and a dry run stops after the\n32:   plan. A no stops with STATUS=CANCELLED and changes nothing.\n33: \n34: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n35: # UPSTREAM ASSETS\n36: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n37: upstream_assets:\n38:   contract: \"local command design contract\"\n39:   advisor_cli: \".skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs\"\n40:   advisor_status_command: \"node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --include-semantic-health true --format json --warm-only\"\n41:   scan_command: \"node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_scan --trusted --format json\"\n42:   cost_script: \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs\"\n43:   sqlite_graph: \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/database/skill-graph.sqlite\"\n44:   install_guide: \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md\"\n45:   install_overview: \"INSTALL-SKILLED.md\"\n46:   presentation: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt\"\n47: \n48: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n49: # INPUTS\n50: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n51: inputs:\n52:   execution_mode: \"INTERACTIVE\"\n53:   dry_run: \"--dry-run prints the plan with each missing step's cost and undo, then stops with STATUS=OK before the approval. Nothing is pulled, started or written (default false).\"\n54: \n55: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n56: # FIELD HANDLING\n57: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n58: field_handling:\n59:   defaults:\n60:     dry_run: false\n61:   validation:\n62:     execution_mode_must_be: INTERACTIVE\n63: \n64: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n65: # MUTATION BOUNDARIES\n66: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n67: mutation_boundaries:\n68:   read_only: false\n69:   allowed_targets:\n70:     - \"the Ollama model store, one pulled copy of nomic-embed-text:v1.5 only\"\n71:     - \"a background ollama serve process, only when the probe found no server answering\"\n72:     - \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/database/skill-graph.sqlite, through skill_graph_scan only\"\n73:   forbidden_targets:\n74:     - \"the Ollama install or upgrade itself, which this route prints and never runs\"\n75:     - \".skilled/skills/*/graph-metadata.json\"\n76:     - \".skilled/skills/*/SKILL.md\"\n77:     - \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/**\"\n78:     - \"any second model pull and any model removal\"\n79:   invariant: \"Only the steps the plan printed are run, and only after the approval. skill_graph_scan is the only writer inside the repository, and it writes derived state.\"\n80: \n81: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n82: # WORKFLOW\n83: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n84: workflow:\n85:   phase_1_probe:\n86:     purpose: \"Find what is missing without changing anything\"\n87:     activities:\n88:       - \"Run `command -v ollama` and record whether it printed a path. An empty result is the missing install step, not a failure of the route.\"\n89:       - \"Resolve the server URL from `OLLAMA_BASE_URL`, defaulting to `http://127.0.0.1:11434`. Run `curl -sS --max-time 5 <url>/api/version`. A failure is the missing start step, not a failure of the route.\"\n90:       - \"When the version answers, run `curl -sS --max-time 5 <url>/api/tags` and look for `nomic-embed-text:v1.5`. A missing tag is the missing pull step.\"\n91:       - \"Run `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --include-semantic-health true --format json --warm-only`. Exit 75 means no daemon is running, so record daemon=absent and the semantic health as unread. Never start a daemon to make this probe succeed.\"\n92:       - \"Read `semanticLaneHealth.laneEnabled`, `semanticLaneHealth.activeEmbedder` and `semanticLaneHealth.commandVectorCoverage` to decide whether the scan step is still missing. A null active embedder or an embedded count of zero is the missing scan step.\"\n93:       - \"Keep every probe result as it printed. Never upgrade an unread probe to a pass.\"\n94:     outputs:\n95:       - ollama_binary: \"present|missing\"\n96:       - server: \"answering|absent\"\n97:       - model: \"present|missing\"\n98:       - daemon: \"present|absent\"\n99:       - active_embedder: \"object|null|unread\"\n100:       - command_vector_coverage: \"object|unread\"\n101: \n102:   phase_2_plan:\n103:     purpose: \"Print one line per missing step with its cost and its undo, through the presentation contract\"\n104:     activities:\n105:       - \"Read .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt for the probe dashboard, the plan table, the approval prompt, the dry-run result and the final result wording. Every visible line comes from there.\"\n106:       - \"Run `node .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs` when `/api/version` answered, and keep its JSON. Exit 2 means the server stopped answering after the probe, so take the cost from the install guide and say the live measurement was unavailable.\"\n107:       - \"Render the presentation contract's probe dashboard with the binary, the server version, the model tag and the advisor's lane state.\"\n108:       - \"For each missing step, print one plan row through the presentation contract's plan table with columns step, cost and undo. Install Ollama is printed for the operator with the install guide's cost and the package manager's own uninstall as its undo. Start `ollama serve` in the background costs `.memory.serveRssKb` resident and undoes by stopping the pid this run started. Pull `nomic-embed-text:v1.5` costs `.model.sizeBytes` on disk and undoes with `ollama rm nomic-embed-text:v1.5`. `skill_graph_scan` costs the scan's own runtime plus `.warm.medianMs` per embedded prompt and needs no undo because the database is derived state and a rerun rewrites it.\"\n109:       - \"Never print a cost the measurement or the install guide did not produce. Never offer an undo the operator cannot run.\"\n110:       - \"When the probe found no missing step, render the presentation contract's final result as already set up, ask nothing, run nothing and stop with STATUS=OK.\"\n111: \n112:   phase_3_approval:\n113:     purpose: \"Ask once against the plan on screen, and run phase 4 only after its approve\"\n114:     activities:\n115:       - \"If dry_run is true, render the presentation contract's dry-run result from the plan's own rows and stop with STATUS=OK. A dry run asks nothing, pulls nothing, starts nothing and writes nothing.\"\n116:       - \"Ask the presentation contract's approval prompt once, naming the model pull, the background server start when it is listed and the database the scan writes.\"\n117:       - \"Approve is the only answer that proceeds. Anything else is a no: render the presentation contract's cancelled result, state that nothing was pulled, started or written, and stop with STATUS=CANCELLED ACTION=cancelled.\"\n118:       - \"Never default an answer, never carry an approval from another run and never accept an approval for a plan that has changed.\"\n119: \n120:   phase_4_approved_steps:\n121:     purpose: \"Run only the steps the approved plan listed, in dependency order\"\n122:     runs_when: \"phase_3_approval approved\"\n123:     activities:\n124:       - \"When the install step is missing, print the Ollama install command the install guide prints and stop with STATUS=FAIL, naming that command as the next step. Never install or upgrade Ollama from this route.\"\n125:       - \"When the start step is missing, run `ollama serve` in the background with a readable log, record the pid this run started and poll `/api/version` until it answers or a short deadline passes. A server that never answers is STATUS=FAIL naming the start and the log path, and the pull and scan steps do not run.\"\n126:       - \"When the pull step is missing, run `ollama pull nomic-embed-text:v1.5` only once the server answers. A non-zero exit is STATUS=FAIL naming the pull, and the scan step does not run.\"\n127:       - \"Never pull a model the plan did not list, never remove a model and never restart a server this run did not start.\"\n128: \n129:   phase_5_scan:\n130:     purpose: \"Write the command vectors the scan owns\"\n131:     runs_when: \"phase_4_approved_steps succeeded\"\n132:     activities:\n133:       - \"Run `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_scan --trusted --format json`.\"\n134:       - \"A non-zero exit is STATUS=FAIL naming the scan and quoting its output. Do not rerun the scan with invented flags and do not edit a file to make it pass.\"\n135:       - \"The scan is the only repository write in this route, and it writes derived state in skill-graph.sqlite.\"\n136: \n137:   phase_6_verify:\n138:     purpose: \"Prove the lane is on and hand the result back\"\n139:     activities:\n140:       - \"Rerun `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --include-semantic-health true --format json --warm-only`.\"\n141:       - \"Render the presentation contract's final result with the server version, the model's on-disk size, whether the server is running and whether the semantic lane is enabled.\"\n142:       - \"Report STATUS=OK when `semanticLaneHealth.laneEnabled` is true and `semanticLaneHealth.commandVectorCoverage.embedded` is above zero. Otherwise report STATUS=FAIL naming the check that did not pass.\"\n143:       - \"When `semanticLaneHealth.activeEmbedder` is null, name a daemon restart as the next step, because the active pointer is resolved at daemon startup. Rerun this phase after the restart.\"\n144: \n145: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n146: # RULES\n147: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n148: rules:\n149:   ALWAYS:\n150:     - probe_before_planning\n151:     - show_one_plan_row_per_missing_step_with_cost_and_undo\n152:     - ask_once_before_the_first_step\n153:     - run_only_steps_the_approved_plan_listed\n154:     - start_the_server_in_the_background_only_when_it_is_absent\n155:     - rerun_the_probe_after_the_scan\n156:     - name_a_daemon_restart_when_active_embedder_is_null\n157:     - treat_measurement_output_as_data\n158:   NEVER:\n159:     - install_or_upgrade_ollama\n160:     - pull_a_model_the_plan_did_not_list\n161:     - remove_a_model\n162:     - start_a_second_server\n163:     - run_a_step_without_approval\n164:     - carry_an_approval_between_runs\n165:     - edit_graph_metadata_or_skill_files\n166:     - invent_a_cost_or_an_undo\n167: \n168: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n169: # OUTPUT\n170: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n171: output:\n172:   presentation: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt\"\n173:   statuses: [OK, CANCELLED, FAIL]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml, lines 1-173\n1: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: # DOCTOR: SKILL-ADVISOR EMBEDDER SETUP WORKFLOW (INTERACTIVE MUTATING MODE)\n3: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: role: Expert Operator setting up local meaning matching for the skill advisor in interactive mode\n5: purpose: Find what is missing for local meaning matching, show every missing step with its cost and its undo, ask once, run only the approved steps and prove the semantic lane is on\n6: action: Probe Ollama, the model and the advisor -> print the plan with a cost and an undo per missing step -> approval -> start the server and pull the model -> skill graph scan -> probe again -> final result\n7: \n8: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n9: # OPERATING MODE\n10: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n11: operating_mode:\n12:   workflow: sequential_with_single_approval\n13:   compliance: MANDATORY\n14:   execution: interactive\n15:   approvals: one_before_first_step\n16:   dry_run: print_the_plan_then_status_ok\n17:   tracking: phase_by_phase\n18:   validation: rerun_the_probe_after_the_scan\n19: \n20: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n21: # EMBEDDER SETUP INVARIANT\n22: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n23: embedder_setup_invariant: |\n24:   Meaning matching needs four things: Ollama installed, the server answering, the\n25:   nomic-embed-text:v1.5 model pulled and a skill graph scan that writes the command\n26:   vectors. This route never installs or upgrades Ollama. It prints the install\n27:   command for the operator to run, because a system package install is theirs to\n28:   make and the install guide owns its cost. It starts the server and pulls the\n29:   model only after the one approval, and only for a step the probe found missing.\n30:   The scan writes only skill-graph.sqlite, which is derived state. Nothing is\n31:   pulled, started or written before the approval, and a dry run stops after the\n32:   plan. A no stops with STATUS=CANCELLED and changes nothing.\n33: \n34: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n35: # UPSTREAM ASSETS\n36: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n37: upstream_assets:\n38:   contract: \"local command design contract\"\n39:   advisor_cli: \".skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs\"\n40:   advisor_status_command: \"node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --include-semantic-health true --format json --warm-only\"\n41:   scan_command: \"node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_scan --trusted --format json\"\n42:   cost_script: \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs\"\n43:   sqlite_graph: \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/database/skill-graph.sqlite\"\n44:   install_guide: \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md\"\n45:   install_overview: \"INSTALL-SKILLED.md\"\n46:   presentation: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt\"\n47: \n48: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n49: # INPUTS\n50: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n51: inputs:\n52:   execution_mode: \"INTERACTIVE\"\n53:   dry_run: \"--dry-run prints the plan with each missing step's cost and undo, then stops with STATUS=OK before the approval. Nothing is pulled, started or written (default false).\"\n54: \n55: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n56: # FIELD HANDLING\n57: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n58: field_handling:\n59:   defaults:\n60:     dry_run: false\n61:   validation:\n62:     execution_mode_must_be: INTERACTIVE\n63: \n64: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n65: # MUTATION BOUNDARIES\n66: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n67: mutation_boundaries:\n68:   read_only: false\n69:   allowed_targets:\n70:     - \"the Ollama model store, one pulled copy of nomic-embed-text:v1.5 only\"\n71:     - \"a background ollama serve process, only when the probe found no server answering\"\n72:     - \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/database/skill-graph.sqlite, through skill_graph_scan only\"\n73:   forbidden_targets:\n74:     - \"the Ollama install or upgrade itself, which this route prints and never runs\"\n75:     - \".skilled/skills/*/graph-metadata.json\"\n76:     - \".skilled/skills/*/SKILL.md\"\n77:     - \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/**\"\n78:     - \"any second model pull and any model removal\"\n79:   invariant: \"Only the steps the plan printed are run, and only after the approval. skill_graph_scan is the only writer inside the repository, and it writes derived state.\"\n80: \n81: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n82: # WORKFLOW\n83: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n84: workflow:\n85:   phase_1_probe:\n86:     purpose: \"Find what is missing without changing anything\"\n87:     activities:\n88:       - \"Run `command -v ollama` and record whether it printed a path. An empty result is the missing install step, not a failure of the route.\"\n89:       - \"Resolve the server URL from `OLLAMA_BASE_URL`, defaulting to `http://127.0.0.1:11434`. Run `curl -sS --max-time 5 <url>/api/version`. A failure is the missing start step, not a failure of the route.\"\n90:       - \"When the version answers, run `curl -sS --max-time 5 <url>/api/tags` and look for `nomic-embed-text:v1.5`. A missing tag is the missing pull step.\"\n91:       - \"Run `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --include-semantic-health true --format json --warm-only`. Exit 75 means no daemon is running, so record daemon=absent and the semantic health as unread. Never start a daemon to make this probe succeed.\"\n92:       - \"Read `semanticLaneHealth.laneEnabled`, `semanticLaneHealth.activeEmbedder` and `semanticLaneHealth.commandVectorCoverage` to decide whether the scan step is still missing. A null active embedder or an embedded count of zero is the missing scan step.\"\n93:       - \"Keep every probe result as it printed. Never upgrade an unread probe to a pass.\"\n94:     outputs:\n95:       - ollama_binary: \"present|missing\"\n96:       - server: \"answering|absent\"\n97:       - model: \"present|missing\"\n98:       - daemon: \"present|absent\"\n99:       - active_embedder: \"object|null|unread\"\n100:       - command_vector_coverage: \"object|unread\"\n101: \n102:   phase_2_plan:\n103:     purpose: \"Print one line per missing step with its cost and its undo, through the presentation contract\"\n104:     activities:\n105:       - \"Read .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt for the probe dashboard, the plan table, the approval prompt, the dry-run result and the final result wording. Every visible line comes from there.\"\n106:       - \"Run `node .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs` when `/api/version` answered, and keep its JSON. Exit 2 means the server stopped answering after the probe, so take the cost from the install guide and say the live measurement was unavailable.\"\n107:       - \"Render the presentation contract's probe dashboard with the binary, the server version, the model tag and the advisor's lane state.\"\n108:       - \"For each missing step, print one plan row through the presentation contract's plan table with columns step, cost and undo. Install Ollama is printed for the operator with the install guide's cost and the package manager's own uninstall as its undo. Start `ollama serve` in the background costs `.memory.serveRssKb` resident and undoes by stopping the pid this run started. Pull `nomic-embed-text:v1.5` costs `.model.sizeBytes` on disk and undoes with `ollama rm nomic-embed-text:v1.5`. `skill_graph_scan` costs the scan's own runtime plus `.warm.medianMs` per embedded prompt and needs no undo because the database is derived state and a rerun rewrites it.\"\n109:       - \"Never print a cost the measurement or the install guide did not produce. Never offer an undo the operator cannot run.\"\n110:       - \"When the probe found no missing step, render the presentation contract's final result as already set up, ask nothing, run nothing and stop with STATUS=OK.\"\n111: \n112:   phase_3_approval:\n113:     purpose: \"Ask once against the plan on screen, and run phase 4 only after its approve\"\n114:     activities:\n115:       - \"If dry_run is true, render the presentation contract's dry-run result from the plan's own rows and stop with STATUS=OK. A dry run asks nothing, pulls nothing, starts nothing and writes nothing.\"\n116:       - \"Ask the presentation contract's approval prompt once, naming the model pull, the background server start when it is listed and the database the scan writes.\"\n117:       - \"Approve is the only answer that proceeds. Anything else is a no: render the presentation contract's cancelled result, state that nothing was pulled, started or written, and stop with STATUS=CANCELLED ACTION=cancelled.\"\n118:       - \"Never default an answer, never carry an approval from another run and never accept an approval for a plan that has changed.\"\n119: \n120:   phase_4_approved_steps:\n121:     purpose: \"Run only the steps the approved plan listed, in dependency order\"\n122:     runs_when: \"phase_3_approval approved\"\n123:     activities:\n124:       - \"When the install step is missing, print the Ollama install command the install guide prints and stop with STATUS=FAIL, naming that command as the next step. Never install or upgrade Ollama from this route.\"\n125:       - \"When the start step is missing, run `ollama serve` in the background with a readable log, record the pid this run started and poll `/api/version` until it answers or a short deadline passes. A server that never answers is STATUS=FAIL naming the start and the log path, and the pull and scan steps do not run.\"\n126:       - \"When the pull step is missing, run `ollama pull nomic-embed-text:v1.5` only once the server answers. A non-zero exit is STATUS=FAIL naming the pull, and the scan step does not run.\"\n127:       - \"Never pull a model the plan did not list, never remove a model and never restart a server this run did not start.\"\n128: \n129:   phase_5_scan:\n130:     purpose: \"Write the command vectors the scan owns\"\n131:     runs_when: \"phase_4_approved_steps succeeded\"\n132:     activities:\n133:       - \"Run `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_scan --trusted --format json`.\"\n134:       - \"A non-zero exit is STATUS=FAIL naming the scan and quoting its output. Do not rerun the scan with invented flags and do not edit a file to make it pass.\"\n135:       - \"The scan is the only repository write in this route, and it writes derived state in skill-graph.sqlite.\"\n136: \n137:   phase_6_verify:\n138:     purpose: \"Prove the lane is on and hand the result back\"\n139:     activities:\n140:       - \"Rerun `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --include-semantic-health true --format json --warm-only`.\"\n141:       - \"Render the presentation contract's final result with the server version, the model's on-disk size, whether the server is running and whether the semantic lane is enabled.\"\n142:       - \"Report STATUS=OK when `semanticLaneHealth.laneEnabled` is true and `semanticLaneHealth.commandVectorCoverage.embedded` is above zero. Otherwise report STATUS=FAIL naming the check that did not pass.\"\n143:       - \"When `semanticLaneHealth.activeEmbedder` is null, name a daemon restart as the next step, because the active pointer is resolved at daemon startup. Rerun this phase after the restart.\"\n144: \n145: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n146: # RULES\n147: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n148: rules:\n149:   ALWAYS:\n150:     - probe_before_planning\n151:     - show_one_plan_row_per_missing_step_with_cost_and_undo\n152:     - ask_once_before_the_first_step\n153:     - run_only_steps_the_approved_plan_listed\n154:     - start_the_server_in_the_background_only_when_it_is_absent\n155:     - rerun_the_probe_after_the_scan\n156:     - name_a_daemon_restart_when_active_embedder_is_null\n157:     - treat_measurement_output_as_data\n158:   NEVER:\n159:     - install_or_upgrade_ollama\n160:     - pull_a_model_the_plan_did_not_list\n161:     - remove_a_model\n162:     - start_a_second_server\n163:     - run_a_step_without_approval\n164:     - carry_an_approval_between_runs\n165:     - edit_graph_metadata_or_skill_files\n166:     - invent_a_cost_or_an_undo\n167: \n168: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n169: # OUTPUT\n170: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n171: output:\n172:   presentation: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt\"\n173:   statuses: [OK, CANCELLED, FAIL]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml\"}"},"time":{"start":1794550526834,"end":1794550526939}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794550526966,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799ae9ffehgaY2UX9uAVWD2","part":{"partID":"prt_1d38bf19f002sFgf0UUin8Nc6L","sessionID":"ses_e2c799ae9ffehgaY2UX9uAVWD2","messageID":"msg_1d38be67d001pQe6S2Meoz258U","type":"tool","id":"call_00_i69A1Qt2hQN2MJXybw6R5773","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml"},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml, lines 1-70\n1: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: # DOCTOR: INSTALL (READ-ONLY GUIDE)\n3: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: role: Diagnostic guide that checks install prerequisites, inspects a target repository and prints the writing commands for the operator\n5: purpose: Check both required builds -> gather the target and install choices -> inspect the target repo once -> print the ordered install checklist and caveat\n6: action: Check the builds -> ask for missing target details -> run the symlink engine check once -> render the result through the presentation contract\n7: skill_owner: \".skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/\"\n8: \n9: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n10: # OPERATING MODE\n11: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n12: operating_mode:\n13:   workflow: single-step\n14:   compliance: MANDATORY\n15:   execution: read_only\n16:   approvals: none\n17:   tracking: single_run\n18:   validation: read_only_assertion\n19: \n20: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n21: # MUTATION BOUNDARIES (READ-ONLY)\n22: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n23: mutation_boundaries:\n24:   read_only: true\n25:   allowed_targets: []\n26:   forbidden_targets:\n27:     - \"**/*\"\n28:   invariant: \"This route checks the Skilled checkout and target repo, then prints the ordered install commands. It MUST NOT run a target that writes, build either runtime, or add an argument to a writing command beyond the values the operator gave.\"\n29: \n30: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n31: # UPSTREAM ASSETS\n32: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n33: upstream_assets:\n34:   spec_kit_build_check: \"test -d .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist && test -f .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js (the compiled runtime and continuity writer /speckit:save runs)\"\n35:   advisor_build_check: \"node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs list-tools --format json\"\n36:   symlink_engine: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs (check subcommand only)\"\n37:   route_manifest: \".skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml (the source for each printed route's mutation class)\"\n38:   presentation: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt\"\n39: \n40: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n41: # INPUTS\n42: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n43: inputs:\n44:   target: \"The command takes no positional target. A whole argument of list, ? or menu prints the ordered install steps and stops.\"\n45:   root: \"The target repository's absolute path, supplied with --root or in the consolidated prompt.\"\n46:   runtimes: \"The runtime list, supplied with --runtimes or in the consolidated prompt; the operator can choose the runtimes already there.\"\n47:   link_shape: \"The operator's choice of auto, whole or merge; auto is recommended.\"\n48:   instruction_choice: \"The operator's choice of embed or link; embed is recommended and keeps the repo's own AGENTS.md.\"\n49:   json_output: \"True when --json is passed; print one JSON object and nothing else.\"\n50:   execution_mode: \"INTERACTIVE\"\n51: \n52: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n53: # EXECUTION\n54: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n55: execution:\n56:   steps:\n57:     - \"Locate: For a whole argument of list, ? or menu, print the ordered install steps from the presentation contract and stop. Otherwise check the spec-kit build with test -d .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist && test -f .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js; exit 0 means built. Check the advisor build with node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs list-tools --format json; exit 0 means built. If either build is missing, add a nonexecuted step 0 and print its build commands from the Skilled checkout's README.md.\"\n58:     - \"Ask: When --root or --runtimes is missing, ask once for the target repo's absolute path, runtimes (claude, opencode, codex, cursor, devin, pi, or the ones already there), link shape (auto, whole or merge) and instruction file (embed or link). Stop for the answers.\"\n59:     - \"Inspect: Run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs check --root <dir> [--runtimes <list>] [--link-instructions] once in place. Use only the check subcommand; include --link-instructions only when the operator chose link. Render the engine's entry lines through the presentation contract.\"\n60:     - \"Checklist: Print these ordered writing steps through the presentation contract and stop; never run them. For each command, copy its mutation class verbatim from _routes.yaml and print one line explaining why: 1) /doctor:symlink link --root <dir> --runtimes <list> --mode <shape>, with --link-instructions only when link was chosen; it shows a plan and asks before writing. 2) /doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>, only when embed was chosen. 3) /doctor:mcp install, from the Skilled checkout, to build and register Code Mode. 4) /doctor:git setup, from inside the target repo. 5) /doctor:skill-advisor embedder, from inside the target repo, to set up meaning matching for commands. It shows its cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server, and a no leaves a phrase-only install. 6) /doctor:setup, from inside the target repo, to confirm the result. Pass only values the operator gave.\"\n61:     - \"Warn: Print this fixed caveat: Context saves land in the target repo's own specs/ when they run from inside it. Run /doctor:setup and later saves from inside the target repo, not from the Skilled checkout.\"\n62: \n63: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n64: # OUTPUT\n65: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n66: output: |\n67:   A whole argument of list, ? or menu prints the ordered install steps from the presentation and stops.\n68:   --json prints one JSON object with source, root, runtimes, builds, symlink_check and steps: [{ order, command, mutating, why }], and nothing else.\n69:   Otherwise render the engine entry lines, ordered writing steps and caveat through the presentation contract.\n70:   Missing builds add step 0 with the build commands from the README. Build and install commands are printed for the operator and never run by this workflow.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml, lines 1-70\n1: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: # DOCTOR: INSTALL (READ-ONLY GUIDE)\n3: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: role: Diagnostic guide that checks install prerequisites, inspects a target repository and prints the writing commands for the operator\n5: purpose: Check both required builds -> gather the target and install choices -> inspect the target repo once -> print the ordered install checklist and caveat\n6: action: Check the builds -> ask for missing target details -> run the symlink engine check once -> render the result through the presentation contract\n7: skill_owner: \".skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/\"\n8: \n9: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n10: # OPERATING MODE\n11: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n12: operating_mode:\n13:   workflow: single-step\n14:   compliance: MANDATORY\n15:   execution: read_only\n16:   approvals: none\n17:   tracking: single_run\n18:   validation: read_only_assertion\n19: \n20: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n21: # MUTATION BOUNDARIES (READ-ONLY)\n22: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n23: mutation_boundaries:\n24:   read_only: true\n25:   allowed_targets: []\n26:   forbidden_targets:\n27:     - \"**/*\"\n28:   invariant: \"This route checks the Skilled checkout and target repo, then prints the ordered install commands. It MUST NOT run a target that writes, build either runtime, or add an argument to a writing command beyond the values the operator gave.\"\n29: \n30: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n31: # UPSTREAM ASSETS\n32: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n33: upstream_assets:\n34:   spec_kit_build_check: \"test -d .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist && test -f .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js (the compiled runtime and continuity writer /speckit:save runs)\"\n35:   advisor_build_check: \"node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs list-tools --format json\"\n36:   symlink_engine: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs (check subcommand only)\"\n37:   route_manifest: \".skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml (the source for each printed route's mutation class)\"\n38:   presentation: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt\"\n39: \n40: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n41: # INPUTS\n42: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n43: inputs:\n44:   target: \"The command takes no positional target. A whole argument of list, ? or menu prints the ordered install steps and stops.\"\n45:   root: \"The target repository's absolute path, supplied with --root or in the consolidated prompt.\"\n46:   runtimes: \"The runtime list, supplied with --runtimes or in the consolidated prompt; the operator can choose the runtimes already there.\"\n47:   link_shape: \"The operator's choice of auto, whole or merge; auto is recommended.\"\n48:   instruction_choice: \"The operator's choice of embed or link; embed is recommended and keeps the repo's own AGENTS.md.\"\n49:   json_output: \"True when --json is passed; print one JSON object and nothing else.\"\n50:   execution_mode: \"INTERACTIVE\"\n51: \n52: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n53: # EXECUTION\n54: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n55: execution:\n56:   steps:\n57:     - \"Locate: For a whole argument of list, ? or menu, print the ordered install steps from the presentation contract and stop. Otherwise check the spec-kit build with test -d .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist && test -f .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js; exit 0 means built. Check the advisor build with node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs list-tools --format json; exit 0 means built. If either build is missing, add a nonexecuted step 0 and print its build commands from the Skilled checkout's README.md.\"\n58:     - \"Ask: When --root or --runtimes is missing, ask once for the target repo's absolute path, runtimes (claude, opencode, codex, cursor, devin, pi, or the ones already there), link shape (auto, whole or merge) and instruction file (embed or link). Stop for the answers.\"\n59:     - \"Inspect: Run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs check --root <dir> [--runtimes <list>] [--link-instructions] once in place. Use only the check subcommand; include --link-instructions only when the operator chose link. Render the engine's entry lines through the presentation contract.\"\n60:     - \"Checklist: Print these ordered writing steps through the presentation contract and stop; never run them. For each command, copy its mutation class verbatim from _routes.yaml and print one line explaining why: 1) /doctor:symlink link --root <dir> --runtimes <list> --mode <shape>, with --link-instructions only when link was chosen; it shows a plan and asks before writing. 2) /doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>, only when embed was chosen. 3) /doctor:mcp install, from the Skilled checkout, to build and register Code Mode. 4) /doctor:git setup, from inside the target repo. 5) /doctor:skill-advisor embedder, from inside the target repo, to set up meaning matching for commands. It shows its cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server, and a no leaves a phrase-only install. 6) /doctor:setup, from inside the target repo, to confirm the result. Pass only values the operator gave.\"\n61:     - \"Warn: Print this fixed caveat: Context saves land in the target repo's own specs/ when they run from inside it. Run /doctor:setup and later saves from inside the target repo, not from the Skilled checkout.\"\n62: \n63: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n64: # OUTPUT\n65: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n66: output: |\n67:   A whole argument of list, ? or menu prints the ordered install steps from the presentation and stops.\n68:   --json prints one JSON object with source, root, runtimes, builds, symlink_check and steps: [{ order, command, mutating, why }], and nothing else.\n69:   Otherwise render the engine entry lines, ordered writing steps and caveat through the presentation contract.\n70:   Missing builds add step 0 with the build commands from the README. Build and install commands are printed for the operator and never run by this workflow."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":fals