{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794550549739,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799ae9ffehgaY2UX9uAVWD2","part":{"partID":"prt_1d38c4ccf001cpk4UNAxoeckOi","sessionID":"ses_e2c799ae9ffehgaY2UX9uAVWD2","messageID":"msg_1d38c3d07001i07B17y9OBXDg5","type":"tool","id":"call_01_V9nJbOd5oebpszGzQDHe4759","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt"},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt, lines 1-111\n1: # /doctor:setup Presentation Contract\n2: \n3: This file is the single source of truth for user-facing presentation in `/doctor:setup`: the argument failure, the doctor target list, the per-leg result table, result templates, and next-step text. The command router owns asset routing only. The workflow YAML owns execution behavior.\n4: \n5: ## 1. Argument Failure\n6: \n7: ```text\n8: Unknown argument: [argument]\n9: /doctor:setup takes no target and no flag. Run /doctor:setup on its own.\n10: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_argument\"\n11: ```\n12: \n13: ## 2. Doctor Target List\n14: \n15: Render this table first, before any leg runs.\n16: \n17: | Command | What it checks |\n18: |---------|----------------|\n19: | `/doctor:setup` | This overview: the doctor target list and the seven read-only setup legs |\n20: | `/doctor:helper [<problem in plain words>] [--json]` | Rank the doctor commands that fit a described problem, with the class and the reason on every line |\n21: | `/doctor:env list` | The documented environment switches and where each value comes from |\n22: | `/doctor:update` | Whether a newer spec-kit release is available (bare runs the read-only check) |\n23: | `/doctor:git setup` | Whether the sk-git install, hooks, trust and standards are live |\n24: | `/doctor:git hooks` | Which shipped git hook gates are on or off, and switching one |\n25: | `/doctor:git standards` | The commit, PR and branch rules in .sk-git/ |\n26: | `/doctor:sk-code setup` | The sk-code setup battery, with a repair command per failing leg |\n27: | `/doctor:sk-code quality` | The repository quality config the gate reads with its tools, errors and disabled hygiene rules, then creating `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-quality/repository/quality.json` once |\n28: | `/doctor:ci report` | Lists every workflow with its switch state, trigger, filters and drift flags, read against the repository CI profile; `scaffold` and `toggle` are the confirmed action routes |\n29: | `/doctor:sk-skill check [<name-or-path>] [--json] [--into-hub <hub>]` | How far one skill, or the whole fleet, is from the Skilled format, row by row, with the repair for each finding |\n30: | `/doctor:sk-skill convert <name-or-path> [--dry-run]` | Moving one skill to the Skilled format: the plan, one yes per write, the backup, the write and the engine's undo block |\n31: | `/doctor:agents-md [check|embed|restore] [--json] [--root <dir>] [--dry-run]` | The root instruction file: which shipped sections are current, embedding the template over a printed plan and its digest, and putting one recorded run back |\n32: | `/doctor:speckit` | The generated trigger index, its lookup and the ripgrep recipes |\n33: | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` | Whether each runtime's agent, command, prompt and hook mirrors match .skilled |\n34: | `/doctor:skill-advisor tune` | Advisor recommendation quality and scoring tuning |\n35: | `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` | Rebuilding the skill graph database |\n36: | `/doctor:skill-advisor skill-budget` | Skill description character budgets |\n37: | `/doctor:skill-advisor parent-skill` | A parent skill hub's structure and registry |\n38: | `/doctor:skill-advisor skill-graph-freshness` | Drift between the compiled, SQLite and on-disk skill graph |\n39: | `/doctor:skill-advisor router-reach` | Whether each declared routing phrase reaches its hub |\n40: | `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` | Meaning matching for commands: whether the local embedder answers, what it costs, and the plan that pulls the model and starts the server after a yes |\n41: | `/doctor:deep-loop` | Deep-loop coverage graphs and convergence for research, review and council runs |\n42: | `/doctor:mcp` | Code Mode install and debug, its UTCP configuration and runtime registration |\n43: | `/doctor:install [--root <dir>] [--runtimes <list>] [--json]` | Putting Skilled into your own project repo: the build check, what is already linked, and the ordered setup commands to run |\n44: | `/doctor:symlink [check|link|unlink] [--json] [--root <dir>]` | The framework links in a project repo: which runtime folders are linked, broken or missing, linking them over a printed plan and its digest, and undoing one recorded run |\n45: | `/doctor:overlay [status|apply|repin] [--json] [--root <dir>]` | A vendored Skilled tree's own overlays: which destinations are out of sync and why, then putting them back, capturing one live edit, or re-pinning the tree to a newer upstream commit over a staged plan, after one yes |\n46: \n47: ## 3. Per-Leg Result Table\n48: \n49: Render one row per leg, in the workflow's order.\n50: \n51: | Leg | Command | Result | Repair |\n52: |-----|---------|--------|--------|\n53: | [leg] | [check-only command] | [PASS|FAIL|SKIP|DEGRADED|ERROR] | [the doctor command that repairs it or shows why, or none] |\n54: \n55: | Leg | Repair when it fails |\n56: |-----|----------------------|\n57: | sk-code | `/doctor:sk-code setup` |\n58: | sk-git | `/doctor:git setup` |\n59: | trigger-index | `/doctor:speckit` |\n60: | runtime-mirrors | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` |\n61: | advisor | Stale build: `npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build`. Other FAIL or DEGRADED results: `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`. |\n62: | embedder | `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` |\n63: | delivery | Missing hook: /doctor:runtime-mirrors, or /doctor:symlink check in a linked project. Unapproved Codex hook: the repair line the check prints, which opens /hooks in a Codex session |\n64: \n65: ## 4. Result Templates\n66: \n67: ### Summary\n68: \n69: ```text\n70: DOCTOR DIAGNOSTIC RESULT\n71: Target: setup\n72: Status: [OK|FAIL|ERROR]\n73: Mutation class: read-only\n74: Evidence: [N] legs, [N] passed, [N] failed, [N] skipped, [N] degraded, [N] errors\n75: Recommendation: [the doctor command for each failing or degraded leg, or none]\n76: Last session hop: [the first line `session-relaunch.cjs history --last 1` printed, or no hop recorded yet]\n77: [open notes: N handoff notes not claimed yet, oldest <filename>; shown only when history printed it]\n78: [the line `session-relaunch.cjs window` printed: Claude context window: N tokens, or Claude context window: none configured with the two settings that supply one]\n79: [orphans: N, about M MB; list them with node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/orphan-process-check.cjs --reap]\n80: STATUS=[status]\n81: ```\n82: \n83: The last session hop line is informational. It shows when a session last handed over, kept, claimed or finished a handoff, and it never changes the status. The open notes line appears only while a handoff note is still open, so a hand-over nobody finished stays visible.\n84: The Claude context window line is informational and never changes the status. It shows the window the Claude relaunch nudge measures against. When no window is configured it names `autoCompactWindow` and `SESSION_RELAUNCH_WINDOW_TOKENS`, and the nudge stays off until one is set or a `[1m]` model runs.\n85: The orphan line is informational only and never changes the doctor status. A model server kept on purpose with `SPECKIT_HF_MODEL_SERVER_ORPHAN_REAP=0` also shows as unsupervised, so do not reap it. With no orphan processes, print `orphans: none`. Run the listed `--reap` command to see each process, then use its confirmation command with `--yes` only when those are the processes to stop.\n86: \n87: ### Failure Summary\n88: \n89: ```text\n90: DOCTOR TARGET FAILED\n91: Target: setup\n92: Step: [leg]\n93: Error: [message]\n94: Next: [recommended command or manual action]\n95: STATUS=ERROR ERROR=\"[message]\"\n96: ```\n97: \n98: ## 5. Troubleshooting Display\n99: \n100: | Situation | Suggested Action |\n101: |-----------|------------------|\n102: | A leg reports FAIL | Run the doctor command in that leg's Repair cell, then rerun `/doctor:setup` |\n103: | The advisor leg reports SKIP | Exit 75 has no `staleDistWarning` in stderr JSON. The advisor daemon is stopped because `--warm-only` does not start it |\n104: | The advisor leg reports FAIL for a stale build | Exit 75 includes `staleDistWarning` in stderr JSON. Run `npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build` |\n105: | The advisor leg reports DEGRADED | Exit 0 has `data.freshness` other than `live`. The skill graph is not live. Run `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` |\n106: | The sk-git leg reports DEGRADED | No sk-git check failed, but one is unknown or a gate is saved off. Run `/doctor:git setup` to see which. On a runtime the battery cannot name, the AI-tool check stays unknown |\n107: | The trigger-index leg reports stale documents | Run `/doctor:speckit` to see which documents are stale |\n108: | The delivery leg reports DEGRADED | A runtime cannot receive the advisor brief. Run the repair the leg names, then rerun /doctor:setup. The install still works without it |\n109: | Route manifest parse error | Run `bash .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh` |\n110: \n111: End interactive presentations with: `What would you like to do next?`","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt, lines 1-111\n1: # /doctor:setup Presentation Contract\n2: \n3: This file is the single source of truth for user-facing presentation in `/doctor:setup`: the argument failure, the doctor target list, the per-leg result table, result templates, and next-step text. The command router owns asset routing only. The workflow YAML owns execution behavior.\n4: \n5: ## 1. Argument Failure\n6: \n7: ```text\n8: Unknown argument: [argument]\n9: /doctor:setup takes no target and no flag. Run /doctor:setup on its own.\n10: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_argument\"\n11: ```\n12: \n13: ## 2. Doctor Target List\n14: \n15: Render this table first, before any leg runs.\n16: \n17: | Command | What it checks |\n18: |---------|----------------|\n19: | `/doctor:setup` | This overview: the doctor target list and the seven read-only setup legs |\n20: | `/doctor:helper [<problem in plain words>] [--json]` | Rank the doctor commands that fit a described problem, with the class and the reason on every line |\n21: | `/doctor:env list` | The documented environment switches and where each value comes from |\n22: | `/doctor:update` | Whether a newer spec-kit release is available (bare runs the read-only check) |\n23: | `/doctor:git setup` | Whether the sk-git install, hooks, trust and standards are live |\n24: | `/doctor:git hooks` | Which shipped git hook gates are on or off, and switching one |\n25: | `/doctor:git standards` | The commit, PR and branch rules in .sk-git/ |\n26: | `/doctor:sk-code setup` | The sk-code setup battery, with a repair command per failing leg |\n27: | `/doctor:sk-code quality` | The repository quality config the gate reads with its tools, errors and disabled hygiene rules, then creating `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-quality/repository/quality.json` once |\n28: | `/doctor:ci report` | Lists every workflow with its switch state, trigger, filters and drift flags, read against the repository CI profile; `scaffold` and `toggle` are the confirmed action routes |\n29: | `/doctor:sk-skill check [<name-or-path>] [--json] [--into-hub <hub>]` | How far one skill, or the whole fleet, is from the Skilled format, row by row, with the repair for each finding |\n30: | `/doctor:sk-skill convert <name-or-path> [--dry-run]` | Moving one skill to the Skilled format: the plan, one yes per write, the backup, the write and the engine's undo block |\n31: | `/doctor:agents-md [check|embed|restore] [--json] [--root <dir>] [--dry-run]` | The root instruction file: which shipped sections are current, embedding the template over a printed plan and its digest, and putting one recorded run back |\n32: | `/doctor:speckit` | The generated trigger index, its lookup and the ripgrep recipes |\n33: | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` | Whether each runtime's agent, command, prompt and hook mirrors match .skilled |\n34: | `/doctor:skill-advisor tune` | Advisor recommendation quality and scoring tuning |\n35: | `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` | Rebuilding the skill graph database |\n36: | `/doctor:skill-advisor skill-budget` | Skill description character budgets |\n37: | `/doctor:skill-advisor parent-skill` | A parent skill hub's structure and registry |\n38: | `/doctor:skill-advisor skill-graph-freshness` | Drift between the compiled, SQLite and on-disk skill graph |\n39: | `/doctor:skill-advisor router-reach` | Whether each declared routing phrase reaches its hub |\n40: | `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` | Meaning matching for commands: whether the local embedder answers, what it costs, and the plan that pulls the model and starts the server after a yes |\n41: | `/doctor:deep-loop` | Deep-loop coverage graphs and convergence for research, review and council runs |\n42: | `/doctor:mcp` | Code Mode install and debug, its UTCP configuration and runtime registration |\n43: | `/doctor:install [--root <dir>] [--runtimes <list>] [--json]` | Putting Skilled into your own project repo: the build check, what is already linked, and the ordered setup commands to run |\n44: | `/doctor:symlink [check|link|unlink] [--json] [--root <dir>]` | The framework links in a project repo: which runtime folders are linked, broken or missing, linking them over a printed plan and its digest, and undoing one recorded run |\n45: | `/doctor:overlay [status|apply|repin] [--json] [--root <dir>]` | A vendored Skilled tree's own overlays: which destinations are out of sync and why, then putting them back, capturing one live edit, or re-pinning the tree to a newer upstream commit over a staged plan, after one yes |\n46: \n47: ## 3. Per-Leg Result Table\n48: \n49: Render one row per leg, in the workflow's order.\n50: \n51: | Leg | Command | Result | Repair |\n52: |-----|---------|--------|--------|\n53: | [leg] | [check-only command] | [PASS|FAIL|SKIP|DEGRADED|ERROR] | [the doctor command that repairs it or shows why, or none] |\n54: \n55: | Leg | Repair when it fails |\n56: |-----|----------------------|\n57: | sk-code | `/doctor:sk-code setup` |\n58: | sk-git | `/doctor:git setup` |\n59: | trigger-index | `/doctor:speckit` |\n60: | runtime-mirrors | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` |\n61: | advisor | Stale build: `npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build`. Other FAIL or DEGRADED results: `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`. |\n62: | embedder | `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` |\n63: | delivery | Missing hook: /doctor:runtime-mirrors, or /doctor:symlink check in a linked project. Unapproved Codex hook: the repair line the check prints, which opens /hooks in a Codex session |\n64: \n65: ## 4. Result Templates\n66: \n67: ### Summary\n68: \n69: ```text\n70: DOCTOR DIAGNOSTIC RESULT\n71: Target: setup\n72: Status: [OK|FAIL|ERROR]\n73: Mutation class: read-only\n74: Evidence: [N] legs, [N] passed, [N] failed, [N] skipped, [N] degraded, [N] errors\n75: Recommendation: [the doctor command for each failing or degraded leg, or none]\n76: Last session hop: [the first line `session-relaunch.cjs history --last 1` printed, or no hop recorded yet]\n77: [open notes: N handoff notes not claimed yet, oldest <filename>; shown only when history printed it]\n78: [the line `session-relaunch.cjs window` printed: Claude context window: N tokens, or Claude context window: none configured with the two settings that supply one]\n79: [orphans: N, about M MB; list them with node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/orphan-process-check.cjs --reap]\n80: STATUS=[status]\n81: ```\n82: \n83: The last session hop line is informational. It shows when a session last handed over, kept, claimed or finished a handoff, and it never changes the status. The open notes line appears only while a handoff note is still open, so a hand-over nobody finished stays visible.\n84: The Claude context window line is informational and never changes the status. It shows the window the Claude relaunch nudge measures against. When no window is configured it names `autoCompactWindow` and `SESSION_RELAUNCH_WINDOW_TOKENS`, and the nudge stays off until one is set or a `[1m]` model runs.\n85: The orphan line is informational only and never changes the doctor status. A model server kept on purpose with `SPECKIT_HF_MODEL_SERVER_ORPHAN_REAP=0` also shows as unsupervised, so do not reap it. With no orphan processes, print `orphans: none`. Run the listed `--reap` command to see each process, then use its confirmation command with `--yes` only when those are the processes to stop.\n86: \n87: ### Failure Summary\n88: \n89: ```text\n90: DOCTOR TARGET FAILED\n91: Target: setup\n92: Step: [leg]\n93: Error: [message]\n94: Next: [recommended command or manual action]\n95: STATUS=ERROR ERROR=\"[message]\"\n96: ```\n97: \n98: ## 5. Troubleshooting Display\n99: \n100: | Situation | Suggested Action |\n101: |-----------|------------------|\n102: | A leg reports FAIL | Run the doctor command in that leg's Repair cell, then rerun `/doctor:setup` |\n103: | The advisor leg reports SKIP | Exit 75 has no `staleDistWarning` in stderr JSON. The advisor daemon is stopped because `--warm-only` does not start it |\n104: | The advisor leg reports FAIL for a stale build | Exit 75 includes `staleDistWarning` in stderr JSON. Run `npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build` |\n105: | The advisor leg reports DEGRADED | Exit 0 has `data.freshness` other than `live`. The skill graph is not live. Run `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` |\n106: | The sk-git leg reports DEGRADED | No sk-git check failed, but one is unknown or a gate is saved off. Run `/doctor:git setup` to see which. On a runtime the battery cannot name, the AI-tool check stays unknown |\n107: | The trigger-index leg reports stale documents | Run `/doctor:speckit` to see which documents are stale |\n108: | The delivery leg reports DEGRADED | A runtime cannot receive the advisor brief. Run the repair the leg names, then rerun /doctor:setup. The install still works without it |\n109: | Route manifest parse error | Run `bash .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh` |\n110: \n111: End interactive presentations with: `What would you like to do next?`"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1794550549711,"end":1794550549739}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794550549750,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799ae9ffehgaY2UX9uAVWD2","part":{"partID":"prt_1d38c4b9b002y1vSLNCWHff1aj","sessionID":"ses_e2c799ae9ffehgaY2UX9uAVWD2","messageID":"msg_1d38c3d07001i07B17y9OBXDg5","type":"tool","id":"call_00_iln1d1e6V0lp3iAHD6LA3499","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt"},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt, lines 1-204\n1: # /doctor:install Presentation Contract\n2: \n3: This file is the single source of truth for user-facing presentation in `/doctor:install`: the argument failure, the build check, the install prompt, the symlink check, the ordered steps, the caveat line, result templates and next-step text. The command router owns flag binding and asset loading. The workflow YAML owns execution behavior.\n4: \n5: This command only reads. Every step that writes is printed with its exact command, and the operator runs it.\n6: \n7: Write for someone who has just cloned Skilled and wants it in their own project: plain words, short sentences, one thing at a time.\n8: \n9: ## 1. Argument Failure\n10: \n11: An unknown argument fails before any workflow YAML loads and prints the wording below with the bracketed parts filled in, then ends with the status line. Nothing is read and nothing is changed.\n12: \n13: | Situation | Wording |\n14: |-----------|---------|\n15: | A flag other than `--root <dir>`, `--runtimes <list>` and `--json` | `Unknown argument: [argument]` then `/doctor:install takes --root <dir>, --runtimes <list> and --json, or list and ?.` then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_argument\"` |\n16: | `--root` or `--runtimes` with no value after it | The same two lines, then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_argument\"` |\n17: | A second positional token | The same two lines, then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_argument\"` |\n18: \n19: `list`, `?` and `menu` as the whole argument print the steps in section 6, with `<dir>`, `<list>` and `<shape>` left as they stand, then stop. They load no workflow and inspect nothing.\n20: \n21: ## 2. The Build Check\n22: \n23: The Skilled checkout is the repository this command runs in. The runtimes load two builds from it, so check both before anything is planned.\n24: \n25: | Build | Check, run from the checkout root | Built when |\n26: |-------|-----------------------------------|------------|\n27: | Spec Kit | `test -d .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist && test -f .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js` | exit 0 |\n28: | Skill Advisor | `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs list-tools --format json` | exit 0 |\n29: \n30: Render both lines, then carry on either way: a missing build never stops the guide.\n31: \n32: ```text\n33: DOCTOR INSTALL — BUILDS\n34: Source: [the Skilled checkout]\n35: Spec Kit build: [found at .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist and runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js | missing]\n36: Advisor CLI: [answers list-tools | missing or not built]\n37: ```\n38: \n39: A missing build becomes step 0 of the checklist. Step 0 carries the README's build commands word for word:\n40: \n41: ```bash\n42: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit install\n43: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit run build\n44: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime install\n45: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build\n46: ```\n47: \n48: Step 0 runs from the Skilled checkout. Its why line is: `Why: the session hooks and the advisor read these builds, so nothing else works until they are there.` It has no mutation class because no doctor route owns it.\n49: \n50: ## 3. The Install Prompt\n51: \n52: Ask every answer that is still missing in one prompt, then wait. This follows the consolidated question protocol. Questions 1 and 2 are dropped when `--root` and `--runtimes` were passed. The link shape and the instruction choice have no flag, so they are always in the prompt.\n53: \n54: ```text\n55: Where should Skilled go? Answer any or all in one reply, for example \"/Users/me/code/my-app, claude and codex, auto, embed\".\n56: \n57: 1) Target repo: the absolute path, for example /Users/me/code/my-app\n58: 2) Runtimes: claude, opencode, codex, cursor, devin, pi, or \"the ones already there\"\n59: 3) Link shape: auto / whole / merge   (auto unless a real folder already sits where a link would go)\n60: 4) Instruction file: embed / link   (embed keeps the repo's own AGENTS.md; link points AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md and REPO RULES.md at the checkout's copies)\n61: ```\n62: \n63: The example carries all four answers so the shape of a full reply is visible. Never print a question the flags already answered.\n64: \n65: ## 4. Accepted Answers\n66: \n67: | Answer | Binds | Meaning |\n68: |--------|-------|---------|\n69: | An absolute path | `--root <dir>` | The project repo that receives the links. The path must exist and be a directory; the engine exits 2 and names it otherwise |\n70: | `claude`, `claude and codex`, `claude,opencode` | `--runtimes <list>` | The runtime folders to link, as a comma list |\n71: | `the ones already there`, empty, `any` | no `--runtimes` | The engine keeps the runtimes its own detection finds in the root, and always links `.skilled` |\n72: | `auto` | `--mode auto` | Whole link where the path is free, merge where a real folder is in the way. The one to pick |\n73: | `whole` | `--mode whole` | One link per entry, refused where a real folder exists |\n74: | `merge` | `--mode merge` | A real folder whose children are links. A local file already in the folder is kept and reported, never overwritten |\n75: | `embed` | step 2 stays | The repo keeps its own `AGENTS.md` and the shipped sections are refreshed into it |\n76: | `link` | step 1 gains `--link-instructions`, step 2 is dropped | `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and `REPO RULES.md` become links into the checkout |\n77: \n78: A runtime name outside the seven, a shape outside the three, or an instruction word outside the two is not guessed. Ask that one question again with the accepted values. When the engine refuses a root, show its `ERROR:` line as it printed and ask question 1 again.\n79: \n80: ## 5. The Symlink Check\n81: \n82: Run `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs check --root <dir> [--runtimes <list>] [--link-instructions]` once, in place and read-only, then render its entry lines as they print:\n83: \n84: ```text\n85: DOCTOR INSTALL — WHAT IS ALREADY THERE\n86: Root: [the target repo]\n87: [the engine's entry lines, verbatim, with its indented detail lines and its repo-level warnings]\n88: ```\n89: \n90: Do not re-sort the lines, re-word a status or sum them into a verdict. A `missing` line is work for step 1, not a failure, and the check still exits 0 for it. The check exits 1 only on drift: a broken or foreign link, including a broken link inside a merged folder, a missing source or a tracked absolute link. Missing children in a partial merge do not count as drift. Add `--link-instructions` when the instruction choice is `link`.\n91: \n92: | Status | What it means for this install |\n93: |--------|-------------------------------|\n94: | `linked-whole` | Already a link into the checkout. Step 1 has nothing to do for it |\n95: | `linked-merge` | A real folder whose children are links. Nothing to do |\n96: | `partial-merge` | A real folder missing some links. Step 1 fills the gaps and never deletes a local file |\n97: | `missing` | Not there yet. Step 1 creates it |\n98: | `broken` | A link whose target is gone. Step 1 replaces it |\n99: | `foreign-link` | A link that points somewhere else. Left alone, and the engine refuses to touch it |\n100: | `local` | A real file or folder of the repo's own. Left alone |\n101: | `source-missing` | The checkout has no such path. Nothing is planned |\n102: \n103: ## 6. The Ordered Steps\n104: \n105: This is the checklist, and it is also what `list`, `?` and `menu` print. Each step carries its exact command, its class and one line of why.\n106: \n107: The class column is the manifest's `mutating` value for the route that owns the printed command, verbatim, so it is read from the route table and never guessed. A command with no route of its own prints `n/a`.\n108: \n109: ```text\n110: 1) /doctor:symlink link --root <dir> --runtimes <list> --mode <shape>   [class]\n111:    Why: creates the links. It shows a plan first and asks before it writes.\n112: \n113: 2) /doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>   [class]\n114:    Why: keeps the repo's own AGENTS.md and refreshes the shipped sections into it. Dropped when the instruction choice is link.\n115: \n116: 3) /doctor:mcp install   [class]\n117:    Why: builds and registers Code Mode. Run it from the Skilled checkout.\n118: \n119: 4) /doctor:git setup   [class]\n120:    Why: checks the git hooks and sk-git settings, and names the repair for each one that is off. Run it from the target repo.\n121: \n122: 5) /doctor:skill-advisor embedder   [class]\n123:    Why: sets up meaning matching for commands. It shows the cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server. Run it from the target repo.\n124: \n125: 6) /doctor:setup   [class]\n126:    Why: confirms the result. Run it from the target repo.\n127: ```\n128: \n129: Run them in this order. Step 1 takes `--link-instructions` when the instruction choice is `link`.\n130: \n131: When the workflow renders the checklist after the check, print this header above the steps:\n132: \n133: ```text\n134: DOCTOR INSTALL — [the target repo]\n135: Source: [the Skilled checkout]\n136: Runtimes: [the runtime list]   Link shape: [auto|whole|merge]   Instruction file: [embed|link]\n137: ```\n138: \n139: A printed step is handed back, never run: each writing command shows its own plan, asks its own yes and writes under its own gate. This command adds no argument to a printed command beyond the values the operator gave.\n140: \n141: ## 7. The Caveat Line\n142: \n143: Print this one line word for word after the steps, on every run, before the result. It is fixed: do not shorten it and do not rewrite it in the operator's words.\n144: \n145: ```text\n146: context saves land in the target repo's own specs/ when they run from inside it, so run /doctor:setup and later saves from inside the target repo, not from the Skilled checkout.\n147: ```\n148: \n149: ## 8. Result Templates\n150: \n151: ### Summary\n152: \n153: ```text\n154: DOCTOR INSTALL RESULT\n155: Source: [the Skilled checkout]\n156: Root: [the target repo]\n157: Runtimes: [the runtime list]\n158: Link shape: [auto|whole|merge]\n159: Instruction file: [embed|link]\n160: Builds: [both found | missing: <which>, printed as step 0]\n161: Already there: [n] linked, [n] missing, [n] to repair\n162: Steps: [n] printed, [n] of them write\n163: Next: run step 1 from the Skilled checkout, then the rest in order\n164: STATUS=OK STEPS=[n]\n165: ```\n166: \n167: ### JSON\n168: \n169: `--json` prints one JSON object and nothing else: no build lines, no steps, no caveat, no header.\n170: \n171: | Key | Value |\n172: |-----|-------|\n173: | `source` | The Skilled checkout's absolute path |\n174: | `root` | The target repo's absolute path |\n175: | `runtimes` | The runtime names, as strings |\n176: | `builds` | One entry per probe in section 2, true or false |\n177: | `symlink_check` | The engine's `check --json` object, unchanged |\n178: | `steps` | One object per printed step: `order`, `command`, `mutating`, `why` |\n179: \n180: ### Failure Summary\n181: \n182: ```text\n183: DOCTOR TARGET FAILED\n184: Target: guide\n185: Step: [the step that failed]\n186: Error: [message]\n187: Next: [the accepted invocation, or the command to rerun]\n188: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"[message]\"\n189: ```\n190: \n191: ## 9. Troubleshooting Display\n192: \n193: | Situation | Suggested Action |\n194: |-----------|------------------|\n195: | The engine exits 2 | Bad invocation or a refused root. Its first line names the flag or the path. Fix that one thing and rerun the same command |\n196: | The root is the checkout, sits inside it, or holds it | The engine refuses it, because linking a checkout into itself would loop. Name the project repo that should receive the links |\n197: | A build is missing | Run the four `npm` commands in section 2 from the checkout, then rerun this guide. They also print as step 0 |\n198: | A step prints `n/a` as its class | That printed command has no route in the manifest yet. The command still works; only its class is unknown |\n199: | A line reads `local` or `foreign-link` | Left alone on purpose. Move that file or link yourself, or bring it under step 1's shape, and rerun the guide |\n200: | Only the steps are wanted | `list` prints them with no build check and no inspection |\n201: | A saved session lands in the checkout's `specs/` | The save ran from the Skilled checkout. Run it again from inside the target repo, as the caveat in section 7 says |\n202: | The project copies Skilled in instead of linking it | This guide covers linking only. A copy that keeps its own changes keeps them as overlays: run `/doctor:overlay status --root <copy>`, and see the overlays reference in `system-skilled-doctor` for adopting the engine when the project already has its own overlay folder |\n203: \n204: End interactive presentations with: `What would you like to do next?`","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt, lines 1-204\n1: # /doctor:install Presentation Contract\n2: \n3: This file is the single source of truth for user-facing presentation in `/doctor:install`: the argument failure, the build check, the install prompt, the symlink check, the ordered steps, the caveat line, result templates and next-step text. The command router owns flag binding and asset loading. The workflow YAML owns execution behavior.\n4: \n5: This command only reads. Every step that writes is printed with its exact command, and the operator runs it.\n6: \n7: Write for someone who has just cloned Skilled and wants it in their own project: plain words, short sentences, one thing at a time.\n8: \n9: ## 1. Argument Failure\n10: \n11: An unknown argument fails before any workflow YAML loads and prints the wording below with the bracketed parts filled in, then ends with the status line. Nothing is read and nothing is changed.\n12: \n13: | Situation | Wording |\n14: |-----------|---------|\n15: | A flag other than `--root <dir>`, `--runtimes <list>` and `--json` | `Unknown argument: [argument]` then `/doctor:install takes --root <dir>, --runtimes <list> and --json, or list and ?.` then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_argument\"` |\n16: | `--root` or `--runtimes` with no value after it | The same two lines, then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_argument\"` |\n17: | A second positional token | The same two lines, then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_argument\"` |\n18: \n19: `list`, `?` and `menu` as the whole argument print the steps in section 6, with `<dir>`, `<list>` and `<shape>` left as they stand, then stop. They load no workflow and inspect nothing.\n20: \n21: ## 2. The Build Check\n22: \n23: The Skilled checkout is the repository this command runs in. The runtimes load two builds from it, so check both before anything is planned.\n24: \n25: | Build | Check, run from the checkout root | Built when |\n26: |-------|-----------------------------------|------------|\n27: | Spec Kit | `test -d .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist && test -f .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js` | exit 0 |\n28: | Skill Advisor | `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs list-tools --format json` | exit 0 |\n29: \n30: Render both lines, then carry on either way: a missing build never stops the guide.\n31: \n32: ```text\n33: DOCTOR INSTALL — BUILDS\n34: Source: [the Skilled checkout]\n35: Spec Kit build: [found at .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist and runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js | missing]\n36: Advisor CLI: [answers list-tools | missing or not built]\n37: ```\n38: \n39: A missing build becomes step 0 of the checklist. Step 0 carries the README's build commands word for word:\n40: \n41: ```bash\n42: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit install\n43: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit run build\n44: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime install\n45: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build\n46: ```\n47: \n48: Step 0 runs from the Skilled checkout. Its why line is: `Why: the session hooks and the advisor read these builds, so nothing else works until they are there.` It has no mutation class because no doctor route owns it.\n49: \n50: ## 3. The Install Prompt\n51: \n52: Ask every answer that is still missing in one prompt, then wait. This follows the consolidated question protocol. Questions 1 and 2 are dropped when `--root` and `--runtimes` were passed. The link shape and the instruction choice have no flag, so they are always in the prompt.\n53: \n54: ```text\n55: Where should Skilled go? Answer any or all in one reply, for example \"/Users/me/code/my-app, claude and codex, auto, embed\".\n56: \n57: 1) Target repo: the absolute path, for example /Users/me/code/my-app\n58: 2) Runtimes: claude, opencode, codex, cursor, devin, pi, or \"the ones already there\"\n59: 3) Link shape: auto / whole / merge   (auto unless a real folder already sits where a link would go)\n60: 4) Instruction file: embed / link   (embed keeps the repo's own AGENTS.md; link points AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md and REPO RULES.md at the checkout's copies)\n61: ```\n62: \n63: The example carries all four answers so the shape of a full reply is visible. Never print a question the flags already answered.\n64: \n65: ## 4. Accepted Answers\n66: \n67: | Answer | Binds | Meaning |\n68: |--------|-------|---------|\n69: | An absolute path | `--root <dir>` | The project repo that receives the links. The path must exist and be a directory; the engine exits 2 and names it otherwise |\n70: | `claude`, `claude and codex`, `claude,opencode` | `--runtimes <list>` | The runtime folders to link, as a comma list |\n71: | `the ones already there`, empty, `any` | no `--runtimes` | The engine keeps the runtimes its own detection finds in the root, and always links `.skilled` |\n72: | `auto` | `--mode auto` | Whole link where the path is free, merge where a real folder is in the way. The one to pick |\n73: | `whole` | `--mode whole` | One link per entry, refused where a real folder exists |\n74: | `merge` | `--mode merge` | A real folder whose children are links. A local file already in the folder is kept and reported, never overwritten |\n75: | `embed` | step 2 stays | The repo keeps its own `AGENTS.md` and the shipped sections are refreshed into it |\n76: | `link` | step 1 gains `--link-instructions`, step 2 is dropped | `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and `REPO RULES.md` become links into the checkout |\n77: \n78: A runtime name outside the seven, a shape outside the three, or an instruction word outside the two is not guessed. Ask that one question again with the accepted values. When the engine refuses a root, show its `ERROR:` line as it printed and ask question 1 again.\n79: \n80: ## 5. The Symlink Check\n81: \n82: Run `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs check --root <dir> [--runtimes <list>] [--link-instructions]` once, in place and read-only, then render its entry lines as they print:\n83: \n84: ```text\n85: DOCTOR INSTALL — WHAT IS ALREADY THERE\n86: Root: [the target repo]\n87: [the engine's entry lines, verbatim, with its indented detail lines and its repo-level warnings]\n88: ```\n89: \n90: Do not re-sort the lines, re-word a status or sum them into a verdict. A `missing` line is work for step 1, not a failure, and the check still exits 0 for it. The check exits 1 only on drift: a broken or foreign link, including a broken link inside a merged folder, a missing source or a tracked absolute link. Missing children in a partial merge do not count as drift. Add `--link-instructions` when the instruction choice is `link`.\n91: \n92: | Status | What it means for this install |\n93: |--------|-------------------------------|\n94: | `linked-whole` | Already a link into the checkout. Step 1 has nothing to do for it |\n95: | `linked-merge` | A real folder whose children are links. Nothing to do |\n96: | `partial-merge` | A real folder missing some links. Step 1 fills the gaps and never deletes a local file |\n97: | `missing` | Not there yet. Step 1 creates it |\n98: | `broken` | A link whose target is gone. Step 1 replaces it |\n99: | `foreign-link` | A link that points somewhere else. Left alone, and the engine refuses to touch it |\n100: | `local` | A real file or folder of the repo's own. Left alone |\n101: | `source-missing` | The checkout has no such path. Nothing is planned |\n102: \n103: ## 6. The Ordered Steps\n104: \n105: This is the checklist, and it is also what `list`, `?` and `menu` print. Each step carries its exact command, its class and one line of why.\n106: \n107: The class column is the manifest's `mutating` value for the route that owns the printed command, verbatim, so it is read from the route table and never guessed. A command with no route of its own prints `n/a`.\n108: \n109: ```text\n110: 1) /doctor:symlink link --root <dir> --runtimes <list> --mode <shape>   [class]\n111:    Why: creates the links. It shows a plan first and asks before it writes.\n112: \n113: 2) /doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>   [class]\n114:    Why: keeps the repo's own AGENTS.md and refreshes the shipped sections into it. Dropped when the instruction choice is link.\n115: \n116: 3) /doctor:mcp install   [class]\n117:    Why: builds and registers Code Mode. Run it from the Skilled checkout.\n118: \n119: 4) /doctor:git setup   [class]\n120:    Why: checks the git hooks and sk-git settings, and names the repair for each one that is off. Run it from the target repo.\n121: \n122: 5) /doctor:skill-advisor embedder   [class]\n123:    Why: sets up meaning matching for commands. It shows the cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server. Run it from the target repo.\n124: \n125: 6) /doctor:setup   [class]\n126:    Why: confirms the result. Run it from the target repo.\n127: ```\n128: \n129: Run them in this order. Step 1 takes `--link-instructions` when the instruction choice is `link`.\n130: \n131: When the workflow renders the checklist after the check, print this header above the steps:\n132: \n133: ```text\n134: DOCTOR INSTALL — [the target repo]\n135: Source: [the Skilled checkout]\n136: Runtimes: [the runtime list]   Link shape: [auto|whole|merge]   Instruction file: [embed|link]\n137: ```\n138: \n139: A printed step is handed back, never run: each writing command shows its own plan, asks its own yes and writes under its own gate. This command adds no argument to a printed command beyond the values the operator gave.\n140: \n141: ## 7. The Caveat Line\n142: \n143: Print this one line word for word after the steps, on every run, before the result. It is fixed: do not shorten it and do not rewrite it in the operator's words.\n144: \n145: ```text\n146: context saves land in the target repo's own specs/ when they run from inside it, so run /doctor:setup and later saves from inside the target repo, not from the Skilled checkout.\n147: ```\n148: \n149: ## 8. Result Templates\n150: \n151: ### Summary\n152: \n153: ```text\n154: DOCTOR INSTALL RESULT\n155: Source: [the Skilled checkout]\n156: Root: [the target repo]\n157: Runtimes: [the runtime list]\n158: Link shape: [auto|whole|merge]\n159: Instruction file: [embed|link]\n160: Builds: [both found | missing: <which>, printed as step 0]\n161: Already there: [n] linked, [n] missing, [n] to repair\n162: Steps: [n] printed, [n] of them write\n163: Next: run step 1 from the Skilled checkout, then the rest in order\n164: STATUS=OK STEPS=[n]\n165: ```\n166: \n167: ### JSON\n168: \n169: `--json` prints one JSON object and nothing else: no build lines, no steps, no caveat, no header.\n170: \n171: | Key | Value |\n172: |-----|-------|\n173: | `source` | The Skilled checkout's absolute path |\n174: | `root` | The target repo's absolute path |\n175: | `runtimes` | The runtime names, as strings |\n176: | `builds` | One entry per probe in section 2, true or false |\n177: | `symlink_check` | The engine's `check --json` object, unchanged |\n178: | `steps` | One object per printed step: `order`, `command`, `mutating`, `why` |\n179: \n180: ### Failure Summary\n181: \n182: ```text\n183: DOCTOR TARGET FAILED\n184: Target: guide\n185: Step: [the step that failed]\n186: Error: [message]\n187: Next: [the accepted invocation, or the command to rerun]\n188: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"[message]\"\n189: ```\n190: \n191: ## 9. Troubleshooting Display\n192: \n193: | Situation | Suggested Action |\n194: |-----------|------------------|\n195: | The engine exits 2 | Bad invocation or a refused root. Its first line names the flag or the path. Fix that one thing and rerun the same command |\n196: | The root is the checkout, sits inside it, or holds it | The engine refuses it, because linking a checkout into itself would loop. Name the project repo that should receive the links |\n197: | A build is missing | Run the four `npm` commands in section 2 from the checkout, then rerun this guide. They also print as step 0 |\n198: | A step prints `n/a` as its class | That printed command has no route in the manifest yet. The command still works; only its class is unknown |\n199: | A line reads `local` or `foreign-link` | Left alone on purpose. Move that file or link yourself, or bring it under step 1's shape, and rerun the guide |\n200: | Only the steps are wanted | `list` prints them with no build check and no inspection |\n201: | A saved session lands in the checkout's `specs/` | The save ran from the Skilled checkout. Run it again from inside the target repo, as the caveat in section 7 says |\n202: | The project copies Skilled in instead of linking it | This guide covers linking only. A copy that keeps its own changes keeps them as overlays: run `/doctor:overlay status --root <copy>`, and see the overlays reference in `system-skilled-doctor` for adopting the engine when the project already has its own overlay folder |\n203: \n204: End interactive presentations with: `What would you like to do next?`"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1794550549403,"end":1794550549750}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794550553421,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799ae9ffehgaY2UX9uAVWD2","part":{"id":"prt_1d38c5b4d001H9Bh05RAcg03Fh","sessionID":"ses_e2c799ae9ffehgaY2UX9uAVWD2","messageID":"msg_1d38c3d07001i07B17y9OBXDg5","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"10a5d360df78015550071ff4eca30750352c2568","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":380,"output":92,"reasoning":360,"cache":{"read":172416,"write":0}}}}
