hboards, approval prompts, diagnostic dashboards, result summaries, or next-step text.\n27: \n28: ---\n29: \n30: ## 2. OWNED ASSETS\n31: \n32: | Purpose | Asset |\n33: |---------|-------|\n34: | Route manifest | `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` |\n35: | Presentation source of truth | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt` |\n36: \n37: ---\n38: \n39: ## 3. MODE ROUTING\n40: \n41: - `_routes.yaml` is the canonical routing and mutation-class manifest; this command owns the routes whose `command` is `/doctor:skill-advisor`.\n42: - `execution_mode` is always `INTERACTIVE`.\n43: - The positional target is parsed before any flag; global flag pre-parse is forbidden.\n44: - Unknown or cross-target flags fail before YAML load.\n45: - The YAML start condition is: target bound, workflow asset exists, presentation asset loaded, and every target setup variable resolved.\n46: - If any referenced asset is missing, stop and report the missing path.\n47: - The YAML owns workflow behavior; the presentation Markdown owns visible wording and layout.\n48: \n49: ---\n50: \n51: ## 4. EXECUTION TARGETS\n52: \n53: These existing YAML assets are referenced only. The router must not modify them.\n54: \n55: | Target | Workflow |\n56: |--------|----------|\n57: | `tune` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-tune.yaml` |\n58: | `rebuild` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-rebuild.yaml` |\n59: | `skill-graph-freshness` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-graph-freshness.yaml` |\n60: | `router-reach` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-router-reach.yaml` |\n61: | `embedder` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml` |\n62: | `skill-budget` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-budget.yaml` |\n63: | `parent-skill` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-parent-skill.yaml` |\n64: \n65: 1. Read `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt`.\n66: 2. Read `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` and keep the `/doctor:skill-advisor` routes.\n67: 3. Take `target` from the input gate.\n68: 4. If target is unknown, render the presentation contract's unknown-target failure and stop.\n69: 5. Resolve `yaml`, `setup_vars`, `allowed_flags`, `mutating`, `mcp_tools`, `cli_commands`, and script invocations from the route.\n70: 6. Parse remaining flags using only the resolved target's `allowed_flags`; reject cross-target flags using the presentation contract's error wording.\n71: 7. Resolve any missing setup variables using the presentation contract's per-target setup prompts.\n72: 8. Load the resolved workflow YAML from `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/<yaml>` and execute it step by step.\n73: 9. Use the presentation contract, not this router, for user prompts, dashboards, result summaries, and next-step display.\n74: \n75: ---\n76: \n77: ## 5. PRESENTATION BOUNDARY\n78: \n79: The following content lives only in `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt`:\n80: \n81: - Target-resolution menu, help text, accepted answers, and failure wording.\n82: - Per-target setup prompts for unresolved fields.\n83: - Route manifest display for `list`, `?`, or `--list`.\n84: - The rebuild plan, approval prompt and result templates.\n85: - Troubleshooting and next-step display text.\n86: \n87: ---\n88: \n89: ## 6. WORKFLOW SUMMARY\n90: \n91: The router resolves a `target` against the `/doctor:skill-advisor` routes in `_routes.yaml`, binds that target's workflow YAML plus its setup variables, allowed flags, and mutation class, then executes it step by step under an always-interactive mode.\n92: `tune` re-tunes the scoring lanes with per-skill review, `rebuild` rebuilds `skill-graph.sqlite` through the advisor CLI behind a backup, and the four read-only targets report graph drift, router reach, description budgets and parent-hub structure.\n93: `list`, `?`, or `--list` render the route manifest instead of di