{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794550735282,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799ae9ffehgaY2UX9uAVWD2","part":{"partID":"prt_1d38f1f670024vDgT8XSwd0ErE","sessionID":"ses_e2c799ae9ffehgaY2UX9uAVWD2","messageID":"msg_1d38f0d64001k1aBjeLHYxqzEX","type":"tool","id":"call_00_cSQiqCUA2wXp6sbmZ0ZQ7802","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && wc -l .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown && rg -n \"agents-md|hook-wiring|codex-hook|doctor:install|doctor:setup|runtimes|seven|dsh\" INSTALL-SKILLED.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown | head -50"},"output":"     272 .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:33:+-- agents-md-check.cjs\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:34:+-- agents-md-embed.cjs\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:35:+-- agents-md-manifest.cjs\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:42:+-- codex-hook-approval-check.cjs\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:48:+-- hook-wiring-check.cjs\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:63:|   +-- agents-md-sections.cjs      # the one segmenter, classifier, block reader and delivery measurement the two engines and their suites share\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:102:| `agents-md-check.cjs` | The read-only AGENTS.md check: twelve rows reporting the install state, the sections lost or reordered, the currency of each body, every pin, the delivery budget, the shape of the repository block, the repository's own content and its local edits, each runtime copy, the `REPO RULES.md` router and the source template's purity. Three of them run their owner as a child instead of re-deriving it, carrying the rule-copy canary's budget lines, the gate 1 pointer sync's Cursor block and the repo-rules checker's summary. `--root <dir>` classifies another repository and `--json` prints the same report for a machine. A row it cannot prove reads `UNKNOWN` rather than `PASS`, so it exits 0 on no finding, 1 on a finding or an unproven row and 2 on a failed precondition. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:103:| `agents-md-embed.cjs` | The writing half of `/doctor:agents-md`, in three subcommands. `plan` composes every target in memory and prints the targets, the diffs, the new block, the byte budget, the preservation ledger, the backup folder and the plan digest, and writes nothing. `apply --plan-digest <digest>` recomposes, refuses a digest the tree no longer produces, backs up every path it will touch, writes only inside the allowlist it checks in code and then proves the composition against the bytes on disk, restoring from the backup and ending `STATUS=FAIL` when one line went missing. `restore --run=<dir>` puts back exactly the paths that run's `manifest.json` records, removes the files, and the empty folders, that run created, and keeps the backup. It exits 0 when there was nothing to do or the work finished, 1 on a failed proof or a declined run and 2 on a failed precondition or a path outside the allowlist. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:104:| `agents-md-manifest.cjs` | Generates and gates the shipped manifest's `derived` key: a copy of every shipped body, its hash and the router rows, taken from the root documents. `--write` refreshes it and `--check` is the freshness gate, so a body that drifted from the template fails here instead of surfacing as a check finding. It refuses a heading no authored entry matches, an authored entry that matches nothing, and text above the first heading, and `--write` runs only in the repository that ships the template. Each of the three engines has its own suite: `agents-md-check.test.cjs`, `agents-md-embed.test.cjs` and `agents-md-manifest.test.cjs`, driven from the recipe folders under `tests/fixtures/agents-md/`. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:111:| `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` | The read-only Codex approval check: it finds the advisor's `UserPromptSubmit` entry in `.codex/hooks.json` and reports whether the Codex config holds a `trusted_hash` for that exact group and index, because Codex skips an unapproved entry without a warning. `--root <dir>` reads another checkout, `--config <path>` reads another config and `--json` prints one object. It prints `SKIP no-codex-hooks`, `PASS codex-hooks-approved`, `WARN codex-advisor-hook-absent` or `WARN codex-hooks-unapproved <root>` with the `/hooks` repair line, and never prints a hash. It exits 0 on a skip or an approval, 1 on a missing or unapproved entry and 2 on a bad argument. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:112:| `hook-wiring-check.cjs` | The read-only hook-wiring check: it reads `.claude/settings.json`, `.codex/hooks.json`, `.cursor/hooks.json` and `.devin/hooks.v1.json`, and reports whether the prompt hook entry is present for each runtime folder it finds. `--root <dir>` is required and `--json` prints one object. It prints `ok <runtime>` or `hook-missing <runtime> <file>`, skips a runtime whose folder is absent and never writes. It exits 0 when every installed runtime is wired, 1 when one is missing and 2 on a bad argument or a missing root. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:171:| `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs [--root <dir>] [--json]` | Report the twelve AGENTS.md rows for this repository or another one, and write nothing. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:172:| `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs plan [--root <dir>] [--keep-claude-md] [--create-router]` | Print every target with its diff, the new block, the budget, the preservation ledger, the backup folder and the plan digest. Writes nothing, and prints `NOTHING TO DO` when the repository is already in its target state. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:173:| `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs apply --plan-digest <digest> [--root <dir>]` | Back up, write inside the allowlist and prove the composition, only with the digest the plan printed. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:174:| `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs restore --run=<dir> --yes` | Put back exactly the paths one run recorded, and remove the files, and the empty folders, that run created. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:175:| `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-manifest.cjs --check` | Fail when the manifest's derived key no longer matches the shipped documents. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:184:| `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agent-roster-mirror-check.cjs` | Report agent-roster coverage drift across runtimes. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:231:| `agents-md-check.cjs` | Read-only over any root: it reads the instruction file, its runtime copies and `REPO RULES.md`, runs three owner tools as children in their check-only forms and writes nothing. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:232:| `agents-md-embed.cjs` | `plan` is read-only. `apply` writes only the paths in its own allowlist, all of them under the target root, after backing each one up under `.skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<digest>/` (or the OS temp folder when that path is not ignored), and restores from that backup itself when its post-write proof fails. `restore` writes only the paths the run's `manifest.json` records and keeps the backup folder. It never runs `git add`, `git commit` or `git stash`. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:233:| `agents-md-manifest.cjs` | `--check` is read-only. `--write` rewrites the manifest's `derived` key and refuses to run outside the repository that ships the template. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:234:| `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` | Read-only over any root. It reads `.codex/hooks.json` and the Codex config, prints no hash and takes no write path. It exits 0 on a skip or an approval, 1 on a missing or unapproved entry and 2 on a bad argument. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:235:| `hook-wiring-check.cjs` | Read-only over any root. It writes no file and runs no installer, and its JSON form reports the same readings as its lines. It exits 0 when every installed runtime carries its entry, 1 when one is missing and 2 on a bad argument or a missing root. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:257:| `agents-md-check.cjs` | `--root <dir>`. It also takes `--manifest <path>` and `--source` |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:54:- `/doctor:install` sets up the embedder by default: its checklist includes `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder`, which prints the cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server, so answering no leaves a phrase-only install.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:296:Source of truth: [`@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/registry.ts`](../system-spec-kit/shared/embeddings/registry.ts). Skill-advisor's local `runtime/lib/embedders/registry.ts` is a re-export shim — adding manifests is a single edit in the shared package. The seven text-tuned manifests registered today, each as a frozen `EmbedderManifest`:\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:372:`/doctor:install` includes the embedder setup by default, and the setup itself runs as `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` from inside the target repo. The route probes `command -v ollama`, `/api/version`, `/api/tags` and `advisor_status --include-semantic-health true`, prints one plan row per missing step with its cost and its undo, and asks once before it runs anything. A no stops with `STATUS=CANCELLED` and changes nothing. `--dry-run` prints the plan and stops with `STATUS=OK`. The route never installs or upgrades Ollama: it prints the install command for the operator, and the install guide owns that cost. The two health flags split the diagnosis: `includeEmbeddingsHealth` probes only the hf-local model server, while `includeSemanticHealth` reports the active embedder and probes its backend.\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:40:Build the Spec Kit first. The runtimes' session hooks load this build.\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:57:Open the repository in any of the seven runtimes: OpenCode, Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Devin, Pi or DeepSeek Harness (DSH). Then run:\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:60:/doctor:setup\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:67:DSH loads the repository's guards and the skill advisor only from the patches a run names, so start it with `--patch .dsh/patches/guards.patch.yml`.\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:69:Codex runs a project hook only after you approve it, so open `/hooks` in a Codex session at the repository root and approve each entry it lists. Codex keeps each approval as a `trusted_hash` in `~/.codex/config.toml`, so a changed entry needs approving again, and `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` prints `PASS codex-hooks-approved` once the advisor's entry is approved.\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:71:`/doctor:setup` also reports a delivery leg, which reads DEGRADED with the repair step when a runtime's prompt hook is missing or Codex has not approved it.\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:108:It installs the dependencies and builds Code Mode when its `dist` is missing or stale. It configures the `.utcp_config.json` manuals. It registers Code Mode in the seven project config files, two of them for Claude. Each write waits for its own approval. Add `--runtime <name>` to register one runtime only: `opencode`, `claude`, `codex`, `cursor`, `pi` or `devin`.\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:116:Your checkout is ready once `/doctor:setup` passes. Run `/doctor:setup` again whenever something looks wrong. To use Skilled in a project of your own, pick a way in below.\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:127:/doctor:install\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:147:| 1 | `/doctor:symlink link --root <dir> --runtimes <list> --mode auto` | the checkout | Links `.skilled` and your runtime folders into the project |\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:148:| 2 | `/doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>` | the checkout | Adds the shipped sections to your `AGENTS.md` and leaves the CLAUDE.md pointer. Skip it if you chose `link` |\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:152:| 6 | `/doctor:setup` | your project | Confirms the whole setup works |\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:197:> **Context saves.** `/speckit:save` records your session's progress in the `specs/` folder of the repo you run it from. Run `/doctor:setup` and every save from your project, not from the checkout.\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:340:| **When something looks wrong** | Run `/doctor:setup` in your project | Run `/doctor:overlay status`, then `/doctor:setup` |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"     272 .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:33:+-- agents-md-check.cjs\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:34:+-- agents-md-embed.cjs\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:35:+-- agents-md-manifest.cjs\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:42:+-- codex-hook-approval-check.cjs\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:48:+-- hook-wiring-check.cjs\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:63:|   +-- agents-md-sections.cjs      # the one segmenter, classifier, block reader and delivery measurement the two engines and their suites share\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:102:| `agents-md-check.cjs` | The read-only AGENTS.md check: twelve rows reporting the install state, the sections lost or reordered, the currency of each body, every pin, the delivery budget, the shape of the repository block, the repository's own content and its local edits, each runtime copy, the `REPO RULES.md` router and the source template's purity. Three of them run their owner as a child instead of re-deriving it, carrying the rule-copy canary's budget lines, the gate 1 pointer sync's Cursor block and the repo-rules checker's summary. `--root <dir>` classifies another repository and `--json` prints the same report for a machine. A row it cannot prove reads `UNKNOWN` rather than `PASS`, so it exits 0 on no finding, 1 on a finding or an unproven row and 2 on a failed precondition. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:103:| `agents-md-embed.cjs` | The writing half of `/doctor:agents-md`, in three subcommands. `plan` composes every target in memory and prints the targets, the diffs, the new block, the byte budget, the preservation ledger, the backup folder and the plan digest, and writes nothing. `apply --plan-digest <digest>` recomposes, refuses a digest the tree no longer produces, backs up every path it will touch, writes only inside the allowlist it checks in code and then proves the composition against the bytes on disk, restoring from the backup and ending `STATUS=FAIL` when one line went missing. `restore --run=<dir>` puts back exactly the paths that run's `manifest.json` records, removes the files, and the empty folders, that run created, and keeps the backup. It exits 0 when there was nothing to do or the work finished, 1 on a failed proof or a declined run and 2 on a failed precondition or a path outside the allowlist. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:104:| `agents-md-manifest.cjs` | Generates and gates the shipped manifest's `derived` key: a copy of every shipped body, its hash and the router rows, taken from the root documents. `--write` refreshes it and `--check` is the freshness gate, so a body that drifted from the template fails here instead of surfacing as a check finding. It refuses a heading no authored entry matches, an authored entry that matches nothing, and text above the first heading, and `--write` runs only in the repository that ships the template. Each of the three engines has its own suite: `agents-md-check.test.cjs`, `agents-md-embed.test.cjs` and `agents-md-manifest.test.cjs`, driven from the recipe folders under `tests/fixtures/agents-md/`. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:111:| `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` | The read-only Codex approval check: it finds the advisor's `UserPromptSubmit` entry in `.codex/hooks.json` and reports whether the Codex config holds a `trusted_hash` for that exact group and index, because Codex skips an unapproved entry without a warning. `--root <dir>` reads another checkout, `--config <path>` reads another config and `--json` prints one object. It prints `SKIP no-codex-hooks`, `PASS codex-hooks-approved`, `WARN codex-advisor-hook-absent` or `WARN codex-hooks-unapproved <root>` with the `/hooks` repair line, and never prints a hash. It exits 0 on a skip or an approval, 1 on a missing or unapproved entry and 2 on a bad argument. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:112:| `hook-wiring-check.cjs` | The read-only hook-wiring check: it reads `.claude/settings.json`, `.codex/hooks.json`, `.cursor/hooks.json` and `.devin/hooks.v1.json`, and reports whether the prompt hook entry is present for each runtime folder it finds. `--root <dir>` is required and `--json` prints one object. It prints `ok <runtime>` or `hook-missing <runtime> <file>`, skips a runtime whose folder is absent and never writes. It exits 0 when every installed runtime is wired, 1 when one is missing and 2 on a bad argument or a missing root. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:171:| `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs [--root <dir>] [--json]` | Report the twelve AGENTS.md rows for this repository or another one, and write nothing. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:172:| `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs plan [--root <dir>] [--keep-claude-md] [--create-router]` | Print every target with its diff, the new block, the budget, the preservation ledger, the backup folder and the plan digest. Writes nothing, and prints `NOTHING TO DO` when the repository is already in its target state. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:173:| `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs apply --plan-digest <digest> [--root <dir>]` | Back up, write inside the allowlist and prove the composition, only with the digest the plan printed. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:174:| `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs restore --run=<dir> --yes` | Put back exactly the paths one run recorded, and remove the files, and the empty folders, that run created. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:175:| `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-manifest.cjs --check` | Fail when the manifest's derived key no longer matches the shipped documents. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:184:| `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agent-roster-mirror-check.cjs` | Report agent-roster coverage drift across runtimes. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:231:| `agents-md-check.cjs` | Read-only over any root: it reads the instruction file, its runtime copies and `REPO RULES.md`, runs three owner tools as children in their check-only forms and writes nothing. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:232:| `agents-md-embed.cjs` | `plan` is read-only. `apply` writes only the paths in its own allowlist, all of them under the target root, after backing each one up under `.skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<digest>/` (or the OS temp folder when that path is not ignored), and restores from that backup itself when its post-write proof fails. `restore` writes only the paths the run's `manifest.json` records and keeps the backup folder. It never runs `git add`, `git commit` or `git stash`. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:233:| `agents-md-manifest.cjs` | `--check` is read-only. `--write` rewrites the manifest's `derived` key and refuses to run outside the repository that ships the template. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:234:| `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` | Read-only over any root. It reads `.codex/hooks.json` and the Codex config, prints no hash and takes no write path. It exits 0 on a skip or an approval, 1 on a missing or unapproved entry and 2 on a bad argument. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:235:| `hook-wiring-check.cjs` | Read-only over any root. It writes no file and runs no installer, and its JSON form reports the same readings as its lines. It exits 0 when every installed runtime carries its entry, 1 when one is missing and 2 on a bad argument or a missing root. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:257:| `agents-md-check.cjs` | `--root <dir>`. It also takes `--manifest <path>` and `--source` |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:54:- `/doctor:install` sets up the embedder by default: its checklist includes `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder`, which prints the cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server, so answering no leaves a phrase-only install.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:296:Source of truth: [`@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/registry.ts`](../system-spec-kit/shared/embeddings/registry.ts). Skill-advisor's local `runtime/lib/embedders/registry.ts` is a re-export shim — adding manifests is a single edit in the shared package. The seven text-tuned manifests registered today, each as a frozen `EmbedderManifest`:\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:372:`/doctor:install` includes the embedder setup by default, and the setup itself runs as `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` from inside the target repo. The route probes `command -v ollama`, `/api/version`, `/api/tags` and `advisor_status --include-semantic-health true`, prints one plan row per missing step with its cost and its undo, and asks once before it runs anything. A no stops with `STATUS=CANCELLED` and changes nothing. `--dry-run` prints the plan and stops with `STATUS=OK`. The route never installs or upgrades Ollama: it prints the install command for the operator, and the install guide owns that cost. The two health flags split the diagnosis: `includeEmbeddingsHealth` probes only the hf-local model server, while `includeSemanticHealth` reports the active embedder and probes its backend.\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:40:Build the Spec Kit first. The runtimes' session hooks load this build.\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:57:Open the repository in any of the seven runtimes: OpenCode, Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Devin, Pi or DeepSeek Harness (DSH). Then run:\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:60:/doctor:setup\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:67:DSH loads the repository's guards and the skill advisor only from the patches a run names, so start it with `--patch .dsh/patches/guards.patch.yml`.\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:69:Codex runs a project hook only after you approve it, so open `/hooks` in a Codex session at the repository root and approve each entry it lists. Codex keeps each approval as a `trusted_hash` in `~/.codex/config.toml`, so a changed entry needs approving again, and `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` prints `PASS codex-hooks-approved` once the advisor's entry is approved.\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:71:`/doctor:setup` also reports a delivery leg, which reads DEGRADED with the repair step when a runtime's prompt hook is missing or Codex has not approved it.\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:108:It installs the dependencies and builds Code Mode when its `dist` is missing or stale. It configures the `.utcp_config.json` manuals. It registers Code Mode in the seven project config files, two of them for Claude. Each write waits for its own approval. Add `--runtime <name>` to register one runtime only: `opencode`, `claude`, `codex`, `cursor`, `pi` or `devin`.\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:116:Your checkout is ready once `/doctor:setup` passes. Run `/doctor:setup` again whenever something looks wrong. To use Skilled in a project of your own, pick a way in below.\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:127:/doctor:install\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:147:| 1 | `/doctor:symlink link --root <dir> --runtimes <list> --mode auto` | the checkout | Links `.skilled` and your runtime folders into the project |\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:148:| 2 | `/doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>` | the checkout | Adds the shipped sections to your `AGENTS.md` and leaves the CLAUDE.md pointer. Skip it if you chose `link` |\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:152:| 6 | `/doctor:setup` | your project | Confirms the whole setup works |\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:197:> **Context saves.** `/speckit:save` records your session's progress in the `specs/` folder of the repo you run it from. Run `/doctor:setup` and every save from your project, not from the checkout.\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:340:| **When something looks wrong** | Run `/doctor:setup` in your project | Run `/doctor:overlay status`, then `/doctor:setup` |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && wc -l .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown && rg -n \\\"agents-md|hook-wiring|codex-hook|doctor:install|doctor:setup|runtimes|seven|dsh\\\" INSTALL-SKILLED.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown | head -50\"}"},"time":{"start":1794550734695,"end":1794550735282}}}}
