{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794550751476,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799ae9ffehgaY2UX9uAVWD2","part":{"partID":"prt_1d38f6092001NLMHve39kJiBUe","sessionID":"ses_e2c799ae9ffehgaY2UX9uAVWD2","messageID":"msg_1d38f555d001dC7zPCQ3Vtej05","type":"tool","id":"call_01_OpwV00mAvPSoKu0vnQll6700","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml"},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml, lines 1-69\n1: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: # DOCTOR: SYMLINK CHECK (READ-ONLY DIAGNOSTIC)\n3: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: role: Diagnostic Operator reporting the link state of one target repository against the Skilled manifest\n5: purpose: Report the status of the core link, selected runtimes and extras by running the check engine once, then render its report through the presentation contract\n6: action: Run the check engine once -> render its report through the presentation contract\n7: skill_owner: \".skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/\"\n8: \n9: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n10: # OPERATING MODE\n11: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n12: operating_mode:\n13:   workflow: single_step_check\n14:   compliance: MANDATORY\n15:   execution: read_only\n16:   approvals: none\n17:   tracking: single_run\n18:   validation: read_only_assertion\n19: \n20: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n21: # MUTATION BOUNDARIES (READ-ONLY)\n22: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n23: mutation_boundaries:\n24:   read_only: true\n25:   allowed_targets: []\n26:   forbidden_targets:\n27:     - \"**/*\"\n28:   invariant: \"This route runs the check subcommand only. It never runs plan, apply or unlink, and it never writes a link, directory, ignore line or run record. Findings describe the target repository and do not change its state. The route also runs the read-only hook-wiring check, which reads each installed runtime's prompt hook entry and never writes.\"\n29: \n30: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n31: # UPSTREAM ASSETS\n32: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n33: upstream_assets:\n34:   engine: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs\"\n35:   manifest: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/symlink-manifest.json\"\n36:   presentation: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-presentation.txt\"\n37:   hook_wiring: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\"\n38: \n39: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n40: # INPUTS\n41: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n42: inputs:\n43:   execution_mode: \"INTERACTIVE\"\n44:   root: \"Required target project repository, passed as --root <dir>. The engine requires it to exist and be a directory.\"\n45:   runtimes: \"Optional comma-separated runtime names, passed as --runtimes <list> when supplied: claude,opencode,codex,cursor,devin,pi. When omitted, the engine selects runtimes whose primary entry already exists in the target root. The core entry is always included.\"\n46:   include: \"Optional comma-separated extras, passed as --include <list> when supplied: repo-rules,github,utcp,env.\"\n47:   link_instructions: \"When true, pass --link-instructions to include AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md and REPO RULES.md.\"\n48:   json_output: \"When true, pass --json and show only the engine's JSON object. The default is false.\"\n49:   target: \"The route accepts the check action. A missing --root value or any unsupported flag is refused by the engine.\"\n50: \n51: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n52: # EXECUTION\n53: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n54: execution:\n55:   steps:\n56:     - \"Check that .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs, .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/symlink-manifest.json and .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-presentation.txt exist. If one is missing, report its path and stop with STATUS=FAIL. Do not create the presentation file here.\"\n57:     - 'Run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs check --root \"{root}\", adding --runtimes \"{runtimes}\" when supplied, --include \"{include}\" when supplied, --link-instructions when requested and --json when requested.'\n58:     - \"The engine reports one status for each selected manifest entry, with detail lines for missing children, broken links and local conflicts. It also reports detected runtimes, tracked absolute links, Git state and applicable warnings.\"\n59:     - \"Exit 0 means no drift was found. Exit 1 means drift was found: broken links, foreign links, broken links inside merged folders, a missing source, or tracked absolute links. Missing children in a partial merge do not count as drift. Show the report and end with STATUS=WARN. Exit 2 means the invocation or target root was refused. Quote the engine message and end with STATUS=FAIL.\"\n60:     - 'After the engine report, run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \"{root}\" to read the prompt hook entry each installed runtime loads. It skips a runtime whose folder is absent. Show every hook-missing <runtime> line as printed. Exit 0 leaves the status unchanged. Exit 1 ends the run with STATUS=WARN and names the repair: copy the prompt hook entry from the matching file in the Skilled checkout into the target file for that runtime. Exit 2 means the check was refused: quote its message and end with STATUS=FAIL.'\n61:     - \"Render the engine output through .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-presentation.txt. When --json was requested, print the engine's JSON object alone.\"\n62: \n63: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n64: # OUTPUT\n65: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n66: output: |\n67:   STATUS=OK when the engine exits 0. Show the check report through the presentation contract.\n68:   STATUS=WARN when the engine exits 1. Show the check report through the presentation contract.\n69:   STATUS=FAIL when the engine exits 2 or cannot run. Name the accepted invocation (/doctor:symlink check --root <dir> [flags]) and quote the engine message.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml, lines 1-69\n1: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: # DOCTOR: SYMLINK CHECK (READ-ONLY DIAGNOSTIC)\n3: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: role: Diagnostic Operator reporting the link state of one target repository against the Skilled manifest\n5: purpose: Report the status of the core link, selected runtimes and extras by running the check engine once, then render its report through the presentation contract\n6: action: Run the check engine once -> render its report through the presentation contract\n7: skill_owner: \".skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/\"\n8: \n9: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n10: # OPERATING MODE\n11: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n12: operating_mode:\n13:   workflow: single_step_check\n14:   compliance: MANDATORY\n15:   execution: read_only\n16:   approvals: none\n17:   tracking: single_run\n18:   validation: read_only_assertion\n19: \n20: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n21: # MUTATION BOUNDARIES (READ-ONLY)\n22: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n23: mutation_boundaries:\n24:   read_only: true\n25:   allowed_targets: []\n26:   forbidden_targets:\n27:     - \"**/*\"\n28:   invariant: \"This route runs the check subcommand only. It never runs plan, apply or unlink, and it never writes a link, directory, ignore line or run record. Findings describe the target repository and do not change its state. The route also runs the read-only hook-wiring check, which reads each installed runtime's prompt hook entry and never writes.\"\n29: \n30: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n31: # UPSTREAM ASSETS\n32: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n33: upstream_assets:\n34:   engine: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs\"\n35:   manifest: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/symlink-manifest.json\"\n36:   presentation: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-presentation.txt\"\n37:   hook_wiring: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\"\n38: \n39: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n40: # INPUTS\n41: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n42: inputs:\n43:   execution_mode: \"INTERACTIVE\"\n44:   root: \"Required target project repository, passed as --root <dir>. The engine requires it to exist and be a directory.\"\n45:   runtimes: \"Optional comma-separated runtime names, passed as --runtimes <list> when supplied: claude,opencode,codex,cursor,devin,pi. When omitted, the engine selects runtimes whose primary entry already exists in the target root. The core entry is always included.\"\n46:   include: \"Optional comma-separated extras, passed as --include <list> when supplied: repo-rules,github,utcp,env.\"\n47:   link_instructions: \"When true, pass --link-instructions to include AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md and REPO RULES.md.\"\n48:   json_output: \"When true, pass --json and show only the engine's JSON object. The default is false.\"\n49:   target: \"The route accepts the check action. A missing --root value or any unsupported flag is refused by the engine.\"\n50: \n51: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n52: # EXECUTION\n53: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n54: execution:\n55:   steps:\n56:     - \"Check that .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs, .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/symlink-manifest.json and .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-presentation.txt exist. If one is missing, report its path and stop with STATUS=FAIL. Do not create the presentation file here.\"\n57:     - 'Run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs check --root \"{root}\", adding --runtimes \"{runtimes}\" when supplied, --include \"{include}\" when supplied, --link-instructions when requested and --json when requested.'\n58:     - \"The engine reports one status for each selected manifest entry, with detail lines for missing children, broken links and local conflicts. It also reports detected runtimes, tracked absolute links, Git state and applicable warnings.\"\n59:     - \"Exit 0 means no drift was found. Exit 1 means drift was found: broken links, foreign links, broken links inside merged folders, a missing source, or tracked absolute links. Missing children in a partial merge do not count as drift. Show the report and end with STATUS=WARN. Exit 2 means the invocation or target root was refused. Quote the engine message and end with STATUS=FAIL.\"\n60:     - 'After the engine report, run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \"{root}\" to read the prompt hook entry each installed runtime loads. It skips a runtime whose folder is absent. Show every hook-missing <runtime> line as printed. Exit 0 leaves the status unchanged. Exit 1 ends the run with STATUS=WARN and names the repair: copy the prompt hook entry from the matching file in the Skilled checkout into the target file for that runtime. Exit 2 means the check was refused: quote its message and end with STATUS=FAIL.'\n61:     - \"Render the engine output through .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-presentation.txt. When --json was requested, print the engine's JSON object alone.\"\n62: \n63: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n64: # OUTPUT\n65: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n66: output: |\n67:   STATUS=OK when the engine exits 0. Show the check report through the presentation contract.\n68:   STATUS=WARN when the engine exits 1. Show the check report through the presentation contract.\n69:   STATUS=FAIL when the engine exits 2 or cannot run. Name the accepted invocation (/doctor:symlink check --root <dir> [flags]) and quote the engine message."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml\"}"},"time":{"start":1794550751378,"end":1794550751476}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794550751479,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799ae9ffehgaY2UX9uAVWD2","part":{"partID":"prt_1d38f6070002zDY7vW6BiFk2PD","sessionID":"ses_e2c799ae9ffehgaY2UX9uAVWD2","messageID":"msg_1d38f555d001dC7zPCQ3Vtej05","type":"tool","id":"call_00_6qmamnRtcgptBjh54nXS2740","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml"},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml, lines 1-193\n1: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: # DOCTOR: RUNTIME MIRROR PARITY (READ-ONLY DIAGNOSTIC)\n3: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: role: Diagnostic Operator reporting whether every runtime config dir still mirrors its canonical source\n5: purpose: Detect drift across the agent, command, prompt and hook mirrors that .claude, .codex, .cursor, .devin, .pi and .dsh derive from .skilled, plus adapter-path resolution drift in the Claude, Codex, Cursor and Devin hook fallback chains\n6: action: Run every upstream-assets checker plus the hook-adapter fallback health checks -> aggregate their verdicts -> report per-surface drift\n7: skill_owner: \".skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/\"\n8: \n9: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n10: # OPERATING MODE\n11: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n12: operating_mode:\n13:   workflow: single-step\n14:   compliance: MANDATORY\n15:   execution: read_only\n16:   approvals: none\n17:   tracking: single_run\n18:   validation: read_only_assertion\n19: \n20: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n21: # MUTATION BOUNDARIES (READ-ONLY)\n22: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n23: mutation_boundaries:\n24:   read_only: true\n25:   allowed_targets: []\n26:   forbidden_targets:\n27:     - \"**/*\"\n28:   invariant: \"Every upstream_assets checker is invoked in its check-only form. This route MUST NOT run any generator in write mode, create or delete a symlink, or install a hook config. Repair is an explicit operator action, never a side effect of a diagnostic.\"\n29: \n30: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n31: # UPSTREAM ASSETS\n32: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n33: upstream_assets:\n34:   runtime_mirrors: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs\"\n35:   codex_agents: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/codex/sync-agents.cjs\"\n36:   codex_prompts: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/codex/sync-prompts.cjs\"\n37:   agent_roster: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agent-roster-mirror-check.cjs\"\n38:   agent_body_parity: \".skilled/bin/check-agent-mirror-sync.cjs\"\n39:   command_catalog: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/command-catalog-mirror-check.cjs\"\n40:   codex_hooks_installer: \".skilled/bin/install-codex-hooks.mjs\"\n41:   codex_hook_approval: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs\"\n42:   pi_agents: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/pi/sync-agents-pi.cjs\"\n43:   pi_prompts: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/pi/sync-prompts-pi.cjs\"\n44:   dsh_skills: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-skills-dsh.cjs\"\n45:   dsh_prompts: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-prompts-dsh.cjs\"\n46:   dsh_agents: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-agents-dsh.cjs\"\n47: \n48: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n49: # HOOK-ADAPTER FALLBACK HEALTH CHECKS\n50: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n51: # Every entry below is the primary adapter behind a `|| { <stderr>; <fallback JSON> }`\n52: # chain in .codex/hooks.json, .devin/hooks.v1.json, .claude/settings.json or\n53: # .cursor/hooks.json (the chains that carry the \"mkHookDrift\" marker). The one\n54: # exception is each fire-and-forget backgrounded reconcile command, which no\n55: # host reads stdout from and which deliberately runs without a fallback branch.\n56: # A missing path here is exactly the state a synthetic\n57: # adapter failure produces (e.g. temporarily renaming the compiled file), so a\n58: # `file_exists` failure on any row below is reported as a degraded hook adapter,\n59: # not a mirror-structure drift.\n60: hook_adapter_fallback_health_checks:\n61:   - { host: claude, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/hooks/dispatch/claude/dispatch-preflight-lint.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n62:   - { host: claude, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/claude/spec-gate-enforce.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n63:   - { host: claude, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/hooks/git-preflight-advisory.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n64:   - { host: claude, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/hooks/git-message-gate.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n65:   - { host: claude, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/hooks/task-dispatch/claude/task-dispatch-guard.cjs\", type: file_exists }\n66:   - { host: claude, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/hooks/task-dispatch/claude/fable-subagent-guard.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n67:   - { host: claude, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/hooks/mcp-route-guard/claude/mcp-route-guard.cjs\", type: file_exists }\n68:   - { host: claude, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/hooks/overlay-guard/claude/overlay-guard.cjs\", type: file_exists }\n69:   - { host: claude, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/hooks/env-secret-guard/command-hook/env-secret-guard.cjs\", type: file_exists }\n70:   - { host: claude, event: PostToolUse, path: \".skilled/hooks/env-secret-guard/command-hook/env-secret-guard-after.cjs\", type: file_exists }\n71:   - { host: claude, event: UserPromptSubmit, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js\", type: file_exists }\n72:   - { host: claude, event: UserPromptSubmit, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/claude/spec-gate-classify.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n73:   - { host: claude, event: SessionStart, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/session-prime.js\", type: file_exists }\n74:   - { host: claude, event: SessionStart, path: \".skilled/bin/worktree-guard.sh\", type: file_exists }\n75:   - { host: claude, event: SessionStart, path: \".skilled/bin/check-git-hooks.sh\", type: file_exists }\n76:   - { host: claude, event: SessionStart, path: \".skilled/bin/git-live-follow.sh\", type: file_exists }\n77:   - { host: claude, event: SessionStart, path: \".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-quality/scripts/check-dist-staleness.sh\", type: file_exists }\n78:   - { host: claude, event: SessionStart, path: \".skilled/bin/install-codex-hooks.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n79:   - { host: claude, event: Stop, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/session-stop.js\", type: file_exists }\n80:   - { host: claude, event: Stop, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/claude/completion-evidence-stop.cjs\", type: file_exists }\n81:   - { host: claude, event: SessionEnd, path: \".skilled/scripts/session-cleanup.sh\", type: file_exists }\n82:   - { host: claude, event: PostToolUse, path: \".skilled/hooks/post-edit-quality/claude/claude-posttooluse.cjs\", type: file_exists }\n83:   - { host: claude, event: PostToolUse, path: \".skilled/hooks/dispatch/claude/dispatch-audit-posttooluse.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n84:   - { host: claude, event: PreCompact, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/compact-inject.js\", type: file_exists }\n85:   - { host: cursor, event: sessionStart, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/cursor/session-start.js\", type: file_exists }\n86:   - { host: cursor, event: sessionStart, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/cursor/spec-gate-prebind.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n87:   - { host: cursor, event: sessionStart, path: \".skilled/bin/worktree-guard.sh\", type: file_exists }\n88:   - { host: cursor, event: sessionStart, path: \".skilled/bin/check-git-hooks.sh\", type: file_exists }\n89:   - { host: cursor, event: sessionStart, path: \".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-quality/scripts/check-dist-staleness.sh\", type: file_exists }\n90:   - { host: cursor, event: sessionStart, path: \".skilled/bin/install-codex-hooks.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n91:   - { host: cursor, event: sessionStart, path: \".skilled/hooks/goal/cursor/goal-inject.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n92:   - { host: cursor, event: sessionEnd, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/cursor/session-end.js\", type: file_exists }\n93:   - { host: cursor, event: sessionEnd, path: \".skilled/scripts/session-cleanup.sh\", type: file_exists }\n94:   - { host: cursor, event: preToolUse, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/cursor/spec-gate-enforce.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n95:   - { host: cursor, event: preToolUse, path: \".skilled/hooks/task-dispatch/cursor/task-dispatch-guard.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n96:   - { host: cursor, event: preToolUse, path: \".skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/hooks/git-preflight-advisory.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n97:   - { host: cursor, event: preToolUse, path: \".skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/hooks/git-message-gate.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n98:   - { host: cursor, event: postToolUse, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/cursor/post-tool-use.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n99:   - { host: cursor, event: beforeSubmitPrompt, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/cursor/spec-gate-classify.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n100:   - { host: cursor, event: beforeSubmitPrompt, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/cursor/user-prompt-submit.js\", type: file_exists }\n101:   - { host: cursor, event: beforeMCPExecution, path: \".skilled/hooks/mcp-route-guard/cursor/mcp-route-guard.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n102:   - { host: cursor, event: preCompact, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/cursor/precompact.js\", type: file_exists }\n103:   - { host: codex, event: SessionStart, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/codex/session-start.js\", type: file_exists }\n104:   - { host: codex, event: SessionStart, path: \".skilled/bin/worktree-guard.sh\", type: file_exists }\n105:   - { host: codex, event: SessionStart, path: \".skilled/bin/check-git-hooks.sh\", type: file_exists }\n106:   - { host: codex, event: SessionStart, path: \".skilled/bin/git-live-follow.sh\", type: file_exists }\n107:   - { host: codex, event: SessionStart, path: \".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-quality/scripts/check-dist-staleness.sh\", type: file_exists }\n108:   - { host: codex, event: UserPromptSubmit, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.js\", type: file_exists }\n109:   - { host: codex, event: UserPromptSubmit, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/codex/spec-gate-classify.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n110:   - { host: codex, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/hooks/dispatch/codex/dispatch-preflight-lint.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n111:   - { host: codex, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/hooks/git-preflight-advisory.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n112:   - { host: codex, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/hooks/git-message-gate.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n113:   - { host: codex, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/codex/spec-gate-enforce.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n114:   - { host: codex, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/hooks/mcp-route-guard/codex/mcp-route-guard.cjs\", type: file_exists }\n115:   - { host: codex, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/hooks/overlay-guard/codex/overlay-guard.cjs\", type: file_exists }\n116:   - { host: codex, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/hooks/env-secret-guard/command-hook/env-secret-guard.cjs\", type: file_exists }\n117:   - { host: codex, event: PostToolUse, path: \".skilled/hooks/env-secret-guard/command-hook/env-secret-guard-after.cjs\", type: file_exists }\n118:   - { host: codex, event: PostToolUse, path: \".skilled/hooks/post-edit-quality/codex/post-edit-quality.cjs\", type: file_exists }\n119:   - { host: codex, event: PostToolUse, path: \".skilled/hooks/dispatch/codex/dispatch-audit-posttooluse.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n120:   - { host: codex, event: Stop, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/codex/session-stop.js\", type: file_exists }\n121:   - { host: codex, event: Stop, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/codex/completion-evidence-stop.cjs\", type: file_exists }\n122:   - { host: codex, event: Stop, path: \".skilled/scripts/session-cleanup.sh\", type: file_exists }\n123:   - { host: codex, event: PreCompact, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/codex/compact-inject.js\", type: file_exists }\n124:   - { host: devin, event: SessionStart, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/devin/session-start.js\", type: file_exists }\n125:   - { host: devin, event: UserPromptSubmit, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/devin/user-prompt-submit.js\", type: file_exists }\n126:   - { host: devin, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/hooks/git-preflight-advisory.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n127:   - { host: devin, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/hooks/git-message-gate.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n128:   - { host: devin, event: SessionStart, path: \".skilled/hooks/goal/devin/goal-inject.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n129:   - { host: devin, event: UserPromptSubmit, path: \".skilled/hooks/goal/devin/goal-inject.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n130:   - { host: devin, event: Stop, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/devin/session-stop.js\", type: file_exists }\n131: \n132: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n133: # INPUTS\n134: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n135: inputs:\n136:   none: \"This diagnostic takes no arguments. Every checker derives its expected state from the canonical trees and the runtimes' own config files.\"\n137: \n138: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n139: # EXECUTION\n140: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n141: execution:\n142:   steps:\n143:     - \"Run upstream_assets.runtime_mirrors with --check. Covers the cursor/devin agent, command and skill symlink trees, all four hook discovery mirrors and the .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/ links into the hook library. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n144:     - \"Run upstream_assets.codex_agents with --check. Covers the generated .codex/agents/*.toml. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n145:     - \"Run upstream_assets.codex_prompts with --check. Covers the generated .codex/prompts/*.md stubs. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n146:     - \"Run upstream_assets.agent_roster. Covers roster coverage across all five surfaces and rejects a real file where a symlink belongs. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift, 2 = checker error (bad argument, canonical dir missing, or crash).\"\n147:     - \"Run upstream_assets.agent_body_parity with --all. Compares each agent body across the runtime trees; same-file mirrors and non-comparable formats are reported, not counted as matches. Exit 0 = all comparable mirrors in sync, 1 = drift or comparison failure, 2 = checker invocation error (unknown option), 3 = not checkable (frontmatter parser unavailable).\"\n148:     - \"Run upstream_assets.command_catalog. Compare command frontmatter with the root and family indexes and hub metadata. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift, 2 = checker error.\"\n149:     - \"Run upstream_assets.codex_hooks_installer with --check --allow-worktree. Covers the user-global ~/.codex/hooks.json against the repo's .codex/hooks.json, including orphaned entries whose .skilled adapter no longer exists on disk. Explicit OK output = in sync; a drift report = drift; refusal, error, or missing affirmative output = error.\"\n150:     - 'Run upstream_assets.codex_hook_approval with --root \"$PWD\". Covers the Codex approval that lets the project advisor hook run at all, since Codex skips an unapproved entry without a warning. PASS = in sync. WARN sets STATUS to WARN and shows the repair line it prints without counting as drift. SKIP leaves STATUS unchanged. Exit 0 = approved or no Codex hooks file, 1 = absent or unapproved, 2 = checker error.'\n151:     - \"Run upstream_assets.pi_agents with --check. Covers the generated .pi/agents/*.md. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n152:     - \"Run upstream_assets.pi_prompts with --check. Covers the generated .pi/prompts/*.md stubs. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n153:     - \"Run upstream_assets.dsh_skills, the command node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-skills-dsh.cjs --check. Covers the generated .dsh/skills/ links. When .dsh/ is absent, report the row as n/a (no .dsh/ tree) without running the check; an n/a row leaves STATUS unchanged, and this run never creates that directory. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n154:     - \"Run upstream_assets.dsh_prompts, the command node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-prompts-dsh.cjs --check. Covers the generated .dsh/prompts/*.md files. When .dsh/ is absent, report the row as n/a (no .dsh/ tree) without running the check; an n/a row leaves STATUS unchanged, and this run never creates that directory. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n155:     - \"Run upstream_assets.dsh_agents, the command node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-agents-dsh.cjs --check. Covers the generated .dsh/agents/*.patch.yml files. When .dsh/ is absent, report the row as n/a (no .dsh/ tree) without running the check; an n/a row leaves STATUS unchanged, and this run never creates that directory. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n156:     - \"For each row in hook_adapter_fallback_health_checks, run its file_exists check (a plain path-existence read, no execution of the adapter or the shell command that wraps it). Collect every row whose path does not resolve as a degraded hook adapter, keyed by host:event:path.\"\n157:     - \"Aggregate: report each surface with its own verdict rather than a single pass/fail, so the operator learns which mirror moved.\"\n158: \n159: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n160: # OUTPUT\n161: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n162: output: |\n163:   STATUS=OK when every checker reports in sync, or n/a for a DSH row while its runtime tree is absent, and the\n164:   Codex hook approval check reports in sync or skip.\n165:   STATUS=WARN when the Codex hook approval check reports an unapproved or absent advisor entry and no checker\n166:   reports drift: show its lines, including the repair line it prints, without adding a drift surface.\n167:   STATUS=DRIFT when any checker reports drift, listing each drifting surface and the repair command for it:\n168:     runtime mirrors  -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs\n169:     codex agents     -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/codex/sync-agents.cjs\n170:     codex prompts    -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/codex/sync-prompts.cjs\n171:     codex hooks      -> node .skilled/bin/install-codex-hooks.mjs\n172:     agent body parity (.skilled/bin/check-agent-mirror-sync.cjs) -> .claude/agents is a hand-maintained real-file mirror; update both its .skilled source and Claude twin, then run node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/codex/sync-agents.cjs for .codex/agents, node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/pi/sync-agents-pi.cjs for .pi/agents, and node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs for the .cursor and .devin links\n173:     pi agents        -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/pi/sync-agents-pi.cjs\n174:     pi prompts       -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/pi/sync-prompts-pi.cjs\n175:     dsh skills       -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-skills-dsh.cjs\n176:     dsh prompts      -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-prompts-dsh.cjs\n177:     dsh agents       -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-agents-dsh.cjs\n178:     command catalog  -> update the root and family indexes, group counts, and hub metadata from command frontmatter\n179:   While .dsh/ is absent the three DSH rows read n/a (no .dsh/ tree), never in sync, and leave\n180:   STATUS unchanged: the mirror does not exist yet, and this run never creates it. Their repair lines are the generators without --check, run once the tree exists.\n181:   The agent roster check has no generator. Its drift is repaired by the runtime-mirrors generator or by hand\n182:   for the authored surfaces (.skilled/agents and .claude/agents).\n183:   Hook CONFIG STRUCTURE is deliberately out of scope for mirroring: the four runtimes use incompatible event\n184:   vocabularies and entry shapes, so those files are hand-authored per runtime and cannot be mirror-checked\n185:   against each other.\n186:   Separately, \"N hook adapters degraded to fallback\" reports the count of hook_adapter_fallback_health_checks\n187:   rows whose path does not resolve, each listed as host:event:path. This is the same drift a live adapter\n188:   failure produces (its fallback JSON would carry \"mkHookDrift\": true and its stderr a matching\n189:   \"mk-hook-drift host=<host> event=<event> adapter=<name>\" line) surfaced without needing to fire the hook or\n190:   read raw JSON. Repair is adapter-specific: rebuild the runtime (npm --prefix\n191:   .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime run build) for a dist/hooks/* path, or restore/recreate the named\n192:   script for a .skilled/bin or .skilled/hooks path.\n193:   STATUS=ERROR when a checker refuses to run, returns an error, or omits an affirmative result.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml, lines 1-193\n1: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: # DOCTOR: RUNTIME MIRROR PARITY (READ-ONLY DIAGNOSTIC)\n3: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: role: Diagnostic Operator reporting whether every runtime config dir still mirrors its canonical source\n5: purpose: Detect drift across the agent, command, prompt and hook mirrors that .claude, .codex, .cursor, .devin, .pi and .dsh derive from .skilled, plus adapter-path resolution drift in the Claude, Codex, Cursor and Devin hook fallback chains\n6: action: Run every upstream-assets checker plus the hook-adapter fallback health checks -> aggregate their verdicts -> report per-surface drift\n7: skill_owner: \".skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/\"\n8: \n9: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n10: # OPERATING MODE\n11: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n12: operating_mode:\n13:   workflow: single-step\n14:   compliance: MANDATORY\n15:   execution: read_only\n16:   approvals: none\n17:   tracking: single_run\n18:   validation: read_only_assertion\n19: \n20: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n21: # MUTATION BOUNDARIES (READ-ONLY)\n22: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n23: mutation_boundaries:\n24:   read_only: true\n25:   allowed_targets: []\n26:   forbidden_targets:\n27:     - \"**/*\"\n28:   invariant: \"Every upstream_assets checker is invoked in its check-only form. This route MUST NOT run any generator in write mode, create or delete a symlink, or install a hook config. Repair is an explicit operator action, never a side effect of a diagnostic.\"\n29: \n30: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n31: # UPSTREAM ASSETS\n32: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n33: upstream_assets:\n34:   runtime_mirrors: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs\"\n35:   codex_agents: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/codex/sync-agents.cjs\"\n36:   codex_prompts: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/codex/sync-prompts.cjs\"\n37:   agent_roster: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agent-roster-mirror-check.cjs\"\n38:   agent_body_parity: \".skilled/bin/check-agent-mirror-sync.cjs\"\n39:   command_catalog: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/command-catalog-mirror-check.cjs\"\n40:   codex_hooks_installer: \".skilled/bin/install-codex-hooks.mjs\"\n41:   codex_hook_approval: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs\"\n42:   pi_agents: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/pi/sync-agents-pi.cjs\"\n43:   pi_prompts: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/pi/sync-prompts-pi.cjs\"\n44:   dsh_skills: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-skills-dsh.cjs\"\n45:   dsh_prompts: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-prompts-dsh.cjs\"\n46:   dsh_agents: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-agents-dsh.cjs\"\n47: \n48: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n49: # HOOK-ADAPTER FALLBACK HEALTH CHECKS\n50: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n51: # Every entry below is the primary adapter behind a `|| { <stderr>; <fallback JSON> }`\n52: # chain in .codex/hooks.json, .devin/hooks.v1.json, .claude/settings.json or\n53: # .cursor/hooks.json (the chains that carry the \"mkHookDrift\" marker). The one\n54: # exception is each fire-and-forget backgrounded reconcile command, which no\n55: # host reads stdout from and which deliberately runs without a fallback branch.\n56: # A missing path here is exactly the state a synthetic\n57: # adapter failure produces (e.g. temporarily renaming the compiled file), so a\n58: # `file_exists` failure on any row below is reported as a degraded hook adapter,\n59: # not a mirror-structure drift.\n60: hook_adapter_fallback_health_checks:\n61:   - { host: claude, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/hooks/dispatch/claude/dispatch-preflight-lint.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n62:   - { host: claude, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/claude/spec-gate-enforce.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n63:   - { host: claude, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/hooks/git-preflight-advisory.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n64:   - { host: claude, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/hooks/git-message-gate.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n65:   - { host: claude, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/hooks/task-dispatch/claude/task-dispatch-guard.cjs\", type: file_exists }\n66:   - { host: claude, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/hooks/task-dispatch/claude/fable-subagent-guard.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n67:   - { host: claude, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/hooks/mcp-route-guard/claude/mcp-route-guard.cjs\", type: file_exists }\n68:   - { host: claude, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/hooks/overlay-guard/claude/overlay-guard.cjs\", type: file_exists }\n69:   - { host: claude, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/hooks/env-secret-guard/command-hook/env-secret-guard.cjs\", type: file_exists }\n70:   - { host: claude, event: PostToolUse, path: \".skilled/hooks/env-secret-guard/command-hook/env-secret-guard-after.cjs\", type: file_exists }\n71:   - { host: claude, event: UserPromptSubmit, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js\", type: file_exists }\n72:   - { host: claude, event: UserPromptSubmit, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/claude/spec-gate-classify.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n73:   - { host: claude, event: SessionStart, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/session-prime.js\", type: file_exists }\n74:   - { host: claude, event: SessionStart, path: \".skilled/bin/worktree-guard.sh\", type: file_exists }\n75:   - { host: claude, event: SessionStart, path: \".skilled/bin/check-git-hooks.sh\", type: file_exists }\n76:   - { host: claude, event: SessionStart, path: \".skilled/bin/git-live-follow.sh\", type: file_exists }\n77:   - { host: claude, event: SessionStart, path: \".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-quality/scripts/check-dist-staleness.sh\", type: file_exists }\n78:   - { host: claude, event: SessionStart, path: \".skilled/bin/install-codex-hooks.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n79:   - { host: claude, event: Stop, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/session-stop.js\", type: file_exists }\n80:   - { host: claude, event: Stop, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/claude/completion-evidence-stop.cjs\", type: file_exists }\n81:   - { host: claude, event: SessionEnd, path: \".skilled/scripts/session-cleanup.sh\", type: file_exists }\n82:   - { host: claude, event: PostToolUse, path: \".skilled/hooks/post-edit-quality/claude/claude-posttooluse.cjs\", type: file_exists }\n83:   - { host: claude, event: PostToolUse, path: \".skilled/hooks/dispatch/claude/dispatch-audit-posttooluse.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n84:   - { host: claude, event: PreCompact, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/compact-inject.js\", type: file_exists }\n85:   - { host: cursor, event: sessionStart, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/cursor/session-start.js\", type: file_exists }\n86:   - { host: cursor, event: sessionStart, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/cursor/spec-gate-prebind.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n87:   - { host: cursor, event: sessionStart, path: \".skilled/bin/worktree-guard.sh\", type: file_exists }\n88:   - { host: cursor, event: sessionStart, path: \".skilled/bin/check-git-hooks.sh\", type: file_exists }\n89:   - { host: cursor, event: sessionStart, path: \".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-quality/scripts/check-dist-staleness.sh\", type: file_exists }\n90:   - { host: cursor, event: sessionStart, path: \".skilled/bin/install-codex-hooks.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n91:   - { host: cursor, event: sessionStart, path: \".skilled/hooks/goal/cursor/goal-inject.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n92:   - { host: cursor, event: sessionEnd, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/cursor/session-end.js\", type: file_exists }\n93:   - { host: cursor, event: sessionEnd, path: \".skilled/scripts/session-cleanup.sh\", type: file_exists }\n94:   - { host: cursor, event: preToolUse, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/cursor/spec-gate-enforce.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n95:   - { host: cursor, event: preToolUse, path: \".skilled/hooks/task-dispatch/cursor/task-dispatch-guard.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n96:   - { host: cursor, event: preToolUse, path: \".skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/hooks/git-preflight-advisory.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n97:   - { host: cursor, event: preToolUse, path: \".skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/hooks/git-message-gate.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n98:   - { host: cursor, event: postToolUse, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/cursor/post-tool-use.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n99:   - { host: cursor, event: beforeSubmitPrompt, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/cursor/spec-gate-classify.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n100:   - { host: cursor, event: beforeSubmitPrompt, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/cursor/user-prompt-submit.js\", type: file_exists }\n101:   - { host: cursor, event: beforeMCPExecution, path: \".skilled/hooks/mcp-route-guard/cursor/mcp-route-guard.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n102:   - { host: cursor, event: preCompact, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/cursor/precompact.js\", type: file_exists }\n103:   - { host: codex, event: SessionStart, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/codex/session-start.js\", type: file_exists }\n104:   - { host: codex, event: SessionStart, path: \".skilled/bin/worktree-guard.sh\", type: file_exists }\n105:   - { host: codex, event: SessionStart, path: \".skilled/bin/check-git-hooks.sh\", type: file_exists }\n106:   - { host: codex, event: SessionStart, path: \".skilled/bin/git-live-follow.sh\", type: file_exists }\n107:   - { host: codex, event: SessionStart, path: \".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-quality/scripts/check-dist-staleness.sh\", type: file_exists }\n108:   - { host: codex, event: UserPromptSubmit, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.js\", type: file_exists }\n109:   - { host: codex, event: UserPromptSubmit, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/codex/spec-gate-classify.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n110:   - { host: codex, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/hooks/dispatch/codex/dispatch-preflight-lint.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n111:   - { host: codex, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/hooks/git-preflight-advisory.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n112:   - { host: codex, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/hooks/git-message-gate.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n113:   - { host: codex, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/codex/spec-gate-enforce.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n114:   - { host: codex, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/hooks/mcp-route-guard/codex/mcp-route-guard.cjs\", type: file_exists }\n115:   - { host: codex, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/hooks/overlay-guard/codex/overlay-guard.cjs\", type: file_exists }\n116:   - { host: codex, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/hooks/env-secret-guard/command-hook/env-secret-guard.cjs\", type: file_exists }\n117:   - { host: codex, event: PostToolUse, path: \".skilled/hooks/env-secret-guard/command-hook/env-secret-guard-after.cjs\", type: file_exists }\n118:   - { host: codex, event: PostToolUse, path: \".skilled/hooks/post-edit-quality/codex/post-edit-quality.cjs\", type: file_exists }\n119:   - { host: codex, event: PostToolUse, path: \".skilled/hooks/dispatch/codex/dispatch-audit-posttooluse.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n120:   - { host: codex, event: Stop, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/codex/session-stop.js\", type: file_exists }\n121:   - { host: codex, event: Stop, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/codex/completion-evidence-stop.cjs\", type: file_exists }\n122:   - { host: codex, event: Stop, path: \".skilled/scripts/session-cleanup.sh\", type: file_exists }\n123:   - { host: codex, event: PreCompact, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/codex/compact-inject.js\", type: file_exists }\n124:   - { host: devin, event: SessionStart, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/devin/session-start.js\", type: file_exists }\n125:   - { host: devin, event: UserPromptSubmit, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/devin/user-prompt-submit.js\", type: file_exists }\n126:   - { host: devin, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/hooks/git-preflight-advisory.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n127:   - { host: devin, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/hooks/git-message-gate.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n128:   - { host: devin, event: SessionStart, path: \".skilled/hooks/goal/devin/goal-inject.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n129:   - { host: devin, event: UserPromptSubmit, path: \".skilled/hooks/goal/devin/goal-inject.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n130:   - { host: devin, event: Stop, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/devin/session-stop.js\", type: file_exists }\n131: \n132: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n133: # INPUTS\n134: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n135: inputs:\n136:   none: \"This diagnostic takes no arguments. Every checker derives its expected state from the canonical trees and the runtimes' own config files.\"\n137: \n138: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n139: # EXECUTION\n140: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n141: execution:\n142:   steps:\n143:     - \"Run upstream_assets.runtime_mirrors with --check. Covers the cursor/devin agent, command and skill symlink trees, all four hook discovery mirrors and the .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/ links into the hook library. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n144:     - \"Run upstream_assets.codex_agents with --check. Covers the generated .codex/agents/*.toml. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n145:     - \"Run upstream_assets.codex_prompts with --check. Covers the generated .codex/prompts/*.md stubs. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n146:     - \"Run upstream_assets.agent_roster. Covers roster coverage across all five surfaces and rejects a real file where a symlink belongs. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift, 2 = checker error (bad argument, canonical dir missing, or crash).\"\n147:     - \"Run upstream_assets.agent_body_parity with --all. Compares each agent body across the runtime trees; same-file mirrors and non-comparable formats are reported, not counted as matches. Exit 0 = all comparable mirrors in sync, 1 = drift or comparison failure, 2 = checker invocation error (unknown option), 3 = not checkable (frontmatter parser unavailable).\"\n148:     - \"Run upstream_assets.command_catalog. Compare command frontmatter with the root and family indexes and hub metadata. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift, 2 = checker error.\"\n149:     - \"Run upstream_assets.codex_hooks_installer with --check --allow-worktree. Covers the user-global ~/.codex/hooks.json against the repo's .codex/hooks.json, including orphaned entries whose .skilled adapter no longer exists on disk. Explicit OK output = in sync; a drift report = drift; refusal, error, or missing affirmative output = error.\"\n150:     - 'Run upstream_assets.codex_hook_approval with --root \"$PWD\". Covers the Codex approval that lets the project advisor hook run at all, since Codex skips an unapproved entry without a warning. PASS = in sync. WARN sets STATUS to WARN and shows the repair line it prints without counting as drift. SKIP leaves STATUS unchanged. Exit 0 = approved or no Codex hooks file, 1 = absent or unapproved, 2 = checker error.'\n151:     - \"Run upstream_assets.pi_agents with --check. Covers the generated .pi/agents/*.md. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n152:     - \"Run upstream_assets.pi_prompts with --check. Covers the generated .pi/prompts/*.md stubs. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n153:     - \"Run upstream_assets.dsh_skills, the command node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-skills-dsh.cjs --check. Covers the generated .dsh/skills/ links. When .dsh/ is absent, report the row as n/a (no .dsh/ tree) without running the check; an n/a row leaves STATUS unchanged, and this run never creates that directory. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n154:     - \"Run upstream_assets.dsh_prompts, the command node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-prompts-dsh.cjs --check. Covers the generated .dsh/prompts/*.md files. When .dsh/ is absent, report the row as n/a (no .dsh/ tree) without running the check; an n/a row leaves STATUS unchanged, and this run never creates that directory. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n155:     - \"Run upstream_assets.dsh_agents, the command node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-agents-dsh.cjs --check. Covers the generated .dsh/agents/*.patch.yml files. When .dsh/ is absent, report the row as n/a (no .dsh/ tree) without running the check; an n/a row leaves STATUS unchanged, and this run never creates that directory. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n156:     - \"For each row in hook_adapter_fallback_health_checks, run its file_exists check (a plain path-existence read, no execution of the adapter or the shell command that wraps it). Collect every row whose path does not resolve as a degraded hook adapter, keyed by host:event:path.\"\n157:     - \"Aggregate: report each surface with its own verdict rather than a single pass/fail, so the operator learns which mirror moved.\"\n158: \n159: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n160: # OUTPUT\n161: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n162: output: |\n163:   STATUS=OK when every checker reports in sync, or n/a for a DSH row while its runtime tree is absent, and the\n164:   Codex hook approval check reports in sync or skip.\n165:   STATUS=WARN when the Codex hook approval check reports an unapproved or absent advisor entry and no checker\n166:   reports drift: show its lines, including the repair line it prints, without adding a drift surface.\n167:   STATUS=DRIFT when any checker reports drift, listing each drifting surface and the repair command for it:\n168:     runtime mirrors  -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs\n169:     codex agents     -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/codex/sync-agents.cjs\n170:     codex prompts    -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/codex/sync-prompts.cjs\n171:     codex hooks      -> node .skilled/bin/install-codex-hooks.mjs\n172:     agent body parity (.skilled/bin/check-agent-mirror-sync.cjs) -> .claude/agents is a hand-maintained real-file mirror; update both its .skilled source and Claude twin, then run node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/codex/sync-agents.cjs for .codex/agents, node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/pi/sync-agents-pi.cjs for .pi/agents, and node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs for the .cursor and .devin links\n173:     pi agents        -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/pi/sync-agents-pi.cjs\n174:     pi prompts       -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/pi/sync-prompts-pi.cjs\n175:     dsh skills       -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-skills-dsh.cjs\n176:     dsh prompts      -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-prompts-dsh.cjs\n177:     dsh agents       -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-agents-dsh.cjs\n178:     command catalog  -> update the root and family indexes, group counts, and hub metadata from command frontmatter\n179:   While .dsh/ is absent the three DSH rows read n/a (no .dsh/ tree), never in sync, and leave\n180:   STATUS unchanged: the mirror does not exist yet, and this run never creates it. Their repair lines are the generators without --check, run once the tree exists.\n181:   The agent roster check has no generator. Its drift is repaired by the runtime-mirrors generator or by hand\n182:   for the authored surfaces (.skilled/agents and .claude/agents).\n183:   Hook CONFIG STRUCTURE is deliberately out of scope for mirroring: the four runtimes use incompatible event\n184:   vocabularies and entry shapes, so those files are hand-authored per runtime and cannot be mirror-checked\n185:   against each other.\n186:   Separately, \"N hook adapters degraded to fallback\" reports the count of hook_adapter_fallback_health_checks\n187:   rows whose path does not resolve, each listed as host:event:path. This is the same drift a live adapter\n188:   failure produces (its fallback JSON would carry \"mkHookDrift\": true and its stderr a matching\n189:   \"mk-hook-drift host=<host> event=<event> adapter=<name>\" line) surfaced without needing to fire the hook or\n190:   read raw JSON. Repair is adapter-specific: rebuild the runtime (npm --prefix\n191:   .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime run build) for a dist/hooks/* path, or restore/recreate the named\n192:   script for a .skilled/bin or .skilled/hooks path.\n193:   STATUS=ERROR when a checker refuses to run, returns an error, or omits an affirmative result."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml\"}"},"time":{"start":1794550751344,"end":1794550751479}}}}
