{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794550775118,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799ae9ffehgaY2UX9uAVWD2","part":{"partID":"prt_1d38fb9690022j2ZCXrxtmT0zK","sessionID":"ses_e2c799ae9ffehgaY2UX9uAVWD2","messageID":"msg_1d38fabef001Md1Pm6A0HjnnTx","type":"tool","id":"call_00_QVHzLNh0O9SGz5JWYhtm1853","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff -U2 35c3188681..320e7b64d4 -- .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt .skilled/commands/doctor/agents-md.md .skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md .skilled/commands/doctor/skill-advisor.md .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown | head -220"},"output":"diff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/agents-md.md b/.skilled/commands/doctor/agents-md.md\nindex 3b98198fa7..094a7943c7 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/agents-md.md\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/agents-md.md\n@@ -58,5 +58,5 @@ Load the presentation contract before showing the menu, a plan, a digest, a resu\n | `--plan-digest <digest>` | `embed` | The digest the plan printed; the apply refuses any bytes it does not match |\n | `--keep-claude-md` | `embed` | Fold a divergent `CLAUDE.md` into the block and keep the file |\n-| `--remove-claude-md` | `embed` | Fold it and remove it, which is the default |\n+| `--remove-claude-md` | `embed` | Fold it and leave a one-line @AGENTS.md pointer in its place, which is the default |\n | `--create-router` | `embed` | Create `REPO RULES.md` from the shipped rows when it is missing |\n | `--run <dir>` | `restore` | The backup directory one apply printed, whose `manifest.json` records what to put back |\ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt\nindex aebf32bd34..0d6e07592e 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt\n@@ -120,5 +120,8 @@ The class column is the manifest's `mutating` value for the route that owns the\n    Why: checks the git hooks and sk-git settings, and names the repair for each one that is off. Run it from the target repo.\n \n-5) /doctor:setup   [class]\n+5) /doctor:skill-advisor embedder   [class]\n+   Why: sets up meaning matching for commands. It shows the cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server. Run it from the target repo.\n+\n+6) /doctor:setup   [class]\n    Why: confirms the result. Run it from the target repo.\n ```\ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml\nindex 03e9a16a9e..10edf61376 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml\n@@ -58,5 +58,5 @@ execution:\n     - \"Ask: When --root or --runtimes is missing, ask once for the target repo's absolute path, runtimes (claude, opencode, codex, cursor, devin, pi, or the ones already there), link shape (auto, whole or merge) and instruction file (embed or link). Stop for the answers.\"\n     - \"Inspect: Run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs check --root <dir> [--runtimes <list>] [--link-instructions] once in place. Use only the check subcommand; include --link-instructions only when the operator chose link. Render the engine's entry lines through the presentation contract.\"\n-    - \"Checklist: Print these ordered writing steps through the presentation contract and stop; never run them. For each command, copy its mutation class verbatim from _routes.yaml and print one line explaining why: 1) /doctor:symlink link --root <dir> --runtimes <list> --mode <shape>, with --link-instructions only when link was chosen; it shows a plan and asks before writing. 2) /doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>, only when embed was chosen. 3) /doctor:mcp install, from the Skilled checkout, to build and register Code Mode. 4) /doctor:git setup, from inside the target repo. 5) /doctor:setup, from inside the target repo, to confirm the result. Pass only values the operator gave.\"\n+    - \"Checklist: Print these ordered writing steps through the presentation contract and stop; never run them. For each command, copy its mutation class verbatim from _routes.yaml and print one line explaining why: 1) /doctor:symlink link --root <dir> --runtimes <list> --mode <shape>, with --link-instructions only when link was chosen; it shows a plan and asks before writing. 2) /doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>, only when embed was chosen. 3) /doctor:mcp install, from the Skilled checkout, to build and register Code Mode. 4) /doctor:git setup, from inside the target repo. 5) /doctor:skill-advisor embedder, from inside the target repo, to set up meaning matching for commands. It shows its cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server, and a no leaves a phrase-only install. 6) /doctor:setup, from inside the target repo, to confirm the result. Pass only values the operator gave.\"\n     - \"Warn: Print this fixed caveat: Context saves land in the target repo's own specs/ when they run from inside it. Run /doctor:setup and later saves from inside the target repo, not from the Skilled checkout.\"\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml\nindex b409cb4761..f2d47538c5 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml\n@@ -39,4 +39,5 @@ upstream_assets:\n   command_catalog: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/command-catalog-mirror-check.cjs\"\n   codex_hooks_installer: \".skilled/bin/install-codex-hooks.mjs\"\n+  codex_hook_approval: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs\"\n   pi_agents: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/pi/sync-agents-pi.cjs\"\n   pi_prompts: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/pi/sync-prompts-pi.cjs\"\n@@ -147,4 +148,5 @@ execution:\n     - \"Run upstream_assets.command_catalog. Compare command frontmatter with the root and family indexes and hub metadata. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift, 2 = checker error.\"\n     - \"Run upstream_assets.codex_hooks_installer with --check --allow-worktree. Covers the user-global ~/.codex/hooks.json against the repo's .codex/hooks.json, including orphaned entries whose .skilled adapter no longer exists on disk. Explicit OK output = in sync; a drift report = drift; refusal, error, or missing affirmative output = error.\"\n+    - 'Run upstream_assets.codex_hook_approval with --root \"$PWD\". Covers the Codex approval that lets the project advisor hook run at all, since Codex skips an unapproved entry without a warning. PASS = in sync. WARN sets STATUS to WARN and shows the repair line it prints without counting as drift. SKIP leaves STATUS unchanged. Exit 0 = approved or no Codex hooks file, 1 = absent or unapproved, 2 = checker error.'\n     - \"Run upstream_assets.pi_agents with --check. Covers the generated .pi/agents/*.md. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n     - \"Run upstream_assets.pi_prompts with --check. Covers the generated .pi/prompts/*.md stubs. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n@@ -159,5 +161,8 @@ execution:\n # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n output: |\n-  STATUS=OK when every checker reports in sync, or n/a for a DSH row while its runtime tree is absent.\n+  STATUS=OK when every checker reports in sync, or n/a for a DSH row while its runtime tree is absent, and the\n+  Codex hook approval check reports in sync or skip.\n+  STATUS=WARN when the Codex hook approval check reports an unapproved or absent advisor entry and no checker\n+  reports drift: show its lines, including the repair line it prints, without adding a drift surface.\n   STATUS=DRIFT when any checker reports drift, listing each drifting surface and the repair command for it:\n     runtime mirrors  -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs\ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt\nindex 4072736def..257b64487b 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt\n@@ -17,5 +17,5 @@ Render this table first, before any leg runs.\n | Command | What it checks |\n |---------|----------------|\n-| `/doctor:setup` | This overview: the doctor target list and the five read-only setup legs |\n+| `/doctor:setup` | This overview: the doctor target list and the seven read-only setup legs |\n | `/doctor:helper [<problem in plain words>] [--json]` | Rank the doctor commands that fit a described problem, with the class and the reason on every line |\n | `/doctor:env list` | The documented environment switches and where each value comes from |\n@@ -38,4 +38,5 @@ Render this table first, before any leg runs.\n | `/doctor:skill-advisor skill-graph-freshness` | Drift between the compiled, SQLite and on-disk skill graph |\n | `/doctor:skill-advisor router-reach` | Whether each declared routing phrase reaches its hub |\n+| `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` | Meaning matching for commands: whether the local embedder answers, what it costs, and the plan that pulls the model and starts the server after a yes |\n | `/doctor:deep-loop` | Deep-loop coverage graphs and convergence for research, review and council runs |\n | `/doctor:mcp` | Code Mode install and debug, its UTCP configuration and runtime registration |\n@@ -59,4 +60,6 @@ Render one row per leg, in the workflow's order.\n | runtime-mirrors | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` |\n | advisor | Stale build: `npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build`. Other FAIL or DEGRADED results: `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`. |\n+| embedder | `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` |\n+| delivery | Missing hook: /doctor:runtime-mirrors, or /doctor:symlink check in a linked project. Unapproved Codex hook: the repair line the check prints, which opens /hooks in a Codex session |\n \n ## 4. Result Templates\n@@ -103,4 +106,5 @@ STATUS=ERROR ERROR=\"[message]\"\n | The sk-git leg reports DEGRADED | No sk-git check failed, but one is unknown or a gate is saved off. Run `/doctor:git setup` to see which. On a runtime the battery cannot name, the AI-tool check stays unknown |\n | The trigger-index leg reports stale documents | Run `/doctor:speckit` to see which documents are stale |\n+| The delivery leg reports DEGRADED | A runtime cannot receive the advisor brief. Run the repair the leg names, then rerun /doctor:setup. The install still works without it |\n | Route manifest parse error | Run `bash .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh` |\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml\nindex dfcce9c832..23d5e54930 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml\n@@ -3,6 +3,6 @@\n # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n role: Diagnostic Operator giving a first-run overview of every doctor command and running the existing read-only setup checks once\n-purpose: List every doctor target with what it checks, run five read-only legs, and name the runnable doctor command that repairs each failing leg\n-action: Print the doctor target list -> run the five read-only legs once -> render the per-leg verdict and repair lines through the presentation contract\n+purpose: List every doctor target with what it checks, run seven read-only legs, and name the runnable doctor command that repairs each failing leg\n+action: Print the doctor target list -> run the seven read-only legs once -> render the per-leg verdict and repair lines through the presentation contract\n skill_owner: \".skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/\"\n \n@@ -38,4 +38,6 @@ upstream_assets:\n   runtime_mirror_check: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs\"\n   hop_history: \".skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/bin/session-relaunch.cjs\"\n+  hook_wiring_check: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\"\n+  codex_approval_check: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs\"\n \n # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n@@ -55,5 +57,7 @@ execution:\n     - \"Leg trigger-index: run node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/generate-trigger-index.mjs --check --json. Exit 0 passes. Exit 1 (stale documents) or 2 and higher (unreadable index) fails, with repair /doctor:speckit.\"\n     - \"Leg runtime-mirrors: run node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check. Exit 0 passes. Any other exit fails, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors.\"\n-    - \"Leg advisor: run node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --format json --timeout-ms 500 --warm-only. Exit 0 with data.freshness set to live is PASS. Exit 0 with any other freshness is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor rebuild. Exit 75 with a staleDistWarning field in stderr JSON is FAIL, with repair npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build. Exit 75 without that field is SKIP because the daemon is not running. Any other exit is FAIL, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor rebuild.\"\n+    - \"Leg advisor: run node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --format json --timeout-ms 500 --warm-only. Exit 0 with data.freshness set to live is PASS. Exit 0 with any other freshness is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor rebuild. Exit 75 with a staleDistWarning field in stderr JSON is FAIL, with repair npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build. Exit 75 without that field is SKIP because the daemon is not running. Any other exit is FAIL, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor rebuild. When data.hookHealth is present, show hook p95 <rollingP95Ms> ms over <invocations> prompts and fail-open <rollingFailOpenRate as a percent> under the leg. It never changes the leg's status.\"\n+    - \"Leg embedder: run node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --include-semantic-health true --format json --timeout-ms 1500 --warm-only. Exit 75 is SKIP, as for the advisor leg, because the daemon is not running. Exit 0 with data.semanticLaneHealth.laneEnabled true and data.semanticLaneHealth.commandVectorCoverage.embedded above 0 is PASS. Any other result is DEGRADED, never FAIL, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor embedder.\"\n+    - \"Leg delivery: run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\" and node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\", and show each line they print under the leg. Both exit 0 is PASS. A hook-missing line is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors in a Skilled checkout or /doctor:symlink check in a linked project. WARN codex-hooks-unapproved is DEGRADED, with the repair line the check printed. WARN codex-advisor-hook-absent is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors. Exit 2 from either check is ERROR. This leg is never FAIL, because a hook that is not wired or not approved stops the brief, not the install.\"\n     - \"Last session hop (informational, not a leg): run node .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/bin/session-relaunch.cjs history --last 1 and show its first output line under the result as the last session hop, plus its open notes line when it prints one. Its exit and output never change the status.\"\n     - \"Claude context window (informational, not a leg): run node .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/bin/session-relaunch.cjs window and show its line. Its exit and output never change the status.\"\ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown b/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown\nindex 0015c63c13..a64b7e6748 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown\n@@ -40,4 +40,5 @@ The scripts validate route manifests, inspect MCP installations, audit parent sk\n +-- ci-scaffold.cjs\n +-- ci-toggle.cjs\n++-- codex-hook-approval-check.cjs\n +-- doctor-helper-match.cjs\n +-- doctor-phrase-reach.cjs\n@@ -45,4 +46,5 @@ The scripts validate route manifests, inspect MCP installations, audit parent sk\n +-- git-setup-check.cjs\n +-- git-standards.cjs\n++-- hook-wiring-check.cjs\n +-- mcp-doctor-lib.sh\n +-- mcp-doctor.sh\n@@ -107,4 +109,6 @@ The scripts validate route manifests, inspect MCP installations, audit parent sk\n | `doctor-helper-match.cjs` | Ranks the doctor commands of `_routes.yaml` against a problem stated in plain words for `/doctor:helper`: one entry per route, standalone command, standalone action and mcp sub-action, scored by inverse-document-frequency overlap over the manifest phrases plus a bonus for a fully covered phrase, with a preference for the mutation class the operator asked for. Each candidate carries the manifest phrase that best matched and the terms it matched, so the reason on every line is evidence. It skips its own route and every private name, reads one YAML file and writes nothing. It exits 0 on a match, 1 on no candidate above the floor and 2 on a bad argument, an unreadable manifest or a missing YAML parser. |\n | `doctor-phrase-reach.cjs` | Scores every activated doctor phrase and each runnable doctor command through the built advisor scorer, then keeps the three results the hooks show. It fails when a phrase reaches neither the top pick nor the second line. It also fails if a runnable command does not rank first or an activated phrase has fewer than three words. It exits 2 when the advisor build is missing or stale. |\n+| `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` | The read-only Codex approval check: it finds the advisor's `UserPromptSubmit` entry in `.codex/hooks.json` and reports whether the Codex config holds a `trusted_hash` for that exact group and index, because Codex skips an unapproved entry without a warning. `--root <dir>` reads another checkout, `--config <path>` reads another config and `--json` prints one object. It prints `SKIP no-codex-hooks`, `PASS codex-hooks-approved`, `WARN codex-advisor-hook-absent` or `WARN codex-hooks-unapproved <root>` with the `/hooks` repair line, and never prints a hash. It exits 0 on a skip or an approval, 1 on a missing or unapproved entry and 2 on a bad argument. |\n+| `hook-wiring-check.cjs` | The read-only hook-wiring check: it reads `.claude/settings.json`, `.codex/hooks.json`, `.cursor/hooks.json` and `.devin/hooks.v1.json`, and reports whether the prompt hook entry is present for each runtime folder it finds. `--root <dir>` is required and `--json` prints one object. It prints `ok <runtime>` or `hook-missing <runtime> <file>`, skips a runtime whose folder is absent and never writes. It exits 0 when every installed runtime is wired, 1 when one is missing and 2 on a bad argument or a missing root. |\n | `opencode-version-battery.cjs` | Checks this repository's OpenCode plugins on OpenCode 1 and 2. On 1 it proves plugin discovery through `debug config` and plugin load through an import check. On 2 it starts and stops a private server with the v2 binary it selected (`$OPENCODE_BIN`, `opencode` or `opencode2`, whichever reports a v2 version) and reads plugin and skill state from it. It exits 0 when every requested leg passes, 1 on a failed leg, 2 on a usage error, a crash or an `--out` file it cannot write and 3 when a leg is degraded or skipped. |\n | `ci-report.cjs` | The `/doctor:ci report` entry, kept thin: the flags, the exit codes and every name `/doctor:ci toggle` reads live here, and the readings live in the `ci-report` modules under `lib/`. It reads every workflow under `.github/workflows/` and reports its switch state, triggers, path filters and drift flags for `/doctor:ci report`. A switch is any variable a job's `if:` compares against `off`, so the workflow file is its only copy, and a repository variable value is reduced to a state and never printed. The branch, the required switch, the exempt files, the README and the rebuild trailer come from the CI profile, and the JSON names the profile it read. It exits 0 on a printed report, 1 when a workflow fails to parse, 2 on a bad argument and 3 when the CI profile is missing or invalid. |\n@@ -228,4 +232,6 @@ On this repository all legs pass on OpenCode 1.19.3 and 2.0.32. OpenCode 1.19.3\n | `agents-md-embed.cjs` | `plan` is read-only. `apply` writes only the paths in its own allowlist, all of them under the target root, after backing each one up under `.skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<digest>/` (or the OS temp folder when that path is not ignored), and restores from that backup itself when its post-write proof fails. `restore` writes only the paths the run's `manifest.json` records and keeps the backup folder. It never runs `git add`, `git commit` or `git stash`. |\n | `agents-md-manifest.cjs` | `--check` is read-only. `--write` rewrites the manifest's `derived` key and refuses to run outside the repository that ships the template. |\n+| `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` | Read-only over any root. It reads `.codex/hooks.json` and the Codex config, prints no hash and takes no write path. It exits 0 on a skip or an approval, 1 on a missing or unapproved entry and 2 on a bad argument. |\n+| `hook-wiring-check.cjs` | Read-only over any root. It writes no file and runs no installer, and its JSON form reports the same readings as its lines. It exits 0 when every installed runtime carries its entry, 1 when one is missing and 2 on a bad argument or a missing root. |\n | `opencode-version-battery.cjs` | The battery itself writes only the `--out` file and temporary folders it removes when each step ends. The private server's folder is also removed on `SIGINT` and `SIGTERM`, and the server is stopped. The import check runs each plugin's v1 factory in a child process rooted at the repository, so anything a plugin does when it loads happens during the check. It never touches the shared v2 service and never prints the private server's password. OpenCode 1 writes into a temporary data folder, not the user's. |\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md b/.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md\nindex 83784647f5..17b68fd61e 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md\n@@ -60,5 +60,6 @@ The argument failure wording, the doctor target list, the per-leg result table,\n \n The workflow prints the doctor target list.\n-It then runs five read-only legs once: the sk-code setup battery, the sk-git setup battery, the trigger index freshness check, the runtime mirror check and the advisor status probe with `--warm-only`.\n+It then runs seven read-only legs once: the sk-code setup battery, the sk-git setup battery, the trigger index freshness check, the runtime mirror check, the advisor status probe with `--warm-only` and the embedder check, which reads the semantic lane and the command vectors, and the delivery check, which reads whether each runtime's prompt hook is wired and whether Codex has approved it.\n+The delivery leg reports DEGRADED, never FAIL, when a prompt hook is missing or the Codex hook is unapproved, and names the repair.\n It reports each leg as passing, skipped, degraded or failing.\n For a failing leg, it names the runnable doctor command that repairs it.\ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/skill-advisor.md b/.skilled/commands/doctor/skill-advisor.md\nindex 86bd89e0d3..a3d73cf751 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/skill-advisor.md\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/skill-advisor.md\n@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@\n ---\n description: \"Tune and rebuild the skill advisor, and audit graph freshness, router reach, budgets and parent hubs.\"\n-argument-hint: \"<tune|rebuild|skill-graph-freshness|router-reach|skill-budget|parent-skill> [flags] | list | ?\"\n+argument-hint: \"<tune|rebuild|skill-graph-freshness|router-reach|embedder|skill-budget|parent-skill> [flags] | list | ?\"\n allowed-tools: Read, Bash, Grep, Glob, Edit, Write\n ---\n@@ -59,4 +59,5 @@ These existing YAML assets are referenced only. The router must not modify them.\n | `skill-graph-freshness` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-graph-freshness.yaml` |\n | `router-reach` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-router-reach.yaml` |\n+| `embedder` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml` |\n | `skill-budget` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-budget.yaml` |\n | `parent-skill` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-parent-skill.yaml` |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"diff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/agents-md.md b/.skilled/commands/doctor/agents-md.md\nindex 3b98198fa7..094a7943c7 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/agents-md.md\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/agents-md.md\n@@ -58,5 +58,5 @@ Load the presentation contract before showing the menu, a plan, a digest, a resu\n | `--plan-digest <digest>` | `embed` | The digest the plan printed; the apply refuses any bytes it does not match |\n | `--keep-claude-md` | `embed` | Fold a divergent `CLAUDE.md` into the block and keep the file |\n-| `--remove-claude-md` | `embed` | Fold it and remove it, which is the default |\n+| `--remove-claude-md` | `embed` | Fold it and leave a one-line @AGENTS.md pointer in its place, which is the default |\n | `--create-router` | `embed` | Create `REPO RULES.md` from the shipped rows when it is missing |\n | `--run <dir>` | `restore` | The backup directory one apply printed, whose `manifest.json` records what to put back |\ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt\nindex aebf32bd34..0d6e07592e 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt\n@@ -120,5 +120,8 @@ The class column is the manifest's `mutating` value for the route that owns the\n    Why: checks the git hooks and sk-git settings, and names the repair for each one that is off. Run it from the target repo.\n \n-5) /doctor:setup   [class]\n+5) /doctor:skill-advisor embedder   [class]\n+   Why: sets up meaning matching for commands. It shows the cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server. Run it from the target repo.\n+\n+6) /doctor:setup   [class]\n    Why: confirms the result. Run it from the target repo.\n ```\ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml\nindex 03e9a16a9e..10edf61376 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml\n@@ -58,5 +58,5 @@ execution:\n     - \"Ask: When --root or --runtimes is missing, ask once for the target repo's absolute path, runtimes (claude, opencode, codex, cursor, devin, pi, or the ones already there), link shape (auto, whole or merge) and instruction file (embed or link). Stop for the answers.\"\n     - \"Inspect: Run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs check --root <dir> [--runtimes <list>] [--link-instructions] once in place. Use only the check subcommand; include --link-instructions only when the operator chose link. Render the engine's entry lines through the presentation contract.\"\n-    - \"Checklist: Print these ordered writing steps through the presentation contract and stop; never run them. For each command, copy its mutation class verbatim from _routes.yaml and print one line explaining why: 1) /doctor:symlink link --root <dir> --runtimes <list> --mode <shape>, with --link-instructions only when link was chosen; it shows a plan and asks before writing. 2) /doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>, only when embed was chosen. 3) /doctor:mcp install, from the Skilled checkout, to build and register Code Mode. 4) /doctor:git setup, from inside the target repo. 5) /doctor:setup, from inside the target repo, to confirm the result. Pass only values the operator gave.\"\n+    - \"Checklist: Print these ordered writing steps through the presentation contract and stop; never run them. For each command, copy its mutation class verbatim from _routes.yaml and print one line explaining why: 1) /doctor:symlink link --root <dir> --runtimes <list> --mode <shape>, with --link-instructions only when link was chosen; it shows a plan and asks before writing. 2) /doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>, only when embed was chosen. 3) /doctor:mcp install, from the Skilled checkout, to build and register Code Mode. 4) /doctor:git setup, from inside the target repo. 5) /doctor:skill-advisor embedder, from inside the target repo, to set up meaning matching for commands. It shows its cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server, and a no leaves a phrase-only install. 6) /doctor:setup, from inside the target repo, to confirm the result. Pass only values the operator gave.\"\n     - \"Warn: Print this fixed caveat: Context saves land in the target repo's own specs/ when they run from inside it. Run /doctor:setup and later saves from inside the target repo, not from the Skilled checkout.\"\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml\nindex b409cb4761..f2d47538c5 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml\n@@ -39,4 +39,5 @@ upstream_assets:\n   command_catalog: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/command-catalog-mirror-check.cjs\"\n   codex_hooks_installer: \".skilled/bin/install-codex-hooks.mjs\"\n+  codex_hook_approval: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs\"\n   pi_agents: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/pi/sync-agents-pi.cjs\"\n   pi_prompts: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/pi/sync-prompts-pi.cjs\"\n@@ -147,4 +148,5 @@ execution:\n     - \"Run upstream_assets.command_catalog. Compare command frontmatter with the root and family indexes and hub metadata. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift, 2 = checker error.\"\n     - \"Run upstream_assets.codex_hooks_installer with --check --allow-worktree. Covers the user-global ~/.codex/hooks.json against the repo's .codex/hooks.json, including orphaned entries whose .skilled adapter no longer exists on disk. Explicit OK output = in sync; a drift report = drift; refusal, error, or missing affirmative output = error.\"\n+    - 'Run upstream_assets.codex_hook_approval with --root \"$PWD\". Covers the Codex approval that lets the project advisor hook run at all, since Codex skips an unapproved entry without a warning. PASS = in sync. WARN sets STATUS to WARN and shows the repair line it prints without counting as drift. SKIP leaves STATUS unchanged. Exit 0 = approved or no Codex hooks file, 1 = absent or unapproved, 2 = checker error.'\n     - \"Run upstream_assets.pi_agents with --check. Covers the generated .pi/agents/*.md. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n     - \"Run upstream_assets.pi_prompts with --check. Covers the generated .pi/prompts/*.md stubs. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n@@ -159,5 +161,8 @@ execution:\n # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n output: |\n-  STATUS=OK when every checker reports in sync, or n/a for a DSH row while its runtime tree is absent.\n+  STATUS=OK when every checker reports in sync, or n/a for a DSH row while its runtime tree is absent, and the\n+  Codex hook approval check reports in sync or skip.\n+  STATUS=WARN when the Codex hook approval check reports an unapproved or absent advisor entry and no checker\n+  reports drift: show its lines, including the repair line it prints, without adding a drift surface.\n   STATUS=DRIFT when any checker reports drift, listing each drifting surface and the repair command for it:\n     runtime mirrors  -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs\ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt\nindex 4072736def..257b64487b 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt\n@@ -17,5 +17,5 @@ Render this table first, before any leg runs.\n | Command | What it checks |\n |---------|----------------|\n-| `/doctor:setup` | This overview: the doctor target list and the five read-only setup legs |\n+| `/doctor:setup` | This overview: the doctor target list and the seven read-only setup legs |\n | `/doctor:helper [<problem in plain words>] [--json]` | Rank the doctor commands that fit a described problem, with the class and the reason on every line |\n | `/doctor:env list` | The documented environment switches and where each value comes from |\n@@ -38,4 +38,5 @@ Render this table first, before any leg runs.\n | `/doctor:skill-advisor skill-graph-freshness` | Drift between the compiled, SQLite and on-disk skill graph |\n | `/doctor:skill-advisor router-reach` | Whether each declared routing phrase reaches its hub |\n+| `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` | Meaning matching for commands: whether the local embedder answers, what it costs, and the plan that pulls the model and starts the server after a yes |\n | `/doctor:deep-loop` | Deep-loop coverage graphs and convergence for research, review and council runs |\n | `/doctor:mcp` | Code Mode install and debug, its UTCP configuration and runtime registration |\n@@ -59,4 +60,6 @@ Render one row per leg, in the workflow's order.\n | runtime-mirrors | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` |\n | advisor | Stale build: `npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build`. Other FAIL or DEGRADED results: `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`. |\n+| embedder | `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` |\n+| delivery | Missing hook: /doctor:runtime-mirrors, or /doctor:symlink check in a linked project. Unapproved Codex hook: the repair line the check prints, which opens /hooks in a Codex session |\n \n ## 4. Result Templates\n@@ -103,4 +106,5 @@ STATUS=ERROR ERROR=\"[message]\"\n | The sk-git leg reports DEGRADED | No sk-git check failed, but one is unknown or a gate is saved off. Run `/doctor:git setup` to see which. On a runtime the battery cannot name, the AI-tool check stays unknown |\n | The trigger-index leg reports stale documents | Run `/doctor:speckit` to see which documents are stale |\n+| The delivery leg reports DEGRADED | A runtime cannot receive the advisor brief. Run the repair the leg names, then rerun /doctor:setup. The install still works without it |\n | Route manifest parse error | Run `bash .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh` |\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml\nindex dfcce9c832..23d5e54930 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml\n@@ -3,6 +3,6 @@\n # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n role: Diagnostic Operator giving a first-run overview of every doctor command and running the existing read-only setup checks once\n-purpose: List every doctor target with what it checks, run five read-only legs, and name the runnable doctor command that repairs each failing leg\n-action: Print the doctor target list -> run the five read-only legs once -> render the per-leg verdict and repair lines through the presentation contract\n+purpose: List every doctor target with what it checks, run seven read-only legs, and name the runnable doctor command that repairs each failing leg\n+action: Print the doctor target list -> run the seven read-only legs once -> render the per-leg verdict and repair lines through the presentation contract\n skill_owner: \".skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/\"\n \n@@ -38,4 +38,6 @@ upstream_assets:\n   runtime_mirror_check: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs\"\n   hop_history: \".skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/bin/session-relaunch.cjs\"\n+  hook_wiring_check: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\"\n+  codex_approval_check: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs\"\n \n # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n@@ -55,5 +57,7 @@ execution:\n     - \"Leg trigger-index: run node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/generate-trigger-index.mjs --check --json. Exit 0 passes. Exit 1 (stale documents) or 2 and higher (unreadable index) fails, with repair /doctor:speckit.\"\n     - \"Leg runtime-mirrors: run node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check. Exit 0 passes. Any other exit fails, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors.\"\n-    - \"Leg advisor: run node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --format json --timeout-ms 500 --warm-only. Exit 0 with data.freshness set to live is PASS. Exit 0 with any other freshness is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor rebuild. Exit 75 with a staleDistWarning field in stderr JSON is FAIL, with repair npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build. Exit 75 without that field is SKIP because the daemon is not running. Any other exit is FAIL, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor rebuild.\"\n+    - \"Leg advisor: run node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --format json --timeout-ms 500 --warm-only. Exit 0 with data.freshness set to live is PASS. Exit 0 with any other freshness is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor rebuild. Exit 75 with a staleDistWarning field in stderr JSON is FAIL, with repair npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build. Exit 75 without that field is SKIP because the daemon is not running. Any other exit is FAIL, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor rebuild. When data.hookHealth is present, show hook p95 <rollingP95Ms> ms over <invocations> prompts and fail-open <rollingFailOpenRate as a percent> under the leg. It never changes the leg's status.\"\n+    - \"Leg embedder: run node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --include-semantic-health true --format json --timeout-ms 1500 --warm-only. Exit 75 is SKIP, as for the advisor leg, because the daemon is not running. Exit 0 with data.semanticLaneHealth.laneEnabled true and data.semanticLaneHealth.commandVectorCoverage.embedded above 0 is PASS. Any other result is DEGRADED, never FAIL, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor embedder.\"\n+    - \"Leg delivery: run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\" and node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\", and show each line they print under the leg. Both exit 0 is PASS. A hook-missing line is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors in a Skilled checkout or /doctor:symlink check in a linked project. WARN codex-hooks-unapproved is DEGRADED, with the repair line the check printed. WARN codex-advisor-hook-absent is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors. Exit 2 from either check is ERROR. This leg is never FAIL, because a hook that is not wired or not approved stops the brief, not the install.\"\n     - \"Last session hop (informational, not a leg): run node .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/bin/session-relaunch.cjs history --last 1 and show its first output line under the result as the last session hop, plus its open notes line when it prints one. Its exit and output never change the status.\"\n     - \"Claude context window (informational, not a leg): run node .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/bin/session-relaunch.cjs window and show its line. Its exit and output never change the status.\"\ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown b/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown\nindex 0015c63c13..a64b7e6748 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown\n@@ -40,4 +40,5 @@ The scripts validate route manifests, inspect MCP installations, audit parent sk\n +-- ci-scaffold.cjs\n +-- ci-toggle.cjs\n++-- codex-hook-approval-check.cjs\n +-- doctor-helper-match.cjs\n +-- doctor-phrase-reach.cjs\n@@ -45,4 +46,5 @@ The scripts validate route manifests, inspect MCP installations, audit parent sk\n +-- git-setup-check.cjs\n +-- git-standards.cjs\n++-- hook-wiring-check.cjs\n +-- mcp-doctor-lib.sh\n +-- mcp-doctor.sh\n@@ -107,4 +109,6 @@ The scripts validate route manifests, inspect MCP installations, audit parent sk\n | `doctor-helper-match.cjs` | Ranks the doctor commands of `_routes.yaml` against a problem stated in plain words for `/doctor:helper`: one entry per route, standalone command, standalone action and mcp sub-action, scored by inverse-document-frequency overlap over the manifest phrases plus a bonus for a fully covered phrase, with a preference for the mutation class the operator asked for. Each candidate carries the manifest phrase that best matched and the terms it matched, so the reason on every line is evidence. It skips its own route and every private name, reads one YAML file and writes nothing. It exits 0 on a match, 1 on no candidate above the floor and 2 on a bad argument, an unreadable manifest or a missing YAML parser. |\n | `doctor-phrase-reach.cjs` | Scores every activated doctor phrase and each runnable doctor command through the built advisor scorer, then keeps the three results the hooks show. It fails when a phrase reaches neither the top pick nor the second line. It also fails if a runnable command does not rank first or an activated phrase has fewer than three words. It exits 2 when the advisor build is missing or stale. |\n+| `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` | The read-only Codex approval check: it finds the advisor's `UserPromptSubmit` entry in `.codex/hooks.json` and reports whether the Codex config holds a `trusted_hash` for that exact group and index, because Codex skips an unapproved entry without a warning. `--root <dir>` reads another checkout, `--config <path>` reads another config and `--json` prints one object. It prints `SKIP no-codex-hooks`, `PASS codex-hooks-approved`, `WARN codex-advisor-hook-absent` or `WARN codex-hooks-unapproved <root>` with the `/hooks` repair line, and never prints a hash. It exits 0 on a skip or an approval, 1 on a missing or unapproved entry and 2 on a bad argument. |\n+| `hook-wiring-check.cjs` | The read-only hook-wiring check: it reads `.claude/settings.json`, `.codex/hooks.json`, `.cursor/hooks.json` and `.devin/hooks.v1.json`, and reports whether the prompt hook entry is present for each runtime folder it finds. `--root <dir>` is required and `--json` prints one object. It prints `ok <runtime>` or `hook-missing <runtime> <file>`, skips a runtime whose folder is absent and never writes. It exits 0 when every installed runtime is wired, 1 when one is missing and 2 on a bad argument or a missing root. |\n | `opencode-version-battery.cjs` | Checks this repository's OpenCode plugins on OpenCode 1 and 2. On 1 it proves plugin discovery through `debug config` and plugin load through an import check. On 2 it starts and stops a private server with the v2 binary it selected (`$OPENCODE_BIN`, `opencode` or `opencode2`, whichever reports a v2 version) and reads plugin and skill state from it. It exits 0 when every requested leg passes, 1 on a failed leg, 2 on a usage error, a crash or an `--out` file it cannot write and 3 when a leg is degraded or skipped. |\n | `ci-report.cjs` | The `/doctor:ci report` entry, kept thin: the flags, the exit codes and every name `/doctor:ci toggle` reads live here, and the readings live in the `ci-report` modules under `lib/`. It reads every workflow under `.github/workflows/` and reports its switch state, triggers, path filters and drift flags for `/doctor:ci report`. A switch is any variable a job's `if:` compares against `off`, so the workflow file is its only copy, and a repository variable value is reduced to a state and never printed. The branch, the required switch, the exempt files, the README and the rebuild trailer come from the CI profile, and the JSON names the profile it read. It exits 0 on a printed report, 1 when a workflow fails to parse, 2 on a bad argument and 3 when the CI profile is missing or invalid. |\n@@ -228,4 +232,6 @@ On this repository all legs pass on OpenCode 1.19.3 and 2.0.32. OpenCode 1.19.3\n | `agents-md-embed.cjs` | `plan` is read-only. `apply` writes only the paths in its own allowlist, all of them under the target root, after backing each one up under `.skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<digest>/` (or the OS temp folder when that path is not ignored), and restores from that backup itself when its post-write proof fails. `restore` writes only the paths the run's `manifest.json` records and keeps the backup folder. It never runs `git add`, `git commit` or `git stash`. |\n | `agents-md-manifest.cjs` | `--check` is read-only. `--write` rewrites the manifest's `derived` key and refuses to run outside the repository that ships the template. |\n+| `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` | Read-only over any root. It reads `.codex/hooks.json` and the Codex config, prints no hash and takes no write path. It exits 0 on a skip or an approval, 1 on a missing or unapproved entry and 2 on a bad argument. |\n+| `hook-wiring-check.cjs` | Read-only over any root. It writes no file and runs no installer, and its JSON form reports the same readings as its lines. It exits 0 when every installed runtime carries its entry, 1 when one is missing and 2 on a bad argument or a missing root. |\n | `opencode-version-battery.cjs` | The battery itself writes only the `--out` file and temporary folders it removes when each step ends. The private server's folder is also removed on `SIGINT` and `SIGTERM`, and the server is stopped. The import check runs each plugin's v1 factory in a child process rooted at the repository, so anything a plugin does when it loads happens during the check. It never touches the shared v2 service and never prints the private server's password. OpenCode 1 writes into a temporary data folder, not the user's. |\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md b/.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md\nindex 83784647f5..17b68fd61e 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md\n@@ -60,5 +60,6 @@ The argument failure wording, the doctor target list, the per-leg result table,\n \n The workflow prints the doctor target list.\n-It then runs five read-only legs once: the sk-code setup battery, the sk-git setup battery, the trigger index freshness check, the runtime mirror check and the advisor status probe with `--warm-only`.\n+It then runs seven read-only legs once: the sk-code setup battery, the sk-git setup battery, the trigger index freshness check, the runtime mirror check, the advisor status probe with `--warm-only` and the embedder check, which reads the semantic lane and the command vectors, and the delivery check, which reads whether each runtime's prompt hook is wired and whether Codex has approved it.\n+The delivery leg reports DEGRADED, never FAIL, when a prompt hook is missing or the Codex hook is unapproved, and names the repair.\n It reports each leg as passing, skipped, degraded or failing.\n For a failing leg, it names the runnable doctor command that repairs it.\ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/skill-advisor.md b/.skilled/commands/doctor/skill-advisor.md\nindex 86bd89e0d3..a3d73cf751 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/skill-advisor.md\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/skill-advisor.md\n@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@\n ---\n description: \"Tune and rebuild the skill advisor, and audit graph freshness, router reach, budgets and parent hubs.\"\n-argument-hint: \"<tune|rebuild|skill-graph-freshness|router-reach|skill-budget|parent-skill> [flags] | list | ?\"\n+argument-hint: \"<tune|rebuild|skill-graph-freshness|router-reach|embedder|skill-budget|parent-skill> [flags] | list | ?\"\n allowed-tools: Read, Bash, Grep, Glob, Edit, Write\n ---\n@@ -59,4 +59,5 @@ These existing YAML assets are referenced only. The router must not modify them.\n | `skill-graph-freshness` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-graph-freshness.yaml` |\n | `router-reach` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-router-reach.yaml` |\n+| `embedder` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml` |\n | `skill-budget` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-budget.yaml` |\n | `parent-skill` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-parent-skill.yaml` |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff -U2 35c3188681..320e7b64d4 -- .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt .skilled/commands/doctor/agents-md.md .skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md .skilled/commands/doctor/skill-advisor.md .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown | head -220\"}"},"time":{"start":1794550774121,"end":1794550775118}}}}
