{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794550927255,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799ae9ffehgaY2UX9uAVWD2","part":{"id":"prt_1d3920f97001LvTznLwZy8diqe","sessionID":"ses_e2c799ae9ffehgaY2UX9uAVWD2","messageID":"msg_1d392053f001hJOHSeoxD8EA2C","type":"step-start","snapshot":"5151b5946c19464ea2160a7c6e2f1d092715ba3a"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794550950489,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799ae9ffehgaY2UX9uAVWD2","part":{"partID":"prt_1d3923a62002XF4D8orN478Mw9","sessionID":"ses_e2c799ae9ffehgaY2UX9uAVWD2","messageID":"msg_1d392053f001hJOHSeoxD8EA2C","type":"tool","id":"call_00_8HifPUgc2Yrge9xRiSS13707","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 4 — security\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review; target agent `@deep-review`; detached fan-out lineage `doctor-install`.\n- Session: `fanout-doctor-install-1794550137809-1ecgc7`, generation 1.\n- Dimension: security. Budget profile: verify.\n- Operator review focus: this iteration covered holdout hygiene (counts only; no holdout prompt text was read or printed) and the write containment of the one mutating engine in this lineage. The mutating-offer safety was revisited at the filesystem boundary.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:88-98, 642-841, 888-918, 1284-1305, 1429-1524`\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:632-735` (symlink handling in A10)\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml:54-69` (hook wiring in a linked project)\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml:25-41` (mutation boundaries)\n- Count-only evidence: `routing-accuracy/holdout-prompts.jsonl` (66 lines), `routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl` (176 lines; 87 none, 45 tune, 44 holdout)\n- Consumer-name evidence: `routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:578-589`, `measure-brief-cost.mjs:105-119`, `score-command-transcripts.mjs:944-960,1157`, `command-offer.mjs:325-349`, `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:446-494`\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\n1. **A symlinked `REPO RULES.md` or `.cursor/rules/repo-local.md` is written through, so apply mutates a file its plan never named** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:783` -- `compose` refuses a symlinked root document (`:652-654`) and skips symlinked folded copies (`:733`), but the router and Cursor mirror branches read and replace without a symlink check (`:783-823`). `assertWritable` (`:888-906`) resolves links and rejects only a target outside the root, so a link pointing at another file **inside** the repository passes; `fs.writeFileSync` in the apply loop (`:1372`) then writes to the link target instead of the allowlisted path.\n   - Case: a repository with `REPO RULES.md -> AGENTS.md` (a shape the `link` install mode itself produces) runs `/doctor:agents-md embed`; the plan prints `target REPO RULES.md: replace`, and apply overwrites `AGENTS.md` with router rows, then the proof reads the real `AGENTS.md` it just clobbered.\n   - Finding class: class-of-bug\n   - Scope proof: the only `isSymlink` guards in the engine are at `:652` (root file), `:733` (folded copies) and `:846,1070` (pointer); `rg -n \"isSymlink\" agents-md-embed.cjs` shows no guard on `routerPath` or `mirrorPath`; `assertWritable` line `:902` compares the resolved target to the real root, not to the allowlisted path.\n   - Affected surface hints: [\"compose router branch\", \"compose cursor mirror branch\", \"assertWritable\", \"commandApply write loop\"]\n   - Claim adjudication:\n     ```json\n     {\"type\":\"security\",\"claim\":\"A symlink at an allowlisted path that points inside the repository is written through, so the run mutates a file outside the bytes the plan printed.\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:783\",\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:809\",\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:902\",\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:1372\"],\"counterevidenceSought\":\"read every isSymlink guard and the real-path branch of assertWritable; checked whether backup/restore would detect a different target\",\"alternativeExplanation\":\"the symlink-engine link mode is expected to link instruction files, and a linked repo may be rejected earlier by A1/E1 state rather than reaching compose\",\"finalSeverity\":\"P1\",\"confidence\":0.75,\"downgradeTrigger\":\"downgrade to P2 if the router and mirror are documented as never symlinked and the embed route refuses a repository that links them\"}\n     ```\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n2. **Automatic rollback restores the backup without the allowlist and hash checks the manual restore enforces** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:1288` -- `restoreFromBackup` iterates `record.paths` with `path.join(root, entry.path)` (`:1289`) and `fs.copyFileSync` (`:1299`), while `commandRestore` calls `assertWritable` (`:1453`) and verifies every backup against `entry.sha256` (`:1464`). A backup that is corrupt or a record whose path was edited is copied back without either check, so the automatic rollback can write outside the allowlist or restore bytes that are not the pre-run ones.\n   - Case: a partial write leaves a truncated backup file for `AGENTS.md`; the post-write proof fails and `restoreFromBackup` copies the truncated file back, reporting only `restored: N file(s)` while the tree is now neither the old nor the new state.\n   - Finding class: instance-only\n   - Scope proof: `rg -n \"assertWritable|sha256\" agents-md-embed.cjs` shows both only in `commandRestore`/`assertWritable`; the `restoreFromBackup` body `:1284-1305` contains neither.\n   - Affected surface hints: [\"restoreFromBackup\", \"commandApply rollback\", \"commandRestore\"]\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Notes |\n|----------|-------|--------|-------|\n| spec_code | core | partial | The embed YAML's mutation-boundary claims were checked against the code; packet `spec.md` still not read at this level. |\n| checklist_evidence | core | notApplicable | Phased parent has no root `checklist.md`. |\n| skill_agent | overlay | notApplicable | No skill or agent definition in scope. |\n| agent_cross_runtime | overlay | pass | A linked project's `.claude`/`.codex`/`.cursor`/`.devin` hook files are symlinks into the checkout, which is why `hook-wiring-check` reads the checkout's entry; recorded as context for the symlink finding. |\n| feature_catalog_code | overlay | partial | Feature catalog entry not read. |\n| playbook_capability | overlay | notApplicable | No playbook file in scope. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\nHoldout consumers named: `run-command-behaviour.mjs` refuses a holdout row before its prompt is read (`:584-589`), `measure-brief-cost.mjs` refuses a holdout id (`:119`), `score-command-transcripts.mjs` marks a holdout row unscored (`:1157`), `command-offer.mjs` refuses an unknown or holdout row (`:325-349`), and `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` tallies holdout rows into aggregate baseline counts only (`:446-494`). No doctor-install file reads a holdout file: `rg -l \"holdout\" .skilled/commands/doctor` returned no path. The counts are 44 holdout rows inside `command-prompts.jsonl` and 66 rows in `holdout-prompts.jsonl`; no prompt text was opened.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Holdout files are in the `accuracy-runner` area, not this lineage's area. They were inspected by file name, line count and split-value count only, as the review focus requires; no content was read.\n- `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` reads holdout rows to compute aggregate tallies. That is an evaluation baseline rather than a tune path, and it writes no prompt text; recorded as an observation, not a finding, because the file is outside this lineage's area.\n- The symlink finding depends on a repository state the engine's own `link` install mode can create. If the install flow always links `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md`/`REPO RULES.md` together, the router symlink is expected, not exotic.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- `assertWritable` (`agents-md-embed.cjs:888-906`) checks containment before allowlist membership and resolves the nearest existing ancestor, so a `..` segment or an outward link is refused.\n- The engine never prints the Codex `trusted_hash`: `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs:15-16,196-204` reports only status, group, index and config path.\n- `hook-wiring-check.cjs` and `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` take no write path and emit no secret; both were run read-only in iteration 2.\n- Backups go to a git-ignored path or the OS temp directory (`agents-md-embed.cjs:953-968`), so a backup is not published by the next commit.\n- The manual restore refuses a record that names another root (`agents-md-embed.cjs:1445-1448`).\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **Holdout prompts leak through a doctor path** — ruled out: no file under `.skilled/commands/doctor` matches `holdout`, and the doctor commands never read the routing-accuracy corpora.\n- **Holdout text is printed by a scoring error message** — ruled out at the code level: refusal messages carry the row id and reason only (`run-command-behaviour.mjs:589`), not the prompt.\n- **The backup directory can be chosen by the caller** — ruled out: `backupBase` derives it from the root and `planFor` refuses an existing directory.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: maintainability\n- Focus area: the two engines' structure and the docs that describe them, with the P1/P2 findings checked for whether a smaller change removes the class\n- Reason: four iterations covered behavior, traceability and security; the remaining dimension is the cost of the next safe change\n- Rotation status: first maintainability pass\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: the symlink write-through finding is the one that must survive to synthesis\n- Required evidence: direct read only, no new discovery beyond the recorded sites\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install/iterations/iteration-004.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install/iterations/iteration-004.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install/iterations/iteration-004.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Review Iteration 4 — security\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review; target agent `@deep-review`; detached fan-out lineage `doctor-install`.\\n- Session: `fanout-doctor-install-1794550137809-1ecgc7`, generation 1.\\n- Dimension: security. Budget profile: verify.\\n- Operator review focus: this iteration covered holdout hygiene (counts only; no holdout prompt text was read or printed) and the write containment of the one mutating engine in this lineage. The mutating-offer safety was revisited at the filesystem boundary.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:88-98, 642-841, 888-918, 1284-1305, 1429-1524`\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:632-735` (symlink handling in A10)\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml:54-69` (hook wiring in a linked project)\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml:25-41` (mutation boundaries)\\n- Count-only evidence: `routing-accuracy/holdout-prompts.jsonl` (66 lines), `routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl` (176 lines; 87 none, 45 tune, 44 holdout)\\n- Consumer-name evidence: `routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:578-589`, `measure-brief-cost.mjs:105-119`, `score-command-transcripts.mjs:944-960,1157`, `command-offer.mjs:325-349`, `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:446-494`\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\n1. **A symlinked `REPO RULES.md` or `.cursor/rules/repo-local.md` is written through, so apply mutates a file its plan never named** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:783` -- `compose` refuses a symlinked root document (`:652-654`) and skips symlinked folded copies (`:733`), but the router and Cursor mirror branches read and replace without a symlink check (`:783-823`). `assertWritable` (`:888-906`) resolves links and rejects only a target outside the root, so a link pointing at another file **inside** the repository passes; `fs.writeFileSync` in the apply loop (`:1372`) then writes to the link target instead of the allowlisted path.\\n   - Case: a repository with `REPO RULES.md -> AGENTS.md` (a shape the `link` install mode itself produces) runs `/doctor:agents-md embed`; the plan prints `target REPO RULES.md: replace`, and apply overwrites `AGENTS.md` with router rows, then the proof reads the real `AGENTS.md` it just clobbered.\\n   - Finding class: class-of-bug\\n   - Scope proof: the only `isSymlink` guards in the engine are at `:652` (root file), `:733` (folded copies) and `:846,1070` (pointer); `rg -n \\\"isSymlink\\\" agents-md-embed.cjs` shows no guard on `routerPath` or `mirrorPath`; `assertWritable` line `:902` compares the resolved target to the real root, not to the allowlisted path.\\n   - Affected surface hints: [\\\"compose router branch\\\", \\\"compose cursor mirror branch\\\", \\\"assertWritable\\\", \\\"commandApply write loop\\\"]\\n   - Claim adjudication:\\n     ```json\\n     {\\\"type\\\":\\\"security\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"A symlink at an allowlisted path that points inside the repository is written through, so the run mutates a file outside the bytes the plan printed.\\\",\\\"evidenceRefs\\\":[\\\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:783\\\",\\\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:809\\\",\\\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:902\\\",\\\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:1372\\\"],\\\"counterevidenceSought\\\":\\\"read every isSymlink guard and the real-path branch of assertWritable; checked whether backup/restore would detect a different target\\\",\\\"alternativeExplanation\\\":\\\"the symlink-engine link mode is expected to link instruction files, and a linked repo may be rejected earlier by A1/E1 state rather than reaching compose\\\",\\\"finalSeverity\\\":\\\"P1\\\",\\\"confidence\\\":0.75,\\\"downgradeTrigger\\\":\\\"downgrade to P2 if the router and mirror are documented as never symlinked and the embed route refuses a repository that links them\\\"}\\n     ```\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n2. **Automatic rollback restores the backup without the allowlist and hash checks the manual restore enforces** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:1288` -- `restoreFromBackup` iterates `record.paths` with `path.join(root, entry.path)` (`:1289`) and `fs.copyFileSync` (`:1299`), while `commandRestore` calls `assertWritable` (`:1453`) and verifies every backup against `entry.sha256` (`:1464`). A backup that is corrupt or a record whose path was edited is copied back without either check, so the automatic rollback can write outside the allowlist or restore bytes that are not the pre-run ones.\\n   - Case: a partial write leaves a truncated backup file for `AGENTS.md`; the post-write proof fails and `restoreFromBackup` copies the truncated file back, reporting only `restored: N file(s)` while the tree is now neither the old nor the new state.\\n   - Finding class: instance-only\\n   - Scope proof: `rg -n \\\"assertWritable|sha256\\\" agents-md-embed.cjs` shows both only in `commandRestore`/`assertWritable`; the `restoreFromBackup` body `:1284-1305` contains neither.\\n   - Affected surface hints: [\\\"restoreFromBackup\\\", \\\"commandApply rollback\\\", \\\"commandRestore\\\"]\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Notes |\\n|----------|-------|--------|-------|\\n| spec_code | core | partial | The embed YAML's mutation-boundary claims were checked against the code; packet `spec.md` still not read at this level. |\\n| checklist_evidence | core | notApplicable | Phased parent has no root `checklist.md`. |\\n| skill_agent | overlay | notApplicable | No skill or agent definition in scope. |\\n| agent_cross_runtime | overlay | pass | A linked project's `.claude`/`.codex`/`.cursor`/`.devin` hook files are symlinks into the checkout, which is why `hook-wiring-check` reads the checkout's entry; recorded as context for the symlink finding. |\\n| feature_catalog_code | overlay | partial | Feature catalog entry not read. |\\n| playbook_capability | overlay | notApplicable | No playbook file in scope. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\nHoldout consumers named: `run-command-behaviour.mjs` refuses a holdout row before its prompt is read (`:584-589`), `measure-brief-cost.mjs` refuses a holdout id (`:119`), `score-command-transcripts.mjs` marks a holdout row unscored (`:1157`), `command-offer.mjs` refuses an unknown or holdout row (`:325-349`), and `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` tallies holdout rows into aggregate baseline counts only (`:446-494`). No doctor-install file reads a holdout file: `rg -l \\\"holdout\\\" .skilled/commands/doctor` returned no path. The counts are 44 holdout rows inside `command-prompts.jsonl` and 66 rows in `holdout-prompts.jsonl`; no prompt text was opened.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Holdout files are in the `accuracy-runner` area, not this lineage's area. They were inspected by file name, line count and split-value count only, as the review focus requires; no content was read.\\n- `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` reads holdout rows to compute aggregate tallies. That is an evaluation baseline rather than a tune path, and it writes no prompt text; recorded as an observation, not a finding, because the file is outside this lineage's area.\\n- The symlink finding depends on a repository state the engine's own `link` install mode can create. If the install flow always links `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md`/`REPO RULES.md` together, the router symlink is expected, not exotic.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- `assertWritable` (`agents-md-embed.cjs:888-906`) checks containment before allowlist membership and resolves the nearest existing ancestor, so a `..` segment or an outward link is refused.\\n- The engine never prints the Codex `trusted_hash`: `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs:15-16,196-204` reports only status, group, index and config path.\\n- `hook-wiring-check.cjs` and `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` take no write path and emit no secret; both were run read-only in iteration 2.\\n- Backups go to a git-ignored path or the OS temp directory (`agents-md-embed.cjs:953-968`), so a backup is not published by the next commit.\\n- The manual restore refuses a record that names another root (`agents-md-embed.cjs:1445-1448`).\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **Holdout prompts leak through a doctor path** — ruled out: no file under `.skilled/commands/doctor` matches `holdout`, and the doctor commands never read the routing-accuracy corpora.\\n- **Holdout text is printed by a scoring error message** — ruled out at the code level: refusal messages carry the row id and reason only (`run-command-behaviour.mjs:589`), not the prompt.\\n- **The backup directory can be chosen by the caller** — ruled out: `backupBase` derives it from the root and `planFor` refuses an existing directory.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: maintainability\\n- Focus area: the two engines' structure and the docs that describe them, with the P1/P2 findings checked for whether a smaller change removes the class\\n- Reason: four iterations covered behavior, traceability and security; the remaining dimension is the cost of the next safe change\\n- Rotation status: first maintainability pass\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: the symlink write-through finding is the one that must survive to synthesis\\n- Required evidence: direct read only, no new discovery beyond the recorded sites\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install/iterations/iteration-004.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794550938210,"end":1794550950489}}}}
