ch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -149,9 +149,9 @@\n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n-- Dimension: maintainability - Focus area: the two engines' structure and the docs that describe them, with the P1/P2 findings checked for whether a smaller change removes the class - Reason: four iterations covered behavior, traceability and security; the remaining dimension is the cost of the next safe change - Rotation status: first maintainability pass - Blocked/productive carry-forward: the symlink write-through finding is the one that must survive to synthesis - Required evidence: direct read only, no new discovery beyond the recorded sites Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\n+- Dimension: maintainability - Focus area: the sibling hook checks' argument and marker handling, and the duplicated router-table readers in the check and embed engines - Reason: the last dimension left is the cost of the next safe change; the two hook checks and the two router readers are places where a small edit silently diverges - Rotation status: first maintainability pass - Blocked/productive carry-forward: all prior findings stay open; no direction is exhausted - Required evidence: direct read of each sibling pair and a concrete divergent input\n \n <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n ## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n \n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\": \"- Dimension: maintainability - Focus area: the sibling hook checks' argument and marker handling, and the duplicated router-table readers in the check and embed engines - Reason: the last dimension left is the cost of the next safe change; the two hook checks and the two router readers are places where a small edit silently diverges - Rotation status: first maintainability pass - Blocked/productive carry-forward: all prior findings stay open; no direction is exhausted - Required evidence: direct read of each sibling pair and a concrete divergent input\", \"oldString\": \"- Dimension: maintainability - Focus area: the two engines' structure and the docs that describe them, with the P1/P2 findings checked for whether a smaller change removes the class - Reason: four iterations covered behavior, traceability and security; the remaining dimension is the cost of the next safe change - Rotation status: first maintainability pass - Blocked/productive carry-forward: the symlink write-through finding is the one that must survive to synthesis - Required evidence: direct read only, no new discovery beyond the recorded sites Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\", \"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794551013315,"end":1794551013368}}}}
