{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794551065005,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799ae9ffehgaY2UX9uAVWD2","part":{"id":"prt_1d39429ad0012q2awdV2QRpjam","sessionID":"ses_e2c799ae9ffehgaY2UX9uAVWD2","messageID":"msg_1d3941c23001Jgl2AYe0909vob","type":"step-start","snapshot":"b5c3e9626d9201017d34e2e5f60faaa5002fa6e6"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794551077365,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799ae9ffehgaY2UX9uAVWD2","part":{"partID":"prt_1d394331c002Oi4UkX1PDWzbeK","sessionID":"ses_e2c799ae9ffehgaY2UX9uAVWD2","messageID":"msg_1d3941c23001Jgl2AYe0909vob","type":"tool","id":"call_00_atveyFtEPffNSH2eBuCB6877","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 5 — maintainability\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review; target agent `@deep-review`; detached fan-out lineage `doctor-install`.\n- Session: `fanout-doctor-install-1794550137809-1ecgc7`, generation 1.\n- Dimension: maintainability. Budget profile: scan.\n- Operator review focus: this iteration covered the sibling-pair risk in the two new hook checks and the two router-table readers, which is the \"docs that disagree with code\" focus one level down — two implementations of one rule that can drift. No holdout file was opened.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs:48-67`\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:79-125`\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:789-833`\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:312-368`\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs`, `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/codex-hook-approval-check.test.cjs` (fixtures reviewed for the two sibling behaviors)\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone new. DR1-P1-001 (partial write) and DR4-P1-001 (symlink write-through) remain active.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **The two sibling hook checks disagree on a value flag whose next token starts with a dash** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs:59` -- `parseArgs` accepts any non-empty next token as the value of `--root`/`--config`, so `--root --json` binds `root = '--json'`; `hook-wiring-check.cjs:87` rejects a value starting with `-` and exits 2. The approval check then looks for `--json/.codex/hooks.json`, finds nothing, and exits 0 with `SKIP no-codex-hooks`, so a typo reads as a clean skip.\n   - Case: an operator runs `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs --root --json`; the check reports `SKIP no-codex-hooks` with exit 0, while the sibling check on the same typo refuses with exit 2 and the usage block.\n   - Finding class: instance-only\n   - Scope proof: `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs:59` tests only `undefined`/`''`; `hook-wiring-check.cjs:87` is the only sibling that tests `startsWith('-')`.\n   - Affected surface hints: [\"codex approval argument parsing\", \"hook wiring argument parsing\"]\n2. **Hook wiring counts a marker anywhere in the event payload, so a mention is read as a wired entry** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:123` -- `wired` is `JSON.stringify(payload).includes(runtime.marker)`. The marker can sit in a comment, a description, a disabled entry or a command that only echoes it, and the runtime reports `ok`.\n   - Case: `.claude/settings.json` carries a `UserPromptSubmit` entry whose command is `echo hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js` (or a `description` that names the file) and no entry that runs the hook; the check prints `ok claude`.\n   - Finding class: instance-only\n   - Scope proof: the only structural test is `includes` at `:123`; the function never inspects `hook.type`, `hook.command` or the entry shape the other fixtures use.\n   - Affected surface hints: [\"hook wiring inspect\", \"A10-adjacent delivery leg\"]\n3. **The check and the embed engines read the same router table by different rules, so a malformed row is \"missing\" to one and \"present\" to the other** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:809` -- `parseTableRows` fixes the width at the header and drops a row whose cell count differs (`:809`), while `routerTable` in the embed engine pushes every pipe row without a width check (`agents-md-embed.cjs:361`). A row with an extra `|` inside a summary is therefore reported missing by `/doctor:agents-md check` and treated as present by `/doctor:agents-md embed`, which adds no row.\n   - Case: a consumer's `REPO RULES.md` trigger row summary contains a literal `|`; `check` reports A11 `missing trigger row for …` and `embed` prints `NOTHING TO DO` for the router, so the operator has a finding with no repair.\n   - Finding class: cross-consumer\n   - Scope proof: the two readers are the only implementations of this table grammar (`rg -n \"TRIGGER TABLE|INDEX\" agents-md-check.cjs agents-md-embed.cjs`), and their row-acceptance conditions differ at `agents-md-check.cjs:809` versus `agents-md-embed.cjs:361`.\n   - Affected surface hints: [\"A11 router row\", \"embed addRouterRows\", \"shared router-table grammar\"]\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Notes |\n|----------|-------|--------|-------|\n| spec_code | core | partial | The sibling behaviors were compared to the docs that promise them; packet `spec.md` remains unread at this level. |\n| checklist_evidence | core | notApplicable | Phased parent has no root `checklist.md`. |\n| skill_agent | overlay | notApplicable | No skill or agent definition in scope. |\n| agent_cross_runtime | overlay | pass | The two hook checks are the cross-runtime surface; both were executed read-only in iteration 2 and behave as documented on this checkout. |\n| feature_catalog_code | overlay | partial | Feature catalog entry not read. |\n| playbook_capability | overlay | notApplicable | No playbook file in scope. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\nSibling surfaces named: `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` and `hook-wiring-check.cjs` are run together by `doctor-setup.yaml:61` (delivery leg) and by `doctor-symlink-check.yaml:60` (hook check), so a divergence between them surfaces in two doctor routes. `agents-md-check.cjs` A11 and `agents-md-embed.cjs` router replacement are the read and write halves of one router contract, called by `/doctor:agents-md check` and `/doctor:agents-md embed` respectively.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- A malformed table row is not a shape the presentation contract documents; the finding is scoped to the two readers disagreeing, not to the router format itself.\n- The approval check's `--root --json` behavior is reachable only by a mistyped invocation. It is reported as maintainability because no correct invocation reaches it.\n- The hook marker could be matched structurally by walking `hooks[].command`, but that is a recommendation, not a new requirement; the docs already say the entry is what matters.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- `hook-wiring-check.cjs:105-112` handles both nested and top-level event shapes, and tested against this checkout it reports `ok` for all four installed runtimes.\n- `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs:131-139` bounds the approval block at the next TOML header, so a `trusted_hash` under another key does not count.\n- `agents-md-embed.cjs:377-406` (`addRouterRows`) inserts only missing rows and reports the count per table, matching its doc comment.\n- `agents-md-check.cjs:825-833` (`missingRows`) compares the resolved rule path, so a reworded summary is not reported as missing.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **The two hook checks duplicate a whole implementation** — ruled out: they share only the marker constant's text; one checks presence, the other approval state, and their outputs do not overlap.\n- **`parseTableRows` and `routerTable` can both be replaced by one helper without behavior change** — not claimed: the embed reader needs line positions for insertion while the check reader does not, so a shared helper must return positions as well as cells. Recorded as a recommendation, not a finding.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- None: this is the final iteration under `maxIterations: 5`. Synthesis follows.\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install/iterations/iteration-005.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install/iterations/iteration-005.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install/iterations/iteration-005.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Review Iteration 5 — maintainability\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review; target agent `@deep-review`; detached fan-out lineage `doctor-install`.\\n- Session: `fanout-doctor-install-1794550137809-1ecgc7`, generation 1.\\n- Dimension: maintainability. Budget profile: scan.\\n- Operator review focus: this iteration covered the sibling-pair risk in the two new hook checks and the two router-table readers, which is the \\\"docs that disagree with code\\\" focus one level down — two implementations of one rule that can drift. No holdout file was opened.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs:48-67`\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:79-125`\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:789-833`\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:312-368`\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs`, `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/codex-hook-approval-check.test.cjs` (fixtures reviewed for the two sibling behaviors)\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone new. DR1-P1-001 (partial write) and DR4-P1-001 (symlink write-through) remain active.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **The two sibling hook checks disagree on a value flag whose next token starts with a dash** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs:59` -- `parseArgs` accepts any non-empty next token as the value of `--root`/`--config`, so `--root --json` binds `root = '--json'`; `hook-wiring-check.cjs:87` rejects a value starting with `-` and exits 2. The approval check then looks for `--json/.codex/hooks.json`, finds nothing, and exits 0 with `SKIP no-codex-hooks`, so a typo reads as a clean skip.\\n   - Case: an operator runs `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs --root --json`; the check reports `SKIP no-codex-hooks` with exit 0, while the sibling check on the same typo refuses with exit 2 and the usage block.\\n   - Finding class: instance-only\\n   - Scope proof: `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs:59` tests only `undefined`/`''`; `hook-wiring-check.cjs:87` is the only sibling that tests `startsWith('-')`.\\n   - Affected surface hints: [\\\"codex approval argument parsing\\\", \\\"hook wiring argument parsing\\\"]\\n2. **Hook wiring counts a marker anywhere in the event payload, so a mention is read as a wired entry** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:123` -- `wired` is `JSON.stringify(payload).includes(runtime.marker)`. The marker can sit in a comment, a description, a disabled entry or a command that only echoes it, and the runtime reports `ok`.\\n   - Case: `.claude/settings.json` carries a `UserPromptSubmit` entry whose command is `echo hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js` (or a `description` that names the file) and no entry that runs the hook; the check prints `ok claude`.\\n   - Finding class: instance-only\\n   - Scope proof: the only structural test is `includes` at `:123`; the function never inspects `hook.type`, `hook.command` or the entry shape the other fixtures use.\\n   - Affected surface hints: [\\\"hook wiring inspect\\\", \\\"A10-adjacent delivery leg\\\"]\\n3. **The check and the embed engines read the same router table by different rules, so a malformed row is \\\"missing\\\" to one and \\\"present\\\" to the other** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:809` -- `parseTableRows` fixes the width at the header and drops a row whose cell count differs (`:809`), while `routerTable` in the embed engine pushes every pipe row without a width check (`agents-md-embed.cjs:361`). A row with an extra `|` inside a summary is therefore reported missing by `/doctor:agents-md check` and treated as present by `/doctor:agents-md embed`, which adds no row.\\n   - Case: a consumer's `REPO RULES.md` trigger row summary contains a literal `|`; `check` reports A11 `missing trigger row for …` and `embed` prints `NOTHING TO DO` for the router, so the operator has a finding with no repair.\\n   - Finding class: cross-consumer\\n   - Scope proof: the two readers are the only implementations of this table grammar (`rg -n \\\"TRIGGER TABLE|INDEX\\\" agents-md-check.cjs agents-md-embed.cjs`), and their row-acceptance conditions differ at `agents-md-check.cjs:809` versus `agents-md-embed.cjs:361`.\\n   - Affected surface hints: [\\\"A11 router row\\\", \\\"embed addRouterRows\\\", \\\"shared router-table grammar\\\"]\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Notes |\\n|----------|-------|--------|-------|\\n| spec_code | core | partial | The sibling behaviors were compared to the docs that promise them; packet `spec.md` remains unread at this level. |\\n| checklist_evidence | core | notApplicable | Phased parent has no root `checklist.md`. |\\n| skill_agent | overlay | notApplicable | No skill or agent definition in scope. |\\n| agent_cross_runtime | overlay | pass | The two hook checks are the cross-runtime surface; both were executed read-only in iteration 2 and behave as documented on this checkout. |\\n| feature_catalog_code | overlay | partial | Feature catalog entry not read. |\\n| playbook_capability | overlay | notApplicable | No playbook file in scope. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\nSibling surfaces named: `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` and `hook-wiring-check.cjs` are run together by `doctor-setup.yaml:61` (delivery leg) and by `doctor-symlink-check.yaml:60` (hook check), so a divergence between them surfaces in two doctor routes. `agents-md-check.cjs` A11 and `agents-md-embed.cjs` router replacement are the read and write halves of one router contract, called by `/doctor:agents-md check` and `/doctor:agents-md embed` respectively.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- A malformed table row is not a shape the presentation contract documents; the finding is scoped to the two readers disagreeing, not to the router format itself.\\n- The approval check's `--root --json` behavior is reachable only by a mistyped invocation. It is reported as maintainability because no correct invocation reaches it.\\n- The hook marker could be matched structurally by walking `hooks[].command`, but that is a recommendation, not a new requirement; the docs already say the entry is what matters.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- `hook-wiring-check.cjs:105-112` handles both nested and top-level event shapes, and tested against this checkout it reports `ok` for all four installed runtimes.\\n- `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs:131-139` bounds the approval block at the next TOML header, so a `trusted_hash` under another key does not count.\\n- `agents-md-embed.cjs:377-406` (`addRouterRows`) inserts only missing rows and reports the count per table, matching its doc comment.\\n- `agents-md-check.cjs:825-833` (`missingRows`) compares the resolved rule path, so a reworded summary is not reported as missing.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **The two hook checks duplicate a whole implementation** — ruled out: they share only the marker constant's text; one checks presence, the other approval state, and their outputs do not overlap.\\n- **`parseTableRows` and `routerTable` can both be replaced by one helper without behavior change** — not claimed: the embed reader needs line positions for insertion while the check reader does not, so a shared helper must return positions as well as cells. Recorded as a recommendation, not a finding.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- None: this is the final iteration under `maxIterations: 5`. Synthesis follows.\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install/iterations/iteration-005.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794551067420,"end":1794551077365}}}}
